var SET1 = [
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）クラウドが提供する最大の価値として、初期の大型設備投資を不要にする費用構造はどれか。","o":["使用量に関わらず毎月定額を支払う固定料金制","物理サーバーを自社で購入し償却する方式","固定費を変動費へ変換する従量課金モデル","利用開始前に容量を全額前払いする契約"],"a":2,"e":"データセンターの先行投資が不要。利用した分だけ支払う仕組み。毎月定額の固定料金制や容量の全額前払いは、使わない分も支払うため先行投資を不要にする仕組みではない。物理サーバーの購入と償却は従来型のオンプレミスの方式。","qEn":"Which cost structure is the greatest value that the AWS (Amazon Web Services) cloud offers by eliminating large upfront capital investment?","oEn":["A fixed-rate plan with the same monthly payment regardless of usage","Buying physical servers and depreciating them in-house","A pay-as-you-go model that converts fixed costs into variable costs","A contract requiring full prepayment of capacity before use"],"eEn":"No upfront data center investment is needed; you pay only for what you use. A fixed monthly plan or full prepayment of capacity means paying for unused resources, so neither eliminates upfront investment. Buying and depreciating physical servers is the traditional on-premises approach."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"CapEx（資本的支出）からOpEx（運用的支出）への移行が意味する変化はどれか。","o":["自社設備への資本的支出から運用的支出への転換","運用的支出から資本的支出への逆方向の転換","減価償却対象の固定資産を新たに取得する変化","初期投資を増やし長期保有資産を積み増す変化"],"a":0,"e":"サーバー購入などの初期投資が不要。月々の利用量に応じた経費化。運用的支出から資本的支出への逆方向の転換や、減価償却する固定資産の取得、長期保有資産の積み増しは、設備を購入する従来のオンプレミスの方式で、クラウド移行の方向ではない。","qEn":"Which change does the shift from CapEx (capital expenditure) to OpEx (operating expenditure) represent?","oEn":["A shift from capital spending on equipment to operating spending","A reverse shift from operating spending to capital spending","A change that newly acquires fixed assets subject to depreciation","A change that increases upfront investment and builds up long-held assets"],"eEn":"No upfront investment such as buying servers is needed; costs are expensed according to monthly usage. A reverse shift from operating to capital spending, acquiring depreciable fixed assets, and building up long-held assets are all traditional on-premises approaches that involve buying equipment, not the direction of cloud migration."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"多数の利用者がインフラを共有することでAWS（Amazon Web Services）が実現するコスト優位性はどれか。","o":["規模の経済による単価の継続的な低下","共有をやめ個別課金へ移行する仕組み","利用者増加に伴う従量単価の段階的な引き上げ","契約者ごとに専用設備を割り当てる方式"],"a":0,"e":"利用者全体の需要集約で調達コストが低下。値下げという形で利用者へ還元。利用者が増えて従量単価が上がるのではなく、規模の経済で下がる。契約者ごとに専用設備を割り当てる方式は共有の利点を失い、コストが上がる。","qEn":"Which cost advantage does AWS (Amazon Web Services) achieve through many customers sharing its infrastructure?","oEn":["A continuous decrease in unit prices through economies of scale","A mechanism that moves away from sharing to individual billing","A stepwise increase in pay-as-you-go unit prices as users grow","An approach that assigns dedicated equipment to each customer"],"eEn":"Aggregating the demand of all customers lowers procurement costs, and the savings are passed on to customers as price reductions. Pay-as-you-go unit prices do not rise as users increase; they fall through economies of scale. Assigning dedicated equipment to each customer loses the benefit of sharing and raises costs."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"キャパシティの推測が不要になることのメリットはどれか。","o":["需要に応じた自動的なリソースの増減","半年前に必要台数を確定し予約する運用","予備機を物理購入して在庫として持つ","ピークを見込み常に最大容量を確保し続ける"],"a":0,"e":"過剰調達や不足の回避。実需要に合わせた最適なスケール。半年前に台数を確定する運用、予備機の在庫、ピークに合わせた常時最大容量は、いずれも需要を推測して先に確保する方式で、過剰や不足が起きやすい。","qEn":"Which is a benefit of no longer having to guess capacity?","oEn":["Automatically scaling resources up and down with demand","An operation that fixes the required number of servers six months ahead and reserves them","Buying spare machines and keeping them in stock","Continuously reserving maximum capacity in anticipation of peaks"],"eEn":"It avoids over-provisioning and shortages, and scales optimally to actual demand. Fixing server counts six months ahead, stocking spare machines, and always holding peak capacity are all approaches that guess demand and secure capacity in advance, which easily leads to excess or shortage."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"新しいリソースを数分で起動できることが示すクラウドの特性はどれか。","o":["物理機材の納品を待って構築を始める必要性","サーバー調達に数週間かかる待ち時間の発生","調達承認や契約手続きが増える運用の複雑化","開発・提供スピードを高める俊敏性（アジリティ）"],"a":3,"e":"物理機材の調達期間が不要。アイデアの即時検証が可能な環境。機材の納品待ちや調達に数週間かかる状態、承認・契約手続きの増加は、クラウドが解消する従来型の課題で、数分で起動できる特性とは逆の説明。","qEn":"Which cloud characteristic is demonstrated by being able to launch new resources in minutes?","oEn":["The need to wait for physical equipment to be delivered before building starts","Waiting times of several weeks to procure servers","Greater operational complexity from more procurement approvals and contract procedures","Agility, which increases development speed"],"eEn":"No lead time for procuring physical equipment is needed, which allows ideas to be tested immediately. Waiting for equipment delivery, procurement taking several weeks, and added approval and contract procedures are traditional problems the cloud eliminates, the opposite of the ability to launch in minutes."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"データセンターの運用・保守をAWS（Amazon Web Services）へ任せることで得られる効果はどれか。","o":["サーバーラックの物理保守を内製化する必要","サーバーOSのパッチ適用をすべて自社で担う運用","差別化につながらない作業からの解放","電源や冷却設備の保守を自社で担う負担増"],"a":2,"e":"ラック管理や電源・空調の運用が不要。本業への集中という選択。ラックの物理保守や電源・冷却設備の保守を自社で担うのは、AWSに任せれば不要になる作業。OSのパッチ適用をすべて自社で担う運用も、任せることで得られる効果ではない。","qEn":"Which is an effect of entrusting data center operation and maintenance to AWS (Amazon Web Services)?","oEn":["The need to handle physical maintenance of server racks in-house","An operation in which the company handles all server OS patching itself","Freedom from undifferentiated heavy lifting","An increased burden of maintaining power and cooling equipment in-house"],"eEn":"Rack management and power and cooling operations are no longer needed, which allows focus on the core business. Physical rack maintenance and maintaining power and cooling equipment in-house are tasks that become unnecessary when entrusted to AWS. Handling all OS patching in-house is also not an effect of entrusting operations to AWS."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"Well-Architected Frameworkで「変更を小さく頻繁に行う」ことを重視する柱はどれか。","o":["運用上の優秀性","セキュリティ","コスト最適化","パフォーマンス効率"],"a":0,"e":"手作業の自動化と継続的改善が中心。失敗から学ぶ運用文化。セキュリティは権限やデータの保護、コスト最適化は支出の見直し、パフォーマンス効率は適切なリソース選択が中心で、変更を小さく頻繁に行うことは運用上の優秀性の原則。","qEn":"Which pillar of the Well-Architected Framework emphasizes making frequent, small changes?","oEn":["Operational Excellence","Security","Cost Optimization","Performance Efficiency"],"eEn":"It centers on automating manual work and continuous improvement, with a culture of learning from failure. Security centers on protecting permissions and data, Cost Optimization on reviewing spending, and Performance Efficiency on choosing appropriate resources; making frequent, small changes is a principle of Operational Excellence."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"障害を見越して回復力のある設計を求める柱はどれか。","o":["堅牢性","信頼性の柱","弾力性","可用性"],"a":1,"e":"自動復旧と水平スケールが要点。需要変化への適応力。堅牢性、弾力性、可用性はWell-Architected Frameworkの柱の名称ではなく、回復力のある設計を求める柱は信頼性。","qEn":"Which pillar calls for resilient design that anticipates failures?","oEn":["Robustness","Reliability","Elasticity","Availability"],"eEn":"The key points are automatic recovery and horizontal scaling, and the ability to adapt to changing demand. Robustness, Elasticity, and Availability are not names of Well-Architected Framework pillars; the pillar that calls for resilient design is Reliability."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"不要なリソースを排除し支出を継続的に見直す柱はどれか。","o":["コスト最適化","持続可能性","運用上の優秀性","パフォーマンス効率"],"a":0,"e":"必要なリソースのみの利用が原則。支出の可視化と分析。持続可能性は環境負荷の低減、運用上の優秀性は運用の自動化と改善、パフォーマンス効率は要件に合う性能の確保が目的で、支出の継続的な見直しが中心ではない。","qEn":"Which pillar involves eliminating unnecessary resources and continuously reviewing spending?","oEn":["Cost Optimization","Sustainability","Operational Excellence","Performance Efficiency"],"eEn":"The principle is to use only the resources you need, with visibility and analysis of spending. Sustainability aims to reduce environmental impact, Operational Excellence to automate and improve operations, and Performance Efficiency to ensure performance that meets requirements; none of them centers on continuously reviewing spending."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ワークロードの環境負荷低減を目的に追加された柱はどれか。","o":["コスト最適化","セキュリティ","持続可能性","運用上の優秀性"],"a":2,"e":"エネルギー消費の最小化が目的。マネージドサービスの活用。コスト最適化は支出、セキュリティはデータやシステムの保護、運用上の優秀性は運用の改善が中心で、環境負荷の低減を目的として加わった柱ではない。","qEn":"Which pillar was added with the aim of reducing the environmental impact of workloads?","oEn":["Cost Optimization","Security","Sustainability","Operational Excellence"],"eEn":"The goal is to minimize energy consumption, for example by using managed services. Cost Optimization centers on spending, Security on protecting data and systems, and Operational Excellence on improving operations; none of them was added with the aim of reducing environmental impact."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"単一障害点をなくす設計が直接寄与する品質はどれか。","o":["一貫性の向上","処理速度の向上","弾力性の向上","システム可用性の向上"],"a":3,"e":"冗長構成による継続稼働。一部故障時のサービス維持。一貫性や処理速度は、単一障害点をなくしても直接は上がらない。弾力性は需要に応じた増減の特性で、故障への耐性とは別の概念。","qEn":"Which quality does a design that eliminates single points of failure directly contribute to?","oEn":["Improved consistency","Improved processing speed","Improved elasticity","Improved availability"],"eEn":"Redundant configurations keep the system running and maintain service when part of it fails. Consistency and processing speed do not directly improve by eliminating single points of failure. Elasticity is a characteristic of scaling with demand and is a separate concept from tolerance to failure."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"疎結合（Loose Coupling）の設計がもたらす利点はどれか。","o":["全コンポーネントを密結合し同期的に呼び出す構成","個々の変更が全体へ即座に波及する構造","コンポーネント間の依存低減と障害の局所化","単一障害点を増やし依存関係を強める設計"],"a":2,"e":"一部の不調が全体へ波及しにくい構造。独立した拡張が可能。密結合で同期的に呼び出す構成は依存が強く、障害が全体へ広がる。変更が全体へ即座に波及する構造も、疎結合とは逆の特徴。","qEn":"Which is a benefit of a loosely coupled design?","oEn":["A configuration where all components are tightly coupled and called synchronously","A structure where each change immediately ripples through the whole system","Reduced dependencies between components and localized failures","A design that adds single points of failure and strengthens dependencies"],"eEn":"The structure makes it harder for a problem in one part to spread to the whole, and components can be scaled independently. A tightly coupled configuration with synchronous calls has strong dependencies, so failures spread throughout. A structure where changes ripple immediately through the whole system is also the opposite of loose coupling."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"単一のサーバーを増強する拡張方式の呼称はどれか。","o":["水平スケールアウト","ロードバランシングによる負荷分散","オートスケーリングによる台数調整","垂直スケーリング（スケールアップ）"],"a":3,"e":"CPU・メモリの増強による対応。物理的な上限という制約。水平スケーリングは台数を増やす方式で、1台の増強ではない。ロードバランシングは負荷を複数台に分ける仕組み、オートスケーリングは台数の自動調整で、どちらも1台の性能を高める方式ではない。","qEn":"What is the name of the scaling approach that increases the capacity of a single server?","oEn":["Horizontal scaling (scale out)","Load balancing to distribute load","Adjusting the number of instances with Auto Scaling","Vertical scaling (scale up)"],"eEn":"It handles demand by adding CPU and memory, but is limited by physical constraints. Horizontal scaling increases the number of servers rather than upgrading one. Load balancing distributes load across multiple servers and Auto Scaling adjusts the number of servers automatically, so neither increases the performance of a single server."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サーバー台数を増やして処理能力を高める方式の呼称はどれか。","o":["垂直スケールアップ","水平スケーリング（スケールアウト）","インスタンスタイプのリサイジング","EBSスナップショットによる複製"],"a":1,"e":"並列処理による負荷分散。クラウドが得意とする拡張方式。垂直スケーリングは1台のCPUやメモリを増強する方式で台数は増えない。インスタンスタイプのリサイジングも同じ垂直方向の変更。EBSスナップショットはバックアップで、処理能力を高める手段ではない。","qEn":"What is the name of the approach that increases processing capacity by adding more servers?","oEn":["Vertical scaling (scale up)","Horizontal scaling (scale out)","Resizing the instance type","Replication with EBS snapshots"],"eEn":"It distributes load through parallel processing and is a scaling approach the cloud does well. Vertical scaling increases the CPU and memory of a single server and does not increase the number of servers. Resizing the instance type is also a vertical change. EBS snapshots are backups and not a means of increasing processing capacity."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）グローバルインフラで最も大きな地理的単位はどれか。","o":["データセンター","ローカルゾーン","サブネット","リージョン"],"a":3,"e":"地理的に独立した複数AZの集合。データ所在地の選択単位。データセンターは1つの施設で、AZはそれらの集まり。ローカルゾーンはリージョンを都市の近くへ拡張する施設、サブネットはVPC内のネットワーク区画で、いずれも最大の地理的単位ではない。","qEn":"Which is the largest geographic unit in the AWS (Amazon Web Services) global infrastructure?","oEn":["Data center","Local Zone","Subnet","Region"],"eEn":"It is a set of multiple geographically independent AZs and the unit for choosing where data resides. A data center is a single facility, and an AZ is a group of them. A Local Zone is a facility that extends a Region closer to a city, and a subnet is a network segment within a VPC; neither is the largest geographic unit."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"1つのリージョン内で物理的に分離された施設群を指すものはどれか。","o":["リージョン（地理的な最大単位）","アベイラビリティーゾーン（AZ）","エッジロケーション（CDN配信拠点）","ローカルゾーン（都市近接の拡張）"],"a":1,"e":"独立した電源・冷却・ネットワークを保持。複数AZ構成で高可用性。リージョンはAZを束ねる上位の単位。エッジロケーションはCDNの配信拠点、ローカルゾーンは特定の都市の近くへリージョンを拡張したもので、リージョン内の分離された施設群ではない。","qEn":"Which term refers to a group of physically separate facilities within a single Region?","oEn":["Region (the largest geographic unit)","Availability Zone (AZ)","Edge location (CDN delivery site)","Local Zone (extension close to a city)"],"eEn":"Each has independent power, cooling, and networking, and a multi-AZ configuration provides high availability. A Region is a higher-level unit that groups AZs. An edge location is a CDN delivery site and a Local Zone extends a Region close to a specific city; neither is a group of separate facilities within a Region."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エンドユーザーに近い場所でコンテンツを配信する拠点はどれか。","o":["アベイラビリティーゾーン","エッジロケーション","オリジンサーバー","ローカルゾーン"],"a":1,"e":"CDNの配信点。低レイテンシー配信の基盤。アベイラビリティーゾーンはリージョン内のデータセンター群で、利用者へのコンテンツ配信拠点ではない。オリジンサーバーは配信元のデータを持つ側で、利用者に近いとは限らない。","qEn":"Which is the site that delivers content close to end users?","oEn":["Availability Zone","Edge location","Origin server","Local Zone"],"eEn":"It is a CDN delivery point and the foundation for low-latency delivery. An Availability Zone is a group of data centers within a Region and is not a content delivery site for users. An origin server holds the source data for delivery and is not necessarily close to users."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウド移行で「ほぼそのまま移す」最小限の手法を表す7Rの1つはどれか。","o":["リパーチェス（SaaSへ乗り換え）","リプラットフォーム（一部最適化）","リホスト（リフト＆シフト）","リファクタリング（作り替え）"],"a":2,"e":"アプリ変更なしの移設。最短での移行という選択。リプラットフォームはデータベースをマネージドサービスにするなど一部を最適化する。リパーチェスはSaaSへの乗り換え、リファクタリングは作り替えで、どちらもほぼそのまま移す手法ではない。","qEn":"Which of the 7 Rs describes the minimal approach to cloud migration of moving things \"almost as they are\"?","oEn":["Repurchase (switch to SaaS)","Replatform (partial optimization)","Rehost (lift and shift)","Refactor (rebuild)"],"eEn":"It moves the application without changes and is the choice for the fastest migration. Replatform makes partial optimizations, such as moving the database to a managed service. Repurchase switches to SaaS and Refactor rebuilds the application; neither moves things almost as they are."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"アプリを大幅に作り変えてクラウド最適化する7Rの手法はどれか。","o":["リプラットフォーム（最小限の調整）","リホスト（そのまま移行するだけ）","リファクタリング／リアーキテクト（再設計）","リパーチェス（SaaS製品へ切替）"],"a":2,"e":"クラウドネイティブ化が目的。工数大・効果大の手法。リホストはアプリを変更せず移す方法、リプラットフォームは最小限の調整で移す方法で、どちらも大幅な作り替えではない。リパーチェスは既存製品をSaaSへ切り替えるだけで、作り替えとは異なる。","qEn":"Which of the 7 Rs substantially reworks an application to optimize it for the cloud?","oEn":["Replatform (minimal adjustments)","Rehost (move as is)","Refactor / Re-architect","Repurchase (switch to a SaaS product)"],"eEn":"Its aim is to become cloud native, and it is the approach with high effort and high benefit. Rehost moves the application without changes and Replatform moves it with minimal adjustments; neither is a substantial rework. Repurchase merely switches an existing product to SaaS, which differs from rebuilding."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Cloud Adoption Framework（CAF）が示すものはどれか。","o":["システムアーキテクチャを評価する6本の設計の柱","料金と割引を定めた購入オプション一覧","組織のクラウド導入を支援する6つの観点","移行を分類する7つのRの戦略群"],"a":2,"e":"ビジネス・人材・ガバナンス・プラットフォーム・セキュリティ・オペレーション。システム設計を評価する6本の柱はWell-Architected Framework、移行を分類する7つのRは移行戦略で、CAFとは別。料金と割引の一覧もCAFの内容ではない。","qEn":"What does the AWS (Amazon Web Services) Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF) provide?","oEn":["Six design pillars for evaluating a system architecture","A list of purchase options defining pricing and discounts","Six perspectives that support an organization's cloud adoption","A set of seven R strategies for categorizing migrations"],"eEn":"The perspectives are Business, People, Governance, Platform, Security, and Operations. The six pillars for evaluating system design belong to the Well-Architected Framework, and the seven Rs for categorizing migrations are migration strategies, both separate from CAF. A list of pricing and discounts is also not part of CAF."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"利用者の管理範囲が最も広いサービスモデルはどれか。","o":["IaaS","FaaS","PaaS","SaaS"],"a":0,"e":"OS以上を利用者が管理。高い自由度という特性。PaaSはOSやミドルウェアをAWSが管理し、利用者はアプリとデータが中心になる。FaaSはさらにサーバーを意識せず関数のコードだけを管理し、SaaSは完成したソフトを使うだけなので、管理範囲は狭い。","qEn":"Which service model gives the customer the broadest scope of management?","eEn":"The customer manages the OS and above, which gives a high degree of freedom. With PaaS, AWS manages the OS and middleware and the customer mainly handles the application and data. FaaS goes further, where the customer manages only function code without thinking about servers, and with SaaS the customer simply uses finished software, so their management scope is narrow."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"アプリ開発に集中でき、OSやミドルウェアを意識しない提供形態はどれか。","o":["DaaS","PaaS（基盤）","IaaS","SaaS"],"a":1,"e":"実行基盤をクラウドが管理。コード提供への集中。IaaSではOSやミドルウェアの管理が利用者側に残り、SaaSは完成したアプリを利用する形態である。DaaSは仮想デスクトップを提供する形態で、アプリ開発の基盤ではない。","qEn":"Which delivery model lets you focus on application development without worrying about the OS or middleware?","eEn":"The cloud manages the runtime platform, so you concentrate on providing code. With IaaS, managing the OS and middleware remains the customer's responsibility, and SaaS is a model for using a finished application. DaaS provides virtual desktops and is not a foundation for application development."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"エラスティシティ（弾力性）が示す特性はどれか。","o":["物理上限まで固定的に確保する仕組み","将来の拡張余地をあらかじめ確保する能力","需要変化に応じた自動的な増減","常に最大構成で稼働させ続ける方式"],"a":2,"e":"ピーク時の拡張と閑散時の縮小。コストの最適化。物理上限まで固定的に確保する方式や常に最大構成で稼働させる方式は、閑散時も費用がかかり縮小しない。将来の拡張余地をあらかじめ確保することは、需要に応じて自動で増減する弾力性とは別の考え方。","qEn":"Which characteristic does elasticity describe?","oEn":["A mechanism that provisions resources up to the physical limit in a fixed way","The ability to reserve room for future expansion in advance","Automatically scaling up and down with changes in demand","A method of always running at maximum configuration"],"eEn":"It expands at peak times and shrinks during quiet times, which optimizes cost. Provisioning up to the physical limit in a fixed way and always running at maximum configuration incur costs even in quiet periods and do not shrink. Reserving room for future expansion in advance is a different idea from elasticity, which scales automatically with demand."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"オンプレミスとクラウドを併用する運用形態の呼称はどれか。","o":["ハイブリッドクラウド","マルチクラウド構成","プライベートクラウド","パブリッククラウド"],"a":0,"e":"既存資産とクラウドの連携。段階的な移行に有効。マルチクラウドは複数のクラウド事業者を使い分ける構成で、オンプレミスとは限らない。プライベートクラウドは自社専用の基盤、パブリッククラウドは共有基盤の利用で、併用の形態ではない。","qEn":"What is the name of the operating model that uses on-premises and the cloud together?","oEn":["Hybrid cloud","Multi-cloud configuration","Private cloud","Public cloud"],"eEn":"It integrates existing assets with the cloud and is effective for gradual migration. Multi-cloud is a configuration that uses multiple cloud providers and does not necessarily involve on-premises. A private cloud is infrastructure dedicated to one company and a public cloud is the use of shared infrastructure; neither is a combined model."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"複数リージョン構成が主に高めるシステム特性はどれか。","o":["災害復旧（DR）能力と可用性","単一AZ内での処理性能の最大化","画面表示の応答速度の向上","ストレージ保存単価の直接的な削減"],"a":0,"e":"地理的に離れた拠点での冗長化。広域障害への耐性。複数リージョン構成の主目的は耐障害性で、単一AZ内の処理性能や画面表示の速度を高めるためではない。ストレージ単価も下がらず、複製分の費用がむしろ増える。","qEn":"Which system characteristics does a multi-Region configuration mainly improve?","oEn":["Disaster recovery (DR) capability and availability","Maximizing processing performance within a single AZ","Faster screen display response","A direct reduction in storage unit prices"],"eEn":"It provides redundancy across geographically distant sites and resilience to wide-area failures. The main purpose of a multi-Region configuration is fault tolerance, not to maximize processing performance within a single AZ or speed up screen display. Storage unit prices also do not fall; the cost of replication actually increases."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）責任共有モデルで、AWSが担う「クラウド本体のセキュリティ」に含まれるものはどれか。","o":["ゲストOSのパッチ適用とセキュリティグループ設定","IAMユーザーの権限設計とS3公開設定の管理","物理施設・ハードウェア・基盤ソフトウェアの保護と保守","顧客データの暗号化とアクセス権限の設定"],"a":2,"e":"データセンターの建物、サーバー機器、ハイパーバイザーなどの基盤はAWSが保護する。ゲストOSのパッチ、セキュリティグループ、S3公開設定、データの暗号化と権限は、利用者の責任である。","qEn":"In the AWS (Amazon Web Services) Shared Responsibility Model, which item is included in \"security of the cloud,\" for which AWS is responsible?","oEn":["Guest OS patching and security group configuration","IAM user permission design and management of S3 public access settings","Protection of physical facilities, hardware, and foundational software","Encryption of customer data and configuring access permissions"],"eEn":"AWS protects the foundation, such as the data center buildings, server equipment, and hypervisors. Guest OS patches, security groups, S3 public access settings, and data encryption and permissions are the customer's responsibility."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"責任共有モデルで、利用者が担う「クラウド内のセキュリティ」に含まれるものはどれか。","o":["ホスト用ハードウェアの保守と交換","データ・OS設定・IAM・アプリの管理責任","データセンターの物理的な警備と入退室管理","基盤ネットワークとハイパーバイザーの維持"],"a":1,"e":"利用者は、データ、OS設定、IAM、アプリなど「クラウド内」を守る。ホスト用ハードウェアの保守、データセンターの警備、基盤ネットワークとハイパーバイザーの維持はAWSの担当である。","qEn":"In the Shared Responsibility Model, which item is included in \"security in the cloud,\" for which the customer is responsible?","oEn":["Maintenance and replacement of host hardware","Management of data, OS configuration, IAM, and applications","Physical security and access control at data centers","Maintenance of the underlying network and hypervisor"],"eEn":"Customers protect what is \"in the cloud,\" such as data, OS configuration, IAM, and applications. Maintaining host hardware, data center security, and maintaining the underlying network and hypervisor are AWS's responsibility."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）利用時、ゲストOSのパッチ適用を担う主体はどれか。","o":["サポート","AWS","ベンダー","利用者（顧客）"],"a":3,"e":"OS以上は利用者管理。AWSは基盤を担当。AWSが担うのは物理基盤とハイパーバイザーまでで、EC2のゲストOSには手を出さない。サポートは問い合わせ対応の窓口で、パッチを適用する主体ではない。","qEn":"When using EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud), who is responsible for patching the guest OS?","oEn":["Support","AWS","The vendor","The customer"],"eEn":"The OS and above are managed by the customer, while AWS handles the foundation. AWS is responsible only up to the physical infrastructure and hypervisor and does not touch the guest OS of EC2. Support is a contact point for inquiries and is not the party that applies patches."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"IAM（Identity and Access Management）の主な役割はどれか。","o":["保存データと通信経路の暗号化処理を担う機能","APIコールやアクティビティのログを記録する機能","利用料金の集計と請求書の発行を行う機能","AWSリソースへのアクセスの認証・認可の管理"],"a":3,"e":"IAMは、誰がAWSリソースに何をできるかを認証・認可で管理する。保存データと通信の暗号化は暗号化機能、APIのログ記録はCloudTrail、料金の集計と請求は課金の機能が担う。","qEn":"What is the main role of IAM (Identity and Access Management)?","oEn":["A feature that encrypts stored data and communication paths","A feature that records logs of API calls and activity","A feature that totals usage charges and issues invoices","Managing authentication and authorization for access to AWS resources"],"eEn":"IAM manages, through authentication and authorization, who can do what with AWS resources. Encryption of stored data and communications is handled by encryption features, API logging by CloudTrail, and charge totals and invoicing by billing features."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）アカウント作成時に生成され、すべての権限を持つ存在はどれか。","o":["フェデレーション","IAM管理者ユーザー","IAMロール","ルートユーザー"],"a":3,"e":"ルートユーザーは、アカウント作成時に生成され、すべての権限を持つ最上位のユーザーである。IAM管理者ユーザーやIAMロールは後から作るもので、フェデレーションは外部IDで一時的にサインインする方式である。","qEn":"Which entity is created when an AWS (Amazon Web Services) account is created and has all permissions?","oEn":["Federation","IAM administrator user","IAM role","Root user"],"eEn":"The root user is the top-level user created with the account and has all permissions. IAM administrator users and IAM roles are created later, and federation is a method of signing in temporarily with an external identity."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ルートユーザーの保護として最優先で実施すべき対策はどれか。","o":["MFA（多要素認証）の有効化","ルート用アクセスキーを新規に発行する","全操作を許可するポリシーを付与する","パスワードを短く覚えやすくする"],"a":0,"e":"ルートユーザーは権限が最強なので、MFA(多要素認証)の有効化が最優先となる。ルート用アクセスキーの新規発行や全操作を許可するポリシーの付与は危険で、パスワードは短くせず長く複雑にする。","qEn":"Which measure should be implemented first to protect the root user?","oEn":["Enable MFA (multi-factor authentication)","Issue a new access key for the root user","Attach a policy that allows all actions","Make the password short and easy to remember"],"eEn":"The root user has the most powerful permissions, so enabling MFA (multi-factor authentication) is the top priority. Issuing a new root access key or attaching a policy that allows all actions is dangerous, and the password should be long and complex, not short."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"共通権限を複数ユーザーへ一括付与する仕組みはどれか。","o":["IAMグループ","IAMポリシー","IAMロール","IAMユーザー"],"a":0,"e":"IAMグループは、複数のユーザーをまとめ、共通の権限を一括で付与する仕組みである。IAMポリシーは権限の内容そのもの、IAMロールは一時的に引き受ける権限、IAMユーザーは個人を表す。","qEn":"Which mechanism grants common permissions to multiple users at once?","oEn":["IAM group","IAM policy","IAM role","IAM user"],"eEn":"An IAM group collects multiple users and grants common permissions to them at once. An IAM policy is the content of the permissions themselves, an IAM role is a set of permissions assumed temporarily, and an IAM user represents an individual."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）やサービスへ一時的に権限を委譲する仕組みはどれか。","o":["IAMロール（一時権限）","IAMユーザー","アクセスキー","IAMグループ"],"a":0,"e":"一時的な認証情報の発行。長期キー不要の委譲。IAMユーザーやアクセスキーは長期の認証情報で、一時的な委譲には向かない。IAMグループはユーザーをまとめて権限を付ける入れ物で、権限を引き受ける仕組みではない。","qEn":"Which mechanism temporarily delegates permissions to EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) or other services?","oEn":["IAM role","IAM user","Access key","IAM group"],"eEn":"Issues temporary credentials; delegation without long-term keys. IAM users and access keys are long-term credentials and are not suited to temporary delegation. An IAM group is a container for attaching permissions to a set of users, not a mechanism for assuming permissions."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"権限の内容を定義するJSONドキュメントはどれか。","o":["IAMグループ","IAMポリシー","セキュリティグループ","IAMロール"],"a":1,"e":"許可・拒否の明文化。エンティティへの関連付け。IAMグループやIAMロールは権限を受け取る側のエンティティで、ポリシーを関連付ける対象。セキュリティグループはJSONの権限定義ではなく、インスタンスの通信を制御するファイアウォール。","qEn":"Which JSON document defines the contents of permissions?","oEn":["IAM group","IAM policy","Security group","IAM role"],"eEn":"States allow and deny explicitly; attached to entities. IAM groups and IAM roles are entities that receive permissions, and the policy is attached to them. A security group is not a JSON permission definition; it is a firewall that controls instance traffic."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティのベストプラクティスとして推奨される権限付与の原則はどれか。","o":["フェイルセーフの原則","最小権限の原則","多層防御の原則","職務分離の原則"],"a":1,"e":"最小権限の原則は、必要最小限の権限だけを与えて攻撃面を小さくする考え方である。多層防御は防御を重ねる設計、職務分離は担当を分ける統制、フェイルセーフは障害時に安全側へ倒す設計である。","qEn":"Which principle of granting permissions is recommended as a security best practice?","oEn":["Principle of fail-safe","Principle of least privilege","Principle of defense in depth","Principle of separation of duties"],"eEn":"The principle of least privilege grants only the minimum permissions required, which reduces the attack surface. Defense in depth is a design that layers defenses, separation of duties is a control that divides responsibilities, and fail-safe is a design that defaults to a safe state on failure."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"IAM（Identity and Access Management）で「明示的な拒否」が持つ効力はどれか。","o":["明示的な許可があれば無効化される","許可より優先される最終的な明示的拒否","評価対象から除外され無視される","警告を表示するが操作は許可される"],"a":1,"e":"IAMでは、明示的な拒否は許可より優先される最終的な拒否で、他のポリシーに許可があっても覆らない。許可で無効化されることも、評価から除外されることも、警告だけで済むこともない。","qEn":"What effect does an explicit deny have in IAM (Identity and Access Management)?","oEn":["It is overridden by an explicit allow","A final deny that takes precedence over any allow","It is excluded from evaluation and ignored","It shows a warning but still permits the action"],"eEn":"In IAM, an explicit deny is a final deny that takes precedence over allows, and it cannot be overridden even if another policy allows the action. It is not overridden by an allow, excluded from evaluation, or reduced to a mere warning."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Organizationsで組織全体の権限上限を設定する機能はどれか。","o":["セキュリティグループ（通信制御）","SCP（サービスコントロールポリシー）","AWS Config（構成の記録）","IAMポリシー（個別権限の定義）"],"a":1,"e":"許可の上限を定義。アカウント横断の制御。IAMポリシーは個別の権限を定義するもので、組織全体の上限は決めない。セキュリティグループは通信の制御、AWS Configは構成の記録と評価で、権限の上限設定はしない。","qEn":"Which feature sets the maximum permissions for an entire organization in Organizations?","oEn":["Security group (traffic control)","SCP (service control policy)","AWS Config (configuration recording and evaluation)","IAM policy (defining individual permissions)"],"eEn":"Defines the maximum permissions allowed; controls across accounts. An IAM policy defines individual permissions and does not set an organization-wide maximum. Security groups control traffic and AWS Config records and evaluates configurations; neither sets a permissions maximum."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ネットワークトラフィックをインスタンス単位で制御するステートフルな仕組みはどれか。","o":["ルートテーブルによる経路制御","インターネットゲートウェイ","セキュリティグループ","ネットワークACL（NACL）"],"a":2,"e":"ステートフルな仮想ファイアウォール。許可ルールのみ。ネットワークACLはサブネット単位でステートレス。ルートテーブルは経路を決める設定、インターネットゲートウェイはVPCとインターネットをつなぐ出入口で、トラフィックの許可・拒否はしない。","qEn":"Which stateful mechanism controls network traffic at the instance level?","oEn":["Routing control by route tables","Internet gateway","Security group","Network ACL (NACL)"],"eEn":"A stateful virtual firewall; allow rules only. A network ACL is stateless and works at the subnet level. A route table sets routing and an internet gateway is the entry and exit point between the VPC and the internet; neither allows or denies traffic."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"サブネット単位でトラフィックを制御するステートレスな仕組みはどれか。","o":["ネットワークACL（NACL）","ルートテーブル（Route Table）","VPCエンドポイント経由の接続","セキュリティグループによる制御"],"a":0,"e":"サブネット境界の制御。許可・拒否の両方を定義。セキュリティグループはインスタンス単位のステートフルな制御で、許可ルールのみを持つ。ルートテーブルは経路を決めるもので、通信の許可・拒否はしない。VPCエンドポイントはAWSサービスへの閉域接続の手段。","qEn":"Which stateless mechanism controls traffic at the subnet level?","oEn":["Network ACL (NACL)","Route table","Connection through a VPC endpoint","Control by security groups"],"eEn":"Controls the subnet boundary; defines both allow and deny rules. A security group is a stateful control at the instance level and has allow rules only. A route table sets routing and does not allow or deny traffic. A VPC endpoint is a means of private connection to AWS services."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"論理的に分離された専用仮想ネットワークを提供するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon CloudFront（CDN配信）","AWS Direct Connect（専用線接続）","VPC（Virtual Private Cloud）","Amazon Route 53（DNSサービス）"],"a":2,"e":"利用者専用のネットワーク空間。サブネット設計の基盤。CloudFrontはコンテンツ配信のCDN、Direct Connectはオンプレミスとの専用線接続、Route 53はDNSサービスで、いずれも分離された仮想ネットワークを提供するものではない。","qEn":"Which service provides a logically isolated, dedicated virtual network?","oEn":["Amazon CloudFront (CDN service)","AWS Direct Connect (dedicated line connection)","VPC (Virtual Private Cloud)","Amazon Route 53 (DNS service)"],"eEn":"A network space dedicated to the customer; the foundation for subnet design. CloudFront is a CDN for content delivery, Direct Connect is a dedicated line to on-premises, and Route 53 is a DNS service; none of them provides an isolated virtual network."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"DDoS（Distributed Denial of Service）攻撃から保護する標準サービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Macie","AWS WAF（L7防御）","AWS Shield","GuardDuty脅威検知"],"a":2,"e":"L3/L4攻撃の緩和。Standardは自動・無料。WAFはレイヤー7のWebリクエストを検査する防御で、DDoS全般を緩和する標準サービスではない。MacieとGuardDutyは機密データの検出と脅威検知で、DDoSの緩和は行わない。","qEn":"Which standard service protects against DDoS (Distributed Denial of Service) attacks?","oEn":["Amazon Macie","AWS WAF (Layer 7 protection)","AWS Shield","GuardDuty threat detection"],"eEn":"Mitigates L3/L4 attacks. Standard is automatic and free. WAF inspects web requests at Layer 7 and is not the standard service for mitigating DDoS in general. Macie and GuardDuty detect sensitive data and threats and do not mitigate DDoS."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Webアプリへのレイヤー7攻撃を防ぐサービスはどれか。","o":["Inspector","GuardDuty","AWS WAF","AWS Shield"],"a":2,"e":"SQLインジェクション等の遮断。ルールベースの保護。AWS ShieldはL3/L4のDDoSを緩和するサービスで、リクエスト内容までは検査しない。GuardDutyは脅威の検知、Inspectorは脆弱性の診断で、通信を遮断する役割はない。","qEn":"Which service protects web applications from Layer 7 attacks?","eEn":"Blocks attacks such as SQL injection; rule-based protection. AWS Shield mitigates L3/L4 DDoS and does not inspect request contents. GuardDuty detects threats and Inspector assesses vulnerabilities; neither blocks traffic."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"機械学習で不正・異常なアクティビティを検知する脅威検知サービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Inspector","Amazon GuardDuty（脅威検知）","Amazon Macie","AWS Security Hub"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon GuardDutyは、ログを機械学習などで分析し、不正や異常な動きを継続的に検知する。Amazon Inspectorは脆弱性の診断、Macieは機密データの検出、Security Hubは検出結果の集約を担う。","qEn":"Which threat detection service uses machine learning to detect fraudulent or abnormal activity?","eEn":"Amazon GuardDuty analyzes logs using machine learning and other methods to continuously detect fraudulent or abnormal activity. Amazon Inspector assesses vulnerabilities, Macie detects sensitive data, and Security Hub aggregates findings."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service）内の個人情報など機密データを発見・分類するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon GuardDuty","AWS Config","Amazon Inspector","Amazon Macie"],"a":3,"e":"機械学習による検出。データ漏洩リスクの可視化。GuardDutyは不正なアクティビティの検知、Inspectorは脆弱性の診断が役割で、S3内の機密データは探さない。AWS Configはリソース構成の記録と評価で、データの中身は見ない。","qEn":"Which service discovers and classifies sensitive data such as personal information in S3 (Simple Storage Service)?","eEn":"Detection using machine learning; visualizes data leakage risk. GuardDuty detects fraudulent activity and Inspector assesses vulnerabilities; neither searches for sensitive data in S3. AWS Config records and evaluates resource configurations and does not look at the contents of data."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"暗号鍵の作成・管理を行うサービスはどれか。","o":["ACM（証明書管理）","AWS Shield","AWS KMS","AWS IAM"],"a":2,"e":"AWS KMSは、暗号鍵の作成と管理を集中して行い、多くのAWSサービスと統合されている。ACMは証明書の管理、AWS ShieldはDDoS防御、AWS IAMは権限の管理で、鍵管理ではない。","qEn":"Which service creates and manages encryption keys?","oEn":["ACM (certificate management)","AWS Shield","AWS KMS","AWS IAM"],"eEn":"AWS KMS centrally creates and manages encryption keys and is integrated with many AWS services. ACM manages certificates, AWS Shield protects against DDoS, and AWS IAM manages permissions; none of them is key management."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"APIコールの操作履歴（誰が何をしたか）を記録するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CloudTrail","AWS Config（構成管理）","AWS Artifact","Amazon CloudWatch"],"a":0,"e":"AWS CloudTrailは、APIコールを記録し、誰がいつ何をしたかの監査ログを残す。AWS Configは構成の変更履歴、AWS Artifactは監査資料の入手、Amazon CloudWatchはメトリクスの監視を担う。","qEn":"Which service records the history of API calls (who did what)?","oEn":["AWS CloudTrail","AWS Config (configuration management)","AWS Artifact","Amazon CloudWatch"],"eEn":"AWS CloudTrail records API calls and keeps an audit log of who did what and when. AWS Config tracks configuration change history, AWS Artifact provides audit documents, and Amazon CloudWatch monitors metrics."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"コンプライアンス報告書（監査資料）をオンデマンド取得するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Security Hub","AWS CloudTrail","AWS Config","AWS Artifact"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Artifactは、コンプライアンス報告書や第三者監査の資料をオンデマンドで取得できる。AWS Security Hubは検出結果の集約、CloudTrailは操作ログ、AWS Configは構成の記録である。","qEn":"Which service provides compliance reports (audit documents) on demand?","eEn":"AWS Artifact provides compliance reports and third-party audit documents on demand. AWS Security Hub aggregates findings, CloudTrail records operation logs, and AWS Config records configurations."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"転送中データ（in transit）の保護に用いる仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS KMSによる保存データの暗号化","IAMロールによるアクセス制御","S3バケットポリシーの設定","TLS/SSLによる通信の暗号化"],"a":3,"e":"転送中データは、TLS/SSLで通信経路を暗号化して盗聴を防ぐ。AWS KMSによる保存データの暗号化は保管中の保護で、IAMロールやS3バケットポリシーはアクセス制御であり通信路の保護ではない。","qEn":"Which mechanism is used to protect data in transit?","oEn":["Encrypting data at rest with AWS KMS","Access control with IAM roles","Configuring S3 bucket policies","Encrypting communications with TLS/SSL"],"eEn":"Data in transit is protected by encrypting the communication path with TLS/SSL to prevent eavesdropping. Encrypting stored data with AWS KMS protects data at rest, and IAM roles and S3 bucket policies are access controls, not protection of the communication path."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"仮想サーバーをオンデマンドで提供する代表的なコンピューティングサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Lambda","AWS Fargate","Amazon EC2（仮想サーバー）","Amazon ECS"],"a":2,"e":"OS以上を自由に管理する仮想マシン。幅広いインスタンスタイプ。LambdaとFargateはサーバーを意識せず使う形態で、仮想サーバーそのものではない。ECSはコンテナのオーケストレーションサービスで、仮想サーバーを直接提供するものではない。","qEn":"Which is the typical compute service that provides virtual servers on demand?","eEn":"A virtual machine whose OS and above you manage freely; a wide range of instance types. Lambda and Fargate are used without thinking about servers and are not virtual servers themselves. ECS is a container orchestration service and does not directly provide virtual servers."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"サーバー管理なしでコードをイベント駆動で実行するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon ECS","AWS Fargate","AWS Lambda（関数）","Amazon EC2"],"a":2,"e":"サーバーレスの関数実行。実行時間に応じた課金。EC2はサーバーの管理が必要で、ECSはコンテナの実行を管理するサービス。Fargateはコンテナ向けのサーバーレス実行基盤で、イベントに応じてコードを実行する関数サービスではない。","qEn":"Which service runs code in an event-driven way without server management?","eEn":"Serverless function execution; billed by execution time. EC2 requires server management, and ECS manages the running of containers. Fargate is a serverless compute engine for containers and is not a function service that runs code in response to events."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）の負荷に応じて台数を自動増減する仕組みはどれか。","o":["Elastic Load Balancing（ELB）","Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling","Amazon CloudFront（CDN配信）","Amazon Route 53（DNS）"],"a":1,"e":"需要連動の自動スケール。可用性とコストの両立。ELBはトラフィックを複数台へ分散するだけで、台数は増減しない。CloudFrontはコンテンツ配信、Route 53はDNSで、どちらもEC2の台数には関与しない。","qEn":"Which mechanism automatically increases or decreases the number of EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) instances according to load?","oEn":["Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)","Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling","Amazon CloudFront (CDN delivery)","Amazon Route 53 (DNS)"],"eEn":"Automatic scaling that follows demand; balances availability and cost. ELB only distributes traffic across multiple instances and does not change their number. CloudFront delivers content and Route 53 provides DNS; neither is involved in the number of EC2 instances."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"受信トラフィックを複数のターゲットへ分散するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon CloudFront（コンテンツ配信）","Elastic Load Balancing（ELB）","Amazon API Gateway（API管理）","Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling（自動増減）"],"a":1,"e":"Elastic Load Balancing(ELB)は、受信トラフィックを複数のターゲットへ分散し、単一障害点を避ける。CloudFrontはコンテンツ配信、API GatewayはAPI管理、EC2 Auto Scalingは台数の自動増減である。","qEn":"Which service distributes incoming traffic across multiple targets?","oEn":["Amazon CloudFront (content delivery)","Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)","Amazon API Gateway (API management)","Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling (automatic scaling in and out)"],"eEn":"Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) distributes incoming traffic across multiple targets and avoids a single point of failure. CloudFront delivers content, API Gateway manages APIs, and EC2 Auto Scaling automatically increases or decreases the number of instances."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"HTTP/HTTPSのレイヤー7ルーティングに適したロードバランサーはどれか。","o":["Gateway Load Balancer","Classic Load Balancer（旧世代）","Network Load Balancer","Application Load Balancer（ALB）"],"a":3,"e":"パスやホストでの振り分け。Webアプリ向けの分散。Network Load BalancerはL4でTCP/UDPを扱い、HTTPのパスやホストでは振り分けない。Gateway Load Balancerは仮想アプライアンス向けで、Classic Load Balancerは旧世代でパスやホストベースのルーティングを持たない。","qEn":"Which load balancer is suited to HTTP/HTTPS Layer 7 routing?","oEn":["Gateway Load Balancer","Classic Load Balancer (previous generation)","Network Load Balancer","Application Load Balancer"],"eEn":"Routes by path or host; distribution for web applications. Network Load Balancer works at L4 with TCP/UDP and does not route by HTTP path or host. Gateway Load Balancer is for virtual appliances, and Classic Load Balancer is a previous-generation option without path- or host-based routing."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"コンテナをサーバー管理なしで実行する仕組みはどれか。","o":["Amazon EC2","AWS Fargate","EC2上のDocker","AWS Lambda"],"a":1,"e":"サーバーレスのコンテナ実行。インフラ運用の不要化。EC2やEC2上のDockerは、サーバーの管理が利用者に残る。Lambdaはイベントで関数を実行するサービスで、コンテナ実行基盤という位置づけではない。","qEn":"Which mechanism runs containers without managing servers?","oEn":["Amazon EC2","AWS Fargate","Docker on EC2","AWS Lambda"],"eEn":"Serverless container execution; removes infrastructure operations. With EC2 or Docker on EC2, server management remains with the customer. Lambda is a service that runs functions in response to events and is not positioned as a container execution platform."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Kubernetesをマネージドで提供するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon EKS（K8s）","AWS Lambda","Amazon ECS","AWS Fargate"],"a":0,"e":"標準Kubernetesの運用支援。コンテナ基盤の構築。ECSはAWS独自のコンテナオーケストレーションで、Kubernetesではない。FargateはECSやEKSで使うサーバーレスの実行基盤、Lambdaは関数実行サービスで、どちらもKubernetesを提供するものではない。","qEn":"Which service provides managed Kubernetes?","eEn":"Operational support for standard Kubernetes; building a container platform. ECS is AWS's own container orchestration and is not Kubernetes. Fargate is a serverless compute engine used with ECS and EKS, and Lambda is a function execution service; neither provides Kubernetes."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"オブジェクトストレージとして無制限にデータを保存するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon FSx","Amazon EBS","Amazon EFS","Amazon S3（オブジェクト）"],"a":3,"e":"高耐久性のオブジェクト保存。容量無制限。EBSはEC2にアタッチするブロックストレージ、EFSとFSxはファイルストレージで、オブジェクトストレージではない。","qEn":"Which service stores unlimited amounts of data as object storage?","eEn":"Highly durable object storage; unlimited capacity. EBS is block storage attached to EC2, and EFS and FSx are file storage; none of them is object storage."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）にアタッチするブロックストレージはどれか。","o":["Amazon S3","Amazon EBS","Amazon FSx","Amazon EFS"],"a":1,"e":"インスタンス用の永続ボリューム。OS・DB用途。S3はオブジェクトストレージで、EC2にアタッチするブロックデバイスではない。EFSとFSxはネットワーク経由でマウントするファイルストレージ。","qEn":"Which is the block storage attached to EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)?","eEn":"A persistent volume for instances; for OS and database use. S3 is object storage and is not a block device attached to EC2. EFS and FSx are file storage mounted over the network."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"複数のEC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）から同時マウントできる共有ファイルストレージはどれか。","o":["Amazon EBS","Amazon EFS（NFS）","Amazon S3","Amazon ECR"],"a":1,"e":"スケーラブルな共有ファイル。NFS互換。EBSは原則1台のEC2に接続するブロックストレージで、S3はオブジェクトストレージでありNFSの共有ファイルシステムではない。ECRはコンテナイメージの保管庫で、ファイルとしてマウントするものではない。","qEn":"Which shared file storage can be mounted simultaneously by multiple EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) instances?","eEn":"Scalable shared files; NFS-compatible. EBS is block storage that is generally attached to a single EC2 instance, and S3 is object storage, not an NFS shared file system. ECR is a repository for container images and is not mounted as files."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"アクセス頻度が低いデータを長期・低コストで保管するS3（Simple Storage Service）のクラスはどれか。","o":["S3 Glacier系","S3標準-IA（低頻度）","S3標準（Standard）","S3 One Zone-IA"],"a":0,"e":"長期保管向けの低コスト。取り出し時間とのトレードオフ。S3標準は頻繁なアクセス向けで保管単価が高い。標準-IAとOne Zone-IAは低頻度アクセス向けで即時に取り出せるが、アーカイブとして最も低コストなのはGlacier系。","qEn":"Which S3 (Simple Storage Service) class stores infrequently accessed data for the long term at low cost?","oEn":["S3 Glacier classes","S3 Standard-IA (infrequent access)","S3 Standard","S3 One Zone-IA"],"eEn":"Low cost for long-term storage; a trade-off with retrieval time. S3 Standard is for frequent access and has a higher storage price. Standard-IA and One Zone-IA are for infrequent access with immediate retrieval, but the lowest-cost archive option is the Glacier classes."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"アクセスパターンが変動するデータを自動で最適階層へ移すS3（Simple Storage Service）クラスはどれか。","o":["S3 Intelligent-Tiering（自動階層化）","S3 One Zone-IA（単一AZ）","S3 Glacier Deep Archive","S3標準（S3 Standard）"],"a":0,"e":"利用状況に応じた自動移動。手動管理の不要化。One Zone-IAとS3標準は、アクセスの多寡に応じて自動で階層を移す仕組みを持たない。Glacier Deep Archiveは長期アーカイブ向けで、アクセスが変動するデータには取り出しに時間がかかり不向き。","qEn":"Which S3 (Simple Storage Service) class automatically moves data with changing access patterns to the optimal tier?","oEn":["S3 Intelligent-Tiering","S3 One Zone-IA (single AZ)","S3 Glacier Deep Archive","S3 Standard"],"eEn":"Automatic movement based on usage; no manual management. One Zone-IA and S3 Standard have no mechanism to move data between tiers automatically according to access frequency. Glacier Deep Archive is for long-term archiving and is unsuitable for data with changing access because retrieval takes time."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"マネージドなリレーショナルデータベースを提供するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Neptune","DynamoDB","Amazon RDS","Redshift"],"a":2,"e":"パッチ・バックアップの自動化。複数DBエンジン対応。DynamoDBはNoSQL、Redshiftはデータウェアハウス、Neptuneはグラフデータベースで、いずれもリレーショナルデータベースではない。","qEn":"Which service provides a managed relational database?","eEn":"Automated patching and backups; supports multiple database engines. DynamoDB is NoSQL, Redshift is a data warehouse, and Neptune is a graph database; none of them is a relational database."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"MySQL/PostgreSQL互換でクラウド最適化された高性能DBはどれか。","o":["Amazon Neptune","Amazon Redshift","Amazon Aurora","Amazon DynamoDB"],"a":2,"e":"高い性能と可用性。マネージドの分散ストレージ。NeptuneはグラフDB、RedshiftはDWH、DynamoDBはNoSQLで、MySQL/PostgreSQL互換のリレーショナルデータベースではない。","qEn":"Which high-performance, cloud-optimized database is compatible with MySQL/PostgreSQL?","eEn":"High performance and availability; managed distributed storage. Neptune is a graph database, Redshift is a data warehouse, and DynamoDB is NoSQL; none of them is a MySQL/PostgreSQL-compatible relational database."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ミリ秒応答のフルマネージドNoSQL（Not only SQL）データベースはどれか。","o":["Amazon Redshift","Amazon RDS（RDBMS）","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon Aurora"],"a":2,"e":"キー・バリュー型の高速処理。自動スケール。RDSとAuroraはリレーショナルデータベースで、NoSQLではない。Redshiftはデータウェアハウスで、ミリ秒応答のトランザクション処理向けではない。","qEn":"Which is the fully managed NoSQL (Not only SQL) database with millisecond response times?","eEn":"Fast key-value processing; automatic scaling. RDS and Aurora are relational databases, not NoSQL. Redshift is a data warehouse and is not intended for millisecond-response transaction processing."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ペタバイト級の分析に適したデータウェアハウスはどれか。","o":["Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon Aurora","Amazon Redshift","Amazon RDS（RDBMS）"],"a":2,"e":"大規模分析の高速処理。列指向ストレージ。DynamoDBはNoSQLのキー・バリュー型、AuroraとRDSはトランザクション処理向けのリレーショナルデータベースで、大規模分析のためのデータウェアハウスではない。","qEn":"Which data warehouse is suited to petabyte-scale analytics?","eEn":"Fast processing for large-scale analytics; columnar storage. DynamoDB is a NoSQL key-value database, and Aurora and RDS are relational databases for transaction processing; none of them is a data warehouse for large-scale analytics."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service）上のデータを標準SQL（Structured Query Language）で直接分析するサーバーレスサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Redshift","Amazon Athena","AWS Glue（ETL）","Amazon EMR（Hadoop）"],"a":1,"e":"クエリ実行量に応じた課金。サーバー不要の分析。Redshiftはデータを取り込んで分析する前提のデータウェアハウス。Glueはデータ変換とカタログ作成、EMRはHadoopなどを動かす処理基盤で、S3を直接SQL分析するサービスではない。","qEn":"Which serverless service analyzes data in S3 (Simple Storage Service) directly using standard SQL (Structured Query Language)?","eEn":"Billed by the amount of queries run; analytics without servers. Redshift is a data warehouse that assumes data is loaded before analysis. Glue transforms data and builds catalogs, and EMR is a processing platform that runs Hadoop and the like; neither is a service that analyzes S3 directly with SQL."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ドメイン名をIPアドレスへ変換するDNS（Domain Name System）サービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Direct Connect","Amazon Route 53","Amazon CloudFront","Amazon API Gateway"],"a":1,"e":"DNSルーティングの提供。ヘルスチェックとの連携。Direct Connectはオンプレミスとの専用線接続、CloudFrontはコンテンツ配信、API GatewayはAPIの公開・管理で、名前解決のサービスではない。","qEn":"Which DNS (Domain Name System) service translates domain names into IP addresses?","eEn":"Provides DNS routing; integrates with health checks. Direct Connect is a dedicated line to on-premises, CloudFront delivers content, and API Gateway publishes and manages APIs; none of them is a name resolution service."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"オンプレミスとAWS（Amazon Web Services）を専用線で接続するサービスはどれか。","o":["Internet Gateway（IGW）","AWS Transit Gateway","AWS Direct Connect","AWS Site-to-Site VPN"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Direct Connectは、オンプレミスとAWSを専用線で結び、安定した帯域と低い遅延を確保する。Site-to-Site VPNはインターネット経由の暗号化通信で、Transit GatewayとInternet Gatewayは専用線ではない。","qEn":"Which service connects on-premises environments to AWS (Amazon Web Services) with a dedicated line?","eEn":"AWS Direct Connect links on-premises environments to AWS with a dedicated line, ensuring stable bandwidth and low latency. Site-to-Site VPN is encrypted communication over the internet, and Transit Gateway and Internet Gateway are not dedicated lines."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"メッセージを一時保管し非同期処理を実現するキューサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Kinesis","Amazon SQS","Amazon MQ","Amazon SNS"],"a":1,"e":"コンポーネントの疎結合化。負荷の平準化。SNSは発行されたメッセージを購読者へ配信するサービスで、溜めておいて取り出す用途ではない。Kinesisはストリームデータのリアルタイム処理、Amazon MQは既存のメッセージブローカーを移行するためのサービス。","qEn":"Which queue service temporarily stores messages to enable asynchronous processing?","eEn":"Decouples components; smooths out load. SNS delivers published messages to subscribers and is not for accumulating messages to be retrieved later. Kinesis processes streaming data in real time, and Amazon MQ is a service for migrating existing message brokers."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"発行・購読型でメッセージを複数の宛先へ配信するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon MQ","Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon Kinesis"],"a":2,"e":"プッシュ通知の配信。ファンアウトの実現。SQSはメッセージを溜めて取り出すキューで、複数の宛先へ同時に配るものではない。Kinesisはストリームデータの処理、Amazon MQは既存のメッセージブローカーを移行する用途が中心。","qEn":"Which service delivers messages to multiple destinations using the publish/subscribe model?","eEn":"Delivers push notifications; enables fan-out. SQS is a queue that accumulates messages for retrieval and does not deliver to multiple destinations at once. Kinesis processes streaming data, and Amazon MQ is mainly for migrating existing message brokers."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"インフラをコードで定義し自動構築するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Elastic Beanstalk","AWS Systems Manager","AWS OpsWorks（Chef管理）","AWS CloudFormation"],"a":3,"e":"テンプレートによる構成管理。再現性の確保。Elastic Beanstalkはアプリをデプロイして環境を自動構成するサービスで、インフラ全体をテンプレートで定義するものではない。Systems Managerは運用管理、OpsWorksはChefによる構成管理が中心。","qEn":"Which service defines infrastructure as code and builds it automatically?","oEn":["AWS Elastic Beanstalk","AWS Systems Manager","AWS OpsWorks (Chef management)","AWS CloudFormation"],"eEn":"Configuration management through templates; ensures reproducibility. Elastic Beanstalk deploys applications and configures the environment automatically, but does not define the entire infrastructure in templates. Systems Manager is for operations management, and OpsWorks centers on configuration management with Chef."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"リソースの監視・メトリクス・ログ・アラームを提供するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS X-Ray（分散トレース）","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Config（構成監視）","AWS CloudTrail（API監査）"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon CloudWatchは、メトリクス、ログ、アラームでリソースの稼働を監視する。AWS X-Rayは分散トレース、AWS Configは構成の監視、AWS CloudTrailはAPI操作の監査を担う。","qEn":"Which service provides resource monitoring, metrics, logs, and alarms?","oEn":["AWS X-Ray (distributed tracing)","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Config (configuration monitoring)","AWS CloudTrail (API auditing)"],"eEn":"Amazon CloudWatch monitors the operation of resources with metrics, logs, and alarms. AWS X-Ray provides distributed tracing, AWS Config monitors configurations, and AWS CloudTrail audits API operations."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"基盤モデル（生成AI）をAPIで利用できるサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon SageMaker","Amazon Bedrock","Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Rekognition"],"a":1,"e":"複数の基盤モデルの利用。生成AIの組み込み。SageMakerは自分でモデルを構築・学習・デプロイする基盤、ComprehendとRekognitionは文章分析と画像分析に特化したAIサービスで、基盤モデルをAPIで選んで使うものではない。","qEn":"Which service lets you use foundation models (generative AI) through an API?","eEn":"Use of multiple foundation models; embedding generative AI. SageMaker is a platform for building, training, and deploying your own models, and Comprehend and Rekognition are AI services specialized in text analysis and image analysis; none of them lets you choose and use foundation models through an API."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"機械学習モデルを構築・学習・デプロイする統合サービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Bedrock","Amazon SageMaker","Amazon Rekognition","Amazon Comprehend"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon SageMakerは、機械学習モデルの構築、学習、デプロイまでを一貫して行う統合サービスである。Bedrockは基盤モデルの利用、Rekognitionは画像分析、Comprehendは文章の分析に特化する。（2026年11月時点：2024年12月3日に Amazon SageMaker は Amazon SageMaker AI に改称され、「Amazon SageMaker」はデータ・分析・AIの統合プラットフォームの名称になった。公式試験ガイド v1.3 の記載も Amazon SageMaker AI。再確認のうえ引用すること）","qEn":"Which integrated service builds, trains, and deploys machine learning models?","eEn":"Amazon SageMaker is an integrated service that handles building, training, and deploying machine learning models end to end. Bedrock provides access to foundation models, Rekognition specializes in image analysis, and Comprehend specializes in text analysis. (As of November 2026: on December 3, 2024, Amazon SageMaker was renamed Amazon SageMaker AI, and \"Amazon SageMaker\" now names the unified platform for data, analytics, and AI. Exam guide v1.3 also lists Amazon SageMaker AI. Verify before citing.)"},
  {"d":"D4","q":"EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）の料金モデルで、初期コミットなしに従量で使う方式はどれか。","o":["リザーブドインスタンス","オンデマンドインスタンス（従量課金）","スポットインスタンス","Savings Plans"],"a":1,"e":"長期契約不要の柔軟性。短期・不定期負荷向け。リザーブドインスタンスとSavings Plansは1年または3年の利用をコミットして割引を受ける方式で、初期コミットなしの従量ではない。","qEn":"In the EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) pricing models, which option is pay-as-you-go with no upfront commitment?","oEn":["Reserved Instances","On-Demand Instances","Spot Instances","Savings Plans"],"eEn":"Flexibility with no long-term contract; for short-term or irregular workloads. Reserved Instances and Savings Plans give discounts in exchange for a 1-year or 3-year commitment, so they are not pay-as-you-go without commitment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"1年または3年の利用を確約して割引を得る方式はどれか。","o":["スポットインスタンス（余剰キャパシティ）","専有ホスト（物理サーバーを専有）","リザーブドインスタンス（RI）","オンデマンドインスタンス（従量課金）"],"a":2,"e":"長期コミットでの割引。予測可能な負荷向け。スポットインスタンスは確約なしで余剰キャパシティを安く使う方式で、中断がありうる。専有ホストは物理サーバーを専有する形態で、割引の方式ではない。オンデマンドは確約なしの従量課金。","qEn":"Which option provides a discount in exchange for committing to 1 or 3 years of usage?","oEn":["Spot Instances (spare capacity)","Dedicated Hosts (dedicated physical servers)","Reserved Instances (RI)","On-Demand Instances (pay as you go)"],"eEn":"Discount for a long-term commitment; for predictable workloads. Spot Instances use spare capacity cheaply with no commitment, but can be interrupted. Dedicated Hosts dedicate a physical server and are not a discount option. On-Demand is pay-as-you-go with no commitment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"一定の利用量を金額でコミットする柔軟な割引プランはどれか。","o":["Savings Plans","オンデマンドインスタンス","スポットインスタンス","リザーブドインスタンス（RI）"],"a":0,"e":"利用額コミットでの割引。サービス横断の柔軟性。リザーブドインスタンスは特定のインスタンス構成の利用を確約する方式で、金額ではなく構成を単位にする。オンデマンドとスポットはコミットを伴わない。","qEn":"Which flexible discount plan commits to a certain amount of usage in dollars?","oEn":["Savings Plans","On-Demand Instances","Spot Instances","Reserved Instances (RI)"],"eEn":"Discount for committing to a usage amount; flexible across services. Reserved Instances commit to using a specific instance configuration, so the unit is the configuration, not an amount of money. On-Demand and Spot involve no commitment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の余剰キャパシティを最大割引で利用する方式はどれか。","o":["リザーブドインスタンス","オンデマンドインスタンス","スポットインスタンス","Savings Plans"],"a":2,"e":"スポットインスタンスは、AWSの余剰キャパシティを最大級の割引で使えるが、中断される可能性がある。リザーブドとSavings Plansは長期契約の割引で、オンデマンドは割引のない通常料金である。","qEn":"Which option uses AWS (Amazon Web Services) spare capacity at the largest discount?","oEn":["Reserved Instances","On-Demand Instances","Spot Instances","Savings Plans"],"eEn":"Spot Instances use AWS spare capacity at one of the largest discounts, but they can be interrupted. Reserved Instances and Savings Plans are discounts for long-term commitments, and On-Demand is the regular rate with no discount."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"物理サーバーを専有しライセンス要件に対応する方式はどれか。","o":["Dedicated Instances（専有インスタンス）","オンデマンドインスタンス（従量課金）","リザーブドインスタンス（RI・予約割引）","Dedicated Hosts（専有ホスト）"],"a":3,"e":"Dedicated Hostsは、物理サーバーを専有し、ソケットやコアの情報も把握できるため、ライセンス要件に対応できる。Dedicated Instancesはハードウェア専有だがホストの可視性がなく、オンデマンドやRIは共有基盤が前提である。","qEn":"Which option dedicates a physical server and addresses licensing requirements?","oEn":["Dedicated Instances","On-Demand Instances (pay as you go)","Reserved Instances (RI, reservation discount)","Dedicated Hosts"],"eEn":"Dedicated Hosts dedicate a physical server and expose socket and core information, so they can meet licensing requirements. Dedicated Instances use dedicated hardware but give no visibility into the host, and On-Demand and RIs assume shared infrastructure."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"一定期間または永続的に無料で使える枠の総称はどれか。","o":["トライアル契約（期間限定の試用）","AWS無料利用枠（Free Tier）","AWS Credits（無料クレジット付与）","AWS Activate（スタートアップ支援）"],"a":1,"e":"AWS無料利用枠(Free Tier)は、一定期間または永続的に無料で使える枠の総称で、検証や学習に向く。AWS Creditsは付与される無料クレジット、AWS Activateはスタートアップ支援で、総称ではない。","qEn":"Which term collectively refers to offers that can be used free for a limited period or permanently?","oEn":["Trial contract (time-limited trial)","AWS Free Tier","AWS Credits (free credits granted)","AWS Activate (startup support)"],"eEn":"The AWS Free Tier is the collective term for offers that can be used free for a limited period or permanently, and is suited to testing and learning. AWS Credits are granted free credits and AWS Activate is startup support; neither is the collective term."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"利用前にコストを見積もるツールはどれか。","o":["AWS Budgets（予算アラート）","TCO計算ツール（Migration Evaluator）","AWS Cost Explorer（実績分析）","AWS Pricing Calculator"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Pricing Calculatorは、構成を入力して利用前に費用を見積もるツールである。AWS Budgetsは予算超過のアラート、Cost Explorerは実績の分析、Migration EvaluatorはTCOの試算に使う。","qEn":"Which tool estimates costs before you use services?","oEn":["AWS Budgets (budget alerts)","TCO calculator (Migration Evaluator)","AWS Cost Explorer (analysis of actual usage)","AWS Pricing Calculator"],"eEn":"AWS Pricing Calculator is a tool for entering a configuration and estimating costs before use. AWS Budgets alerts on budget overruns, Cost Explorer analyzes actual usage, and Migration Evaluator is used to estimate TCO."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"過去の利用傾向を可視化し将来予測するツールはどれか。","o":["Cost and Usage Report","AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Budgets（予算管理）"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Cost Explorerは、過去の利用傾向をグラフで可視化し、将来のコストを予測する。Cost and Usage Reportは詳細な利用データの出力、Pricing Calculatorは事前の見積もり、Budgetsは予算管理である。","qEn":"Which tool visualizes past usage trends and forecasts the future?","oEn":["Cost and Usage Report","AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Budgets (budget management)"],"eEn":"AWS Cost Explorer visualizes past usage trends in graphs and forecasts future costs. Cost and Usage Report outputs detailed usage data, Pricing Calculator provides advance estimates, and Budgets manages budgets."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"予算超過時にアラート通知する仕組みはどれか。","o":["CloudWatch","Cost Explorer","Trusted Advisor","AWS Budgets"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Budgetsは、しきい値を設定し、予算を超えそうなときにアラートで通知する。CloudWatchは稼働監視、Cost Explorerは費用の分析、Trusted Advisorはベストプラクティスの助言を担う。","qEn":"Which mechanism sends alerts when a budget is exceeded?","eEn":"AWS Budgets lets you set thresholds and sends alerts when a budget is likely to be exceeded. CloudWatch monitors operation, Cost Explorer analyzes costs, and Trusted Advisor gives best-practice advice."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"詳細な課金明細をデータとして出力する仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Pricing Calculator（事前見積もり）","AWS Cost Explorer（利用実績の可視化）","AWS Cost Anomaly Detection（異常検知）","AWS Cost and Usage Report（CUR）"],"a":3,"e":"最も詳細な使用・コストデータ。分析基盤への連携。Pricing Calculatorは利用前の見積もりツール、Cost Explorerは画面上で実績を可視化するツールで、明細データの出力はしない。Cost Anomaly Detectionは支出の異常を検知する機能。","qEn":"Which mechanism outputs detailed billing line items as data?","oEn":["AWS Pricing Calculator (advance estimates)","AWS Cost Explorer (visualizing actual usage)","AWS Cost Anomaly Detection (anomaly detection)","AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR)"],"eEn":"The most detailed usage and cost data; integrates with analytics platforms. Pricing Calculator is an estimating tool for before use, and Cost Explorer is a tool for visualizing actual usage on screen; neither outputs line-item data. Cost Anomaly Detection is a feature that detects abnormal spending."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"複数アカウントの請求を1つにまとめる仕組みはどれか。","o":["SCP（Service Control Policy）","Cost Categories（コストのグループ化）","コスト配分タグ（Cost Allocation Tags）","一括請求（Consolidated Billing）"],"a":3,"e":"Organizationsでの請求集約。ボリューム割引の共有。SCPは権限の上限を決める仕組みで、請求には関係しない。コスト配分タグとCost Categoriesは費用を分類・集計する仕組みで、複数アカウントの請求を1つにまとめるものではない。","qEn":"Which mechanism combines the billing of multiple accounts into one?","oEn":["SCP (Service Control Policy)","Cost Categories (grouping costs)","Cost Allocation Tags","Consolidated Billing"],"eEn":"Consolidates billing in Organizations; shares volume discounts. SCPs set the maximum permissions and are unrelated to billing. Cost allocation tags and Cost Categories classify and aggregate costs, and do not combine the billing of multiple accounts into one."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"コストを部門やプロジェクト別に集計するための仕組みはどれか。","o":["使用状況レポート","リザーブド割引","コスト配分タグ","Trusted Advisor"],"a":2,"e":"コスト配分タグは、リソースにタグを付けて部門やプロジェクト別に費用を集計できる。使用状況レポートは利用データの出力、リザーブド割引は購入の割引、Trusted Advisorはコスト最適化やセキュリティの推奨を示す機能で、費用を部門別に集計する仕組みではない。","qEn":"Which mechanism is used to aggregate costs by department or project?","oEn":["Usage report","Reserved discounts","Cost allocation tags","Trusted Advisor"],"eEn":"Cost allocation tags let you tag resources and aggregate costs by department or project. A usage report outputs usage data, reserved discounts are purchase discounts, and Trusted Advisor is a feature that gives cost optimization and security recommendations; none aggregates costs by department."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の最も基本的な無料サポートプランはどれか。","o":["エンタープライズサポート","ビジネスサポート","開発者サポート","ベーシックサポート"],"a":3,"e":"全顧客に無償提供。ドキュメントとフォーラム。開発者、ビジネス、エンタープライズの各サポートは有料のプランで、無料で使える基本プランではない。","qEn":"Which is the most basic free support plan for AWS (Amazon Web Services)?","oEn":["Enterprise Support","Business Support","Developer Support","Basic Support"],"eEn":"Provided at no charge to all customers; documentation and forums. Developer, Business, and Enterprise Support are paid plans, not a free basic plan."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"開発・テスト環境向けで業務時間内のメール対応が含まれるプランはどれか。","o":["無料サポート","開発者サポート","ベーシックサポート","ビジネスサポート"],"a":1,"e":"技術的な相談対応。低コストの有償プラン。ベーシックサポートは無料の基本プランで、技術的な問い合わせ対応を含まない。ビジネスサポートは24時間365日の電話・チャットまで含む本番環境向けで、開発・テスト向けの位置づけではない。（2026年11月時点：Developerは2025年12月2日に新規受付を終了し、2027年1月1日に提供終了。後継は月額29ドルからで24時間365日対応のBusiness Support+）","qEn":"Which plan is intended for development and test environments and includes email support during business hours?","oEn":["Free support","Developer Support","Basic Support","Business Support"],"eEn":"Technical consultation; a low-cost paid plan. Basic Support is the free basic plan and does not include technical support. Business Support is for production environments and includes 24/7 phone and chat, so it is not positioned for development and testing. (As of November 2026: Developer Support stopped accepting new subscriptions on December 2, 2025 and will be discontinued on January 1, 2027. Its successor is Business Support+, which starts at $29 per month and offers 24/7 access.)"},
  {"d":"D4","q":"本番環境向けで24時間365日対応・電話/チャットを含むプランはどれか。","o":["開発者サポート（Developer）","AWS re:Post（利用者どうしのコミュニティ）","ベーシックサポート（Basic）","ビジネスサポート+（Business Support+）"],"a":3,"e":"本番向けに24時間365日、電話・チャットで技術支援を受ける入門のプランはビジネスサポート+（2026年10月時点。AWSはサポートを再編中で、Developer・Business・Enterprise On-Rampは2027年1月1日に終了予定）。ベーシックは請求とアカウントの支援が中心で、re:Postは利用者どうしのQ&Aサイトである。","qEn":"Which plan is intended for production environments and includes 24/7 support by phone and chat?","oEn":["Developer Support","AWS re:Post (community Q&A among users)","Basic Support","Business Support+"],"eEn":"The entry-level plan that provides 24/7 technical support by phone and chat for production is Business Support+ (as of October 2026; AWS is restructuring its support, and Developer, Business, and Enterprise On-Ramp are scheduled to end on January 1, 2027). Basic centers on billing and account assistance, and re:Post is a Q&A site among users."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"専任のTAMが付く最上位プランはどれか。","o":["エンタープライズ On-Ramp","開発者サポート（メール対応）","ビジネスサポート（24/7対応）","エンタープライズサポート"],"a":3,"e":"専任の技術担当。最短15分の応答目標（重大時）。エンタープライズ On-Rampは専任のTAMではなく、複数のTAMを共有するプールが付く下位のプラン。ビジネスと開発者サポートにはTAMが付かない。（2026年11月時点：現行の最上位はUnified Operationsで、Enterprise Supportと同じく専任TAMが付く。Enterprise On-Rampは2027年1月1日に提供終了）","qEn":"Which top-tier plan includes a dedicated TAM?","oEn":["Enterprise On-Ramp","Developer Support (email support)","Business Support (24/7 support)","Enterprise Support"],"eEn":"A dedicated technical contact; response target as fast as 15 minutes (for critical cases). Enterprise On-Ramp is a lower-tier plan that comes with a pool of TAMs shared among customers rather than a dedicated TAM. Business and Developer Support do not include a TAM. (As of November 2026: the top plan is now Unified Operations, which, like Enterprise Support, includes a designated TAM. Enterprise On-Ramp will be discontinued on January 1, 2027.)"},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）サービスの稼働状況や障害を確認するダッシュボードはどれか。","o":["AWS CloudTrail（API監査ログ）","Amazon CloudWatch（監視）","AWS Health Dashboard","AWS Trusted Advisor"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Health Dashboardは、AWSサービスの稼働状況や障害、自分のリソースへの影響を確認できる。CloudTrailはAPI監査ログ、CloudWatchは自分のリソースの監視、Trusted Advisorは構成の助言である。","qEn":"Which dashboard shows the operating status and outages of AWS (Amazon Web Services) services?","oEn":["AWS CloudTrail (API audit logs)","Amazon CloudWatch (monitoring)","AWS Health Dashboard","AWS Trusted Advisor"],"eEn":"The AWS Health Dashboard shows the operating status and outages of AWS services and their impact on your own resources. CloudTrail provides API audit logs, CloudWatch monitors your own resources, and Trusted Advisor gives configuration advice."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"ベストプラクティスに基づき構成・コストを助言するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Config（構成評価）","AWS Well-Architected Tool","AWS Trusted Advisor","AWS Compute Optimizer"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Trusted Advisorは、ベストプラクティスに沿って構成やコストの問題をチェックし、改善を助言する。AWS Configは構成の評価、Well-Architected Toolは設計レビュー、Compute Optimizerはサイズの推奨に特化する。","qEn":"Which service advises on configuration and cost based on best practices?","oEn":["AWS Config (configuration evaluation)","AWS Well-Architected Tool","AWS Trusted Advisor","AWS Compute Optimizer"],"eEn":"AWS Trusted Advisor checks for configuration and cost issues against best practices and advises on improvements. AWS Config evaluates configurations, Well-Architected Tool reviews designs, and Compute Optimizer specializes in sizing recommendations."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"データ転送料金で原則無料となる方向はどれか。","o":["アウトバウンド（インターネットへの送信）","インバウンド（AWSへの受信）","同一アベイラビリティゾーン内","リージョン間のデータ転送"],"a":1,"e":"データ転送料金では、AWSへのインバウンド(受信)は原則無料で、課金の中心はアウトバウンドである。インターネットへの送信やリージョン間のデータ転送には料金がかかる。","qEn":"In data transfer pricing, which direction is generally free?","oEn":["Outbound (sending to the internet)","Inbound (receiving into AWS)","Within the same Availability Zone","Data transfer between Regions"],"eEn":"In data transfer pricing, inbound (receiving) traffic into AWS is generally free, and charges center on outbound. Sending to the internet and transferring data between Regions incur charges."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"コスト最適化で「適切なサイズへ見直す」手法はどれか。","o":["スケールアウト（水平スケーリング）","ライトサイジング（Right Sizing）の実施","リザーブドインスタンス（前払い割引）","オートスケーリング（Auto Scaling）"],"a":1,"e":"ライトサイジング(Right Sizing)は、過剰なリソースを実際の需要に合う大きさへ見直す手法である。スケールアウトとオートスケーリングは台数の増減、リザーブドインスタンスは割引購入で、サイズの見直しではない。","qEn":"In cost optimization, which technique is \"reviewing to the appropriate size\"?","oEn":["Scaling out (horizontal scaling)","Right sizing","Reserved Instances (upfront discount)","Auto Scaling"],"eEn":"Right sizing is a technique of adjusting oversized resources to a size that matches actual demand. Scaling out and Auto Scaling increase or decrease the number of instances, and Reserved Instances are a discounted purchase; none of them reviews size."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"コスト異常を自動で検知する機能はどれか。","o":["AWS Cost Anomaly Detection","Amazon CloudWatch（メトリクス監視）","AWS Cost Explorer（傾向分析）","AWS Budgets（予算しきい値アラート）"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Cost Anomaly Detectionは、機械学習で通常と異なる支出を自動検知し、早期に通知する。Cost Explorerは傾向分析、Budgetsは設定したしきい値のアラート、CloudWatchはメトリクス監視である。","qEn":"Which feature automatically detects cost anomalies?","oEn":["AWS Cost Anomaly Detection","Amazon CloudWatch (metric monitoring)","AWS Cost Explorer (trend analysis)","AWS Budgets (threshold alerts on budgets)"],"eEn":"AWS Cost Anomaly Detection uses machine learning to automatically detect spending that differs from the usual and notifies you early. Cost Explorer analyzes trends, Budgets alerts on thresholds you set, and CloudWatch monitors metrics."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"ソフトウェアをAWS（Amazon Web Services）請求に統合して購入できる仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Service Catalog","AWS Artifact（監査文書）","AWS Marketplace","AWS Config（構成管理）"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Marketplaceは、サードパーティ製のソフトウェアをAWSの請求に統合して購入できる。AWS Service Catalogは承認済み製品の配布、AWS Artifactは監査文書、AWS Configは構成管理である。","qEn":"Which mechanism lets you purchase software integrated into your AWS (Amazon Web Services) bill?","oEn":["AWS Service Catalog","AWS Artifact (audit documents)","AWS Marketplace","AWS Config (configuration management)"],"eEn":"AWS Marketplace lets you purchase third-party software integrated into your AWS bill. AWS Service Catalog distributes approved products, AWS Artifact provides audit documents, and AWS Config manages configurations."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"技術的な質問への自己解決を支援する公式Q&Aコミュニティはどれか。","o":["AWS re:Post","Trusted Advisor","AWS Marketplace","AWS ドキュメント"],"a":0,"e":"AWS re:Postは、技術的な質問を投稿して自己解決を図れる公式のQ&Aコミュニティである。Trusted Advisorは構成の助言、AWS Marketplaceはソフトの購入、AWSドキュメントは公式の資料集である。","qEn":"Which official Q&A community supports self-service resolution of technical questions?","oEn":["AWS re:Post","Trusted Advisor","AWS Marketplace","AWS Documentation"],"eEn":"AWS re:Post is the official Q&A community where you can post technical questions and resolve them on your own. Trusted Advisor gives configuration advice, AWS Marketplace is for purchasing software, and AWS Documentation is the official collection of reference materials."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リソースの最適サイズを推奨するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon CloudWatch（使用率監視）","AWS Trusted Advisor（推奨事項）","AWS Cost Explorer（RI推奨）","AWS Compute Optimizer"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Compute Optimizerは、利用実績から最適なサイズを推奨し、コストと性能の改善を助ける。CloudWatchは使用率の監視、Trusted Advisorは推奨事項の確認、Cost ExplorerのRI推奨は購入の提案である。","qEn":"Which service recommends the optimal size for resources?","oEn":["Amazon CloudWatch (utilization monitoring)","AWS Trusted Advisor (recommendations)","AWS Cost Explorer (RI recommendations)","AWS Compute Optimizer"],"eEn":"AWS Compute Optimizer recommends the optimal size based on actual usage and helps improve cost and performance. CloudWatch monitors utilization, Trusted Advisor shows recommendations, and the RI recommendations in Cost Explorer are purchase suggestions."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"複数アカウントの請求を統合しボリューム割引を共有する効果を持つものはどれか。","o":["SCP（サービスコントロールポリシー）","AWS Organizationsの一括請求","各アカウントで個別に支払う請求","コスト配分タグでの部門別集計"],"a":1,"e":"使用量の合算による単価低下。全体最適化。SCPは権限の上限を決める仕組みで、請求とは無関係。各アカウントで個別に支払うと使用量が合算されず、ボリューム割引も共有できない。コスト配分タグは集計用で、請求の統合や割引の共有はしない。","qEn":"Which option has the effect of combining the billing of multiple accounts and sharing volume discounts?","oEn":["SCP (service control policy)","Consolidated billing in Organizations","Billing paid separately by each account","Aggregation by department with cost allocation tags"],"eEn":"Lower unit prices through combined usage; overall optimization. SCPs set the maximum permissions and are unrelated to billing. If each account pays separately, usage is not combined and volume discounts cannot be shared. Cost allocation tags are for aggregation and do not consolidate billing or share discounts."}];

var SET2 = [
  {"d":"D1","q":"システムが障害から自動的に立ち直る能力を表す概念はどれか。","o":["密結合アーキテクチャ（Tight Coupling）","弾力性・回復力（Resilience）","固定キャパシティ（Fixed Capacity）","単一障害点（Single Point）"],"a":1,"e":"自己修復による稼働継続。需要急増への耐性。","qEn":"Which concept describes a system's ability to recover automatically from failures?","oEn":["Tightly coupled architecture","Resilience","Fixed capacity","Single point of failure"],"eEn":"Continued operation through self-healing; resistance to sudden surges in demand."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ステートレスなアプリ設計が水平スケールに適する理由はどれか。","o":["常に同一サーバーへ接続しセッションを保持する","どのインスタンスでも処理可能で状態を保持しない","セッション情報を各インスタンスに固定する","各サーバーがローカルに状態を保存する必要がある"],"a":1,"e":"セッション情報を外部へ分離。台数増減への柔軟な対応。","qEn":"Why is a stateless application design suited to horizontal scaling?","oEn":["It always connects to the same server and keeps the session","Any instance can handle requests and none holds state","It pins session information to each instance","Each server must store state locally"],"eEn":"Session information is separated out externally; flexible response to scaling the number of instances up or down."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"オンプレミスとクラウドを併用しない、共有インフラのみを使う形態はどれか。","o":["ハイブリッドクラウド","コミュニティクラウド","プライベートクラウド","パブリッククラウド環境"],"a":3,"e":"共有インフラを多数の利用者が使用。従量課金での提供。","qEn":"Which model uses only shared infrastructure, without combining on-premises and cloud?","oEn":["Hybrid cloud","Community cloud","Private cloud","Public cloud"],"eEn":"Shared infrastructure used by many customers; provided with pay-as-you-go pricing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"自社専有の環境のみで完結する運用形態はどれか。","o":["プライベートクラウド","パブリッククラウド","コミュニティクラウド","ハイブリッドクラウド"],"a":0,"e":"専有インフラによる完全な管理。高い統制と高コストの両面。","qEn":"Which operating model is completed entirely within an environment dedicated to the company?","oEn":["Private cloud","Public cloud","Community cloud","Hybrid cloud"],"eEn":"Full control over dedicated infrastructure; both high control and high cost."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウド移行で「ほぼそのまま移す」最小限の手法を表す7Rの1つはどれか。","o":["リホスト（リフト＆シフト）","リプラットフォーム（一部最適化）","リパーチェス（SaaSへ移行）","リファクタリング（作り替え）"],"a":0,"e":"アプリ変更なしの移設。最短での移行という選択。","qEn":"Which of the 7 Rs describes the minimal approach of moving to the cloud \"almost as is\"?","oEn":["Rehost (lift and shift)","Replatform (partial optimization)","Repurchase (move to SaaS)","Refactor (rebuild)"],"eEn":"Moving without changing the application; the choice of the fastest migration."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"移行せず廃止する判断を表す7Rの用語はどれか。","o":["リホスト","リロケート","リタイア","リテイン"],"a":2,"e":"リタイアは、不要な資産を移行せずに廃止する判断を指す7Rの用語である。リホストはそのまま移す、リロケートはハイパーバイザー単位で移す、リテインは当面オンプレミスに残す判断である。","qEn":"Which of the 7 Rs describes the decision to decommission instead of migrating?","oEn":["Rehost","Relocate","Retire","Retain"],"eEn":"Retire is the 7 Rs term for the decision to decommission unneeded assets rather than migrate them. Rehost moves them as is, Relocate moves them at the hypervisor level, and Retain is the decision to keep them on-premises for now."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"SaaS（Software as a Service）製品へ乗り換える7Rの手法はどれか。","o":["リパーチェス","リロケート","リアーキテクト","リファクタリング"],"a":0,"e":"自社運用から購入製品への切替。運用負担の削減。","qEn":"Which of the 7 Rs is the approach of switching to a SaaS (Software as a Service) product?","oEn":["Repurchase","Relocate","Rearchitect","Refactor"],"eEn":"Switching from self-operated systems to a purchased product; reduced operational burden."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Cloud Adoption Framework（CAF）が示すものはどれか。","o":["クラウドの5つの特性を定義する枠組み","Well-Architectedの6本の設計の柱","アプリ移行のための7つの戦略（7R）","組織のクラウド導入を支援する6つの観点"],"a":3,"e":"ビジネス・人材・ガバナンス・プラットフォーム・セキュリティ・オペレーション。","qEn":"What does the AWS (Amazon Web Services) Cloud Adoption Framework (CAF) present?","oEn":["A framework defining the five characteristics of the cloud","The six pillars of Well-Architected design","The seven strategies for migrating applications (7 Rs)","Six perspectives that support an organization's cloud adoption"],"eEn":"Business, People, Governance, Platform, Security, and Operations."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"メールやグループウェアのように完成品を利用する形態はどれか。","o":["SaaS","FaaS","IaaS","PaaS"],"a":0,"e":"アプリ全体をサービスとして利用。管理負担が最小。","qEn":"Which model uses a finished product, like email or groupware?","eEn":"Using the whole application as a service; minimal management burden."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"サーバー管理を意識せずコードを実行できるモデルの呼称はどれか。","o":["コンテナ化","サーバーレス","ハイパーバイザ","ベアメタル"],"a":1,"e":"インフラ運用をAWSが担当。実行時間に応じた課金。","qEn":"What is the name of the model in which you can run code without thinking about server management?","oEn":["Containerization","Serverless","Hypervisor","Bare metal"],"eEn":"AWS handles infrastructure operations; billed by execution time."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"フォールトトレランス（Fault Tolerance）が意味するものはどれか。","o":["障害後に手動で復旧する運用方式","処理速度を最優先で最大化する能力","障害発生時も機能を維持する耐障害性","単一障害点を意図的に集約する設計"],"a":2,"e":"予備系への自動切替。サービス無停止の追求。","qEn":"What does fault tolerance mean?","oEn":["An operating method of recovering manually after a failure occurs","The ability to maximize processing speed above all else","Resilience to failures that maintains functionality even when a failure occurs","A design that deliberately concentrates single points of failure"],"eEn":"Automatic switchover to a standby system; pursuing no service downtime."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"アジリティ（俊敏性）向上が事業にもたらす効果はどれか。","o":["市場投入までの時間短縮","実験の失敗コストの増加","資本的支出（CapEx）の増加","調達リードタイムの長期化"],"a":0,"e":"実験コストの低下。失敗の許容と高速な改善。","qEn":"What effect does improved agility have on the business?","oEn":["Shorter time to market","Higher cost of failed experiments","Increased capital expenditure (CapEx)","Longer procurement lead times"],"eEn":"Lower cost of experimentation; tolerance for failure and fast improvement."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"データセンターの物理的セキュリティを担う主体はどれか。","o":["AWS（責任共有モデルのクラウド側）","AWSパートナー（APN認定事業者）","お客様（ゲストOSとデータの管理者）","利用者（責任共有モデルのお客様側）"],"a":0,"e":"施設の警備と入退室管理。利用者の責任外。","qEn":"Who is responsible for the physical security of data centers?","oEn":["AWS (the cloud side of the shared responsibility model)","AWS Partners (APN-certified providers)","The customer (administrator of the guest OS and data)","The user (the customer side of the shared responsibility model)"],"eEn":"Facility security and entry and exit control; outside the customer's responsibility."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"オートスケーリングが解決する主な課題はどれか。","o":["データベースの自動バックアップ取得","需要変動への手動対応の排除","ストレージ容量の物理的な上限撤廃","アプリケーションコードの自動修正"],"a":1,"e":"負荷に応じた自動増減。過不足のないリソース確保。","qEn":"What main problem does Auto Scaling solve?","oEn":["Taking automatic database backups","Eliminating manual response to demand fluctuations","Removing the physical limit on storage capacity","Automatically fixing application code"],"eEn":"Automatic scaling in and out according to load; securing neither too few nor too many resources."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"複数AZ（Availability Zone）構成が主に高めるシステム特性はどれか。","o":["ストレージの保存単価の削減","データ転送の物理的な高速化","可用性（単一AZ障害への耐性）","リージョン間をまたぐ災害復旧の実現"],"a":2,"e":"片方の障害時にもう片方が継続。リージョン内での冗長化。","qEn":"Which system characteristic is mainly improved by a multi-AZ (Availability Zone) configuration?","oEn":["Lower storage unit price","Physically faster data transfer","Availability (tolerance to a single-AZ failure)","Disaster recovery across Regions"],"eEn":"If one fails, the other continues; redundancy within a Region."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"リージョン選択で考慮すべき主要な要素に含まれないものはどれか。","o":["サービスの提供状況","データ転送コスト","ネットワーク遅延","インスタンスの色"],"a":3,"e":"レイテンシー・コンプライアンス・サービス可用性・料金の4点が判断軸。","qEn":"Which of the following is NOT a key factor to consider when choosing a Region?","oEn":["Service availability","Data transfer cost","Network latency","The color of the instance"],"eEn":"Four decision criteria: latency, compliance, service availability, and pricing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"パフォーマンス効率の柱で重視される考え方はどれか。","o":["最新技術の民主化と適正リソースの選択","障害からの自動復旧と回復力の確保","コスト最適化のための支出の継続的な管理","常に最大スペックのリソースを確保する"],"a":0,"e":"サーバーレスなどの活用。コストと性能の両立。","qEn":"Which idea is emphasized in the Performance Efficiency pillar?","oEn":["Democratizing advanced technologies and choosing appropriate resources","Automatic recovery from failures and ensuring resilience","Continuously managing spending for cost optimization","Always securing resources at maximum specifications"],"eEn":"Use of serverless and similar approaches; balancing cost and performance."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの「不変インフラ（Immutable Infrastructure）」が防ぐ問題はどれか。","o":["データベースのクエリ性能低下","構成のばらつき（構成ドリフト）","デプロイ後のOSの脆弱性の発生","ストレージ容量の枯渇問題"],"a":1,"e":"不変インフラは、変更時にサーバーを作り直すため、構成のばらつき(構成ドリフト)を防ぐ。データベースのクエリ性能、OSの脆弱性の発生、ストレージ容量の枯渇は、それだけでは防げない。","qEn":"Which problem does cloud \"immutable infrastructure\" prevent?","oEn":["Degraded database query performance","Configuration variation (configuration drift)","OS vulnerabilities arising after deployment","Exhaustion of storage capacity"],"eEn":"Immutable infrastructure rebuilds servers when changes are made, which prevents configuration variation (configuration drift). Database query performance, OS vulnerabilities, and storage capacity exhaustion are not prevented by it alone."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"マイクロサービスアーキテクチャの利点はどれか。","o":["単一のコードベースへの密な結合","サービス単位での独立した開発・拡張","全機能を一括でまとめてデプロイする必要性","サービス間通信の複雑さの排除"],"a":1,"e":"マイクロサービスは、機能をサービスごとに分けて独立に開発・拡張でき、障害の影響も局所化できる。単一コードベースへの密な結合や全機能の一括デプロイは、モノリス型の特徴である。","qEn":"What is an advantage of microservices architecture?","oEn":["Tight coupling to a single codebase","Independent development and scaling by service","The need to deploy all functions together at once","Elimination of the complexity of communication between services"],"eEn":"Microservices split functionality into services that can be developed and scaled independently, and the impact of failures can also be localized. Tight coupling to a single codebase and deploying all functions together are characteristics of monolithic designs."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「キャパシティの予測が不要」になることの財務的効果はどれか。","o":["初期の設備投資（CapEx）の増加","使用量に依存しない固定料金化","長期契約による割引の必須化","過剰投資の回避による資金効率向上"],"a":3,"e":"キャパシティを予測する必要がなくなると、実際の需要に合わせて使えるため、過剰投資を避けて資金効率が上がる。初期のCapExは減り、固定料金や長期契約は必須でない。","qEn":"What is the financial effect of no longer needing to predict capacity?","oEn":["Higher upfront capital expenditure (CapEx)","Fixed pricing independent of usage","Mandatory discounts through long-term contracts","Better capital efficiency by avoiding overinvestment"],"eEn":"When you no longer need to predict capacity, you can use resources to match actual demand, which avoids overinvestment and improves capital efficiency. Upfront CapEx decreases, and fixed pricing and long-term contracts are not required."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"グローバル展開でレイテンシーを下げる基本方針はどれか。","o":["インスタンスのスペックを最大化する","すべての処理を単一リージョンに集約する","ユーザーに近いリージョン・エッジの利用","オンプレミスのデータセンターへ集中させる"],"a":2,"e":"ユーザーに近いリージョンやエッジを使えば、物理的な距離が縮まり、応答時間が短くなる。インスタンスのスペック最大化や単一リージョンへの集約、オンプレミスへの集中では距離の問題は解決しない。","qEn":"What is the basic approach to reducing latency in global deployments?","oEn":["Maximize instance specifications","Consolidate all processing in a single Region","Use Regions and edge locations close to users","Concentrate everything in on-premises data centers"],"eEn":"Using Regions and edge locations close to users reduces physical distance and shortens response times. Maximizing instance specifications, consolidating in a single Region, or concentrating in on-premises data centers does not solve the distance problem."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウド移行の「リロケート（Relocate）」が指すものはどれか。","o":["アプリを全面的に再設計しクラウドネイティブ化する手法","変更を加えず既存環境を維持し続ける手法","SaaS製品へ置き換えて再購入する手法","VMware環境などを再ホストせず移設する手法"],"a":3,"e":"ハイパーバイザー単位の移行。最小変更での移設。","qEn":"What does \"Relocate\" refer to in cloud migration?","oEn":["Redesigning the application entirely to make it cloud native","Keeping the existing environment as is without changes","Replacing it with a SaaS product and repurchasing","Moving VMware environments and the like without rehosting"],"eEn":"Migration at the hypervisor level; relocation with minimal changes."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） CAF（Cloud Adoption Framework）の「ピープルパースペクティブ」が扱う範囲はどれか。","o":["セキュリティとコンプライアンスの統制","人材・スキル・組織文化の変革","事業戦略と投資対効果の定義","ITインフラの構築と運用の自動化"],"a":1,"e":"トレーニングと役割定義。導入の人的側面。","qEn":"What does the \"People perspective\" of the AWS (Amazon Web Services) CAF (Cloud Adoption Framework) cover?","oEn":["Control of security and compliance","Transformation of people, skills, and organizational culture","Defining business strategy and return on investment","Building IT infrastructure and automating operations"],"eEn":"Training and role definition; the human side of adoption."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの「グローバルリーチ」が事業へもたらす機会はどれか。","o":["特定地域のみへのサービス限定","調達リードタイムの長期化","データセンターの自社建設","新市場への迅速な進出"],"a":3,"e":"グローバルリーチにより、各地へ低コストで素早く展開でき、新市場への迅速な進出が可能になる。特定地域のみへの限定やデータセンターの自社建設、調達リードタイムの長期化は、オンプレミス側の制約である。","qEn":"What opportunity does the cloud's \"global reach\" bring to the business?","oEn":["Limiting the service to specific regions only","Longer procurement lead times","Building your own data centers","Rapid entry into new markets"],"eEn":"Global reach lets you deploy quickly and at low cost in many places, enabling rapid entry into new markets. Limiting to specific regions, building your own data centers, and longer procurement lead times are constraints of on-premises environments."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service）のバケットへのアクセス制御を担う主体はどれか。","o":["監査人","利用者（顧客）","第三者","AWS"],"a":1,"e":"データとアクセス権の管理。設定責任は利用者。","qEn":"Who is responsible for controlling access to an S3 (Simple Storage Service) bucket?","oEn":["The auditor","The customer","A third party","AWS"],"eEn":"Managing data and access permissions; configuration is the customer's responsibility."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"個々の利用者を表すIAM（Identity and Access Management）のエンティティはどれか。","o":["ルートユーザー","IAMグループ","個別のIAMユーザー","IAMロール"],"a":2,"e":"恒久的な認証情報を保持。人や用途ごとに発行。","qEn":"Which IAM (Identity and Access Management) entity represents an individual user?","oEn":["Root user","IAM group","IAM user","IAM role"],"eEn":"Holds permanent credentials; issued per person or purpose."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"暗号鍵の評価で許可がない場合のIAM（Identity and Access Management）の既定動作はどれか。","o":["既定で全リソースへのアクセスを許可","暗黙的な拒否（Implicit Deny）","明示的な許可（Explicit Allow）","評価をスキップし管理者へ承認を要求"],"a":1,"e":"IAMでは、許可の記述がなければ暗黙的な拒否(Implicit Deny)が既定で働く。既定で全リソースへのアクセスを許可することはなく、評価をスキップして管理者の承認を求める動作もない。","qEn":"When no permission is granted in an evaluation, what is the default behavior of IAM (Identity and Access Management)?","oEn":["Allow access to all resources by default","Implicit deny","Explicit allow","Skip evaluation and ask an administrator for approval"],"eEn":"In IAM, if there is no allow statement, an implicit deny applies by default. It does not allow access to all resources by default, nor does it skip evaluation and ask an administrator for approval."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"専有ハードウェアで鍵を管理するコンプライアンス向けサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS KMS（共有型）","AWS CloudHSM","Amazon Inspector","Amazon Cognito"],"a":1,"e":"FIPS準拠の専有HSM。厳格な鍵管理。","qEn":"Which compliance-oriented service manages keys on dedicated hardware?","oEn":["AWS KMS (shared)","AWS CloudHSM","Amazon Inspector","Amazon Cognito"],"eEn":"A dedicated HSM that is FIPS compliant; strict key management."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティアラートを集約しダッシュボード化するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CloudTrail","AWS Security Hub","Amazon Inspector","Amazon GuardDuty"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Security Hubは、複数サービスのセキュリティアラートを集約し、ダッシュボードで横断的に見せる。CloudTrailは操作の記録、Inspectorは脆弱性の診断、GuardDutyは脅威の検知で、集約の役ではない。","qEn":"Which service aggregates security alerts and presents them in a dashboard?","eEn":"AWS Security Hub aggregates security alerts from multiple services and shows them across services in a dashboard. CloudTrail records operations, Inspector assesses vulnerabilities, and GuardDuty detects threats; none of them is for aggregation."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"保管中データ（at rest）の暗号化として正しいものはどれか。","o":["TLSによるHTTPS通信の保護","ネットワークを流れる転送中データの暗号化","VPN経由の拠点間通信の保護","S3やEBSに保存されたデータの暗号化"],"a":3,"e":"保管中データの暗号化は、S3やEBSなどストレージに保存したデータを暗号化することで、KMSの鍵を使う。TLSによるHTTPS通信、転送中データ、VPN経由の拠点間通信の保護は、通信路側の対策である。","qEn":"Which of the following correctly describes encryption of data at rest?","oEn":["Protection of HTTPS communication with TLS","Encryption of data in transit over the network","Protection of site-to-site communication over VPN","Encryption of data stored in S3 or EBS"],"eEn":"Encrypting data at rest means encrypting data stored in storage such as S3 and EBS, using KMS keys. HTTPS with TLS, data in transit, and site-to-site communication over VPN are all measures for the communication path."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ユーザー認証情報を一元管理しアプリへサインイン機能を提供するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Single Sign-On","Amazon Cognito","AWS Secrets Manager","Login with Amazon"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon Cognitoは、ユーザー認証情報を管理し、アプリにサインアップやサインインの機能を提供する。AWS Secrets Managerは秘密情報の保管で、Login with Amazonは外部のIDプロバイダー、AWS Single Sign-Onは社内向けのSSOである。","qEn":"Which service centrally manages user credentials and provides sign-in functionality to applications?","eEn":"Amazon Cognito manages user credentials and provides sign-up and sign-in functionality to applications. AWS Secrets Manager stores secrets, Login with Amazon is an external identity provider, and AWS Single Sign-On is an SSO for internal use."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"複数アカウントへ一時的・安全にサインインを集約する仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Directory Service","AWS Organizations と SCP","Amazon Cognito ユーザープール","AWS IAM Identity Center（旧SSO）"],"a":3,"e":"シングルサインオンの提供。一元的なアクセス管理。","qEn":"Which mechanism consolidates temporary, secure sign-in across multiple accounts?","oEn":["AWS Directory Service","AWS Organizations and SCPs","Amazon Cognito user pools","AWS IAM Identity Center"],"eEn":"Provides single sign-on; centralized access management."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"アクセスキー漏洩リスクを下げるためEC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）に推奨される方式はどれか。","o":["IAMロールの割り当て","ルートユーザーのキー共有","アクセスキーの環境変数への設定","認証情報をコードに直接記述"],"a":0,"e":"EC2にはIAMロールを割り当てると、長期のアクセスキーを使わずに一時認証情報で動ける。コードへの認証情報の直接記述や環境変数への設定、ルートユーザーのキー共有は漏洩リスクが高い。","qEn":"Which method is recommended for EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) to reduce the risk of access key leakage?","oEn":["Assigning an IAM role","Sharing the root user's keys","Setting access keys in environment variables","Writing credentials directly in code"],"eEn":"Assigning an IAM role to EC2 lets it operate with temporary credentials without long-term access keys. Writing credentials directly in code, setting them in environment variables, or sharing the root user's keys carries a high risk of leakage."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のコンプライアンスプログラム準拠状況を確認する手段はどれか。","o":["Amazon CloudWatchのメトリクス確認","AWS Artifactでの報告書取得","AWS Trusted Advisorの推奨事項","AWS Cost Explorerの費用分析"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Artifactで、AWSのコンプライアンスプログラムに関する第三者監査の報告書を入手し、準拠状況を確認できる。CloudWatchのメトリクス、Trusted Advisorの推奨事項、Cost Explorerの費用分析は準拠の確認手段ではない。","qEn":"Which method is used to check AWS (Amazon Web Services) compliance program conformance?","oEn":["Checking Amazon CloudWatch metrics","Obtaining reports from AWS Artifact","Recommendations from AWS Trusted Advisor","Cost analysis in AWS Cost Explorer"],"eEn":"With AWS Artifact, you can obtain third-party audit reports on AWS compliance programs and check conformance. CloudWatch metrics, Trusted Advisor recommendations, and Cost Explorer cost analysis are not ways to check conformance."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ログの改ざん検知や保全に役立つCloudTrailの機能はどれか。","o":["課金データの月次集計","自動的なスケールアウト","リアルタイム描画","ログファイルの整合性検証"],"a":3,"e":"CloudTrailのログファイルの整合性検証は、ログが改ざんされていないかを検出する機能で、証跡の信頼性を保つ。課金データの月次集計、自動的なスケールアウト、リアルタイムのグラフ描画は別のサービスの役割である。","qEn":"Which CloudTrail feature helps detect tampering with logs and preserve them?","oEn":["Monthly aggregation of billing data","Automatic scale-out","Real-time graph rendering","Log file integrity validation"],"eEn":"CloudTrail log file integrity validation detects whether logs have been tampered with and preserves the trustworthiness of the trail. Monthly aggregation of billing data, automatic scale-out, and real-time graph rendering are roles of other services."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティインシデント調査を支援するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Inspector","AWS Shield Advanced","Amazon Detective","Amazon Macie"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon Detectiveは、関連するログを自動で分析し、セキュリティインシデントの原因を可視化して調査を助ける。Inspectorは脆弱性の診断、Shield Advancedは高度なDDoS防御、Macieは機密データの検出である。","qEn":"Which service supports security incident investigation?","eEn":"Amazon Detective automatically analyzes related logs, visualizes the cause of a security incident, and helps with the investigation. Inspector assesses vulnerabilities, Shield Advanced provides advanced DDoS protection, and Macie detects sensitive data."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ファイアウォールルールを複数アカウントで一元管理するサービスはどれか。","o":["セキュリティグループの一括編集","AWS Firewall Manager","AWS WAF を各アカウントで個別に設定する","ネットワークACLをサブネット毎に設定"],"a":1,"e":"複数アカウントへの一括適用。一貫したポリシー。","qEn":"Which service centrally manages firewall rules across multiple accounts?","oEn":["Bulk editing of security groups","AWS Firewall Manager","Configuring AWS WAF individually in each account","Configuring network ACLs for each subnet"],"eEn":"Applies rules to multiple accounts at once; consistent policy."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）へ安全に接続しSSH（Secure Shell）鍵管理を不要にする仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Systems Manager Session Manager","AWS Client VPN を用いたトンネル経由の接続","AWS Direct Connect による専用線接続","踏み台（Bastion）ホストを経由した SSH 鍵ペアでのログイン接続"],"a":0,"e":"ポート開放不要の接続。監査可能なアクセス。","qEn":"Which mechanism lets you connect securely to EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) without managing SSH (Secure Shell) keys?","oEn":["AWS Systems Manager Session Manager","Connection through a tunnel using AWS Client VPN","Dedicated line connection through AWS Direct Connect","Login with an SSH key pair through a bastion host"],"eEn":"Connection without opening ports; auditable access."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティグループの「ステートフル」が意味するものはどれか。","o":["往復それぞれにルールが必要","通信の状態を保持しない","戻りトラフィックの自動的な許可","拒否ルールのみを設定できる"],"a":2,"e":"セキュリティグループはステートフルで、往路の通信を許可すれば戻りのトラフィックも自動で許可される。往復それぞれにルールが必要なのはステートレスなNACLで、拒否ルールだけを設定できるわけでもない。","qEn":"What does \"stateful\" mean for a security group?","oEn":["Rules are needed for each direction of a round trip","It does not keep the state of communications","Return traffic is automatically allowed","Only deny rules can be set"],"eEn":"Security groups are stateful: if you allow outbound-direction traffic, the return traffic is automatically allowed as well. Needing rules for each direction is characteristic of the stateless NACL, and it is not true that only deny rules can be set."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"NACL（Network Access Control List）の「ステートレス」が意味するものはどれか。","o":["インスタンス単位で適用される","往復それぞれにルールが必要","許可ルールのみ設定できる","戻りトラフィックが自動的に許可される"],"a":1,"e":"NACLはステートレスで、戻りの通信も別に許可しなければならないため、往復それぞれにルールが必要になる。戻りトラフィックが自動で許可されるのはセキュリティグループで、NACLはサブネット単位に適用される。","qEn":"What does \"stateless\" mean for a NACL (Network Access Control List)?","oEn":["It is applied at the instance level","Rules are needed for each direction of a round trip","Only allow rules can be set","Return traffic is automatically allowed"],"eEn":"A NACL is stateless, and return traffic must be allowed separately, so rules are needed for each direction of a round trip. Automatic allowing of return traffic is how security groups work, and a NACL is applied at the subnet level."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"IAM（Identity and Access Management） Access Analyzerが検出するものはどれか。","o":["外部へ公開された意図しないアクセス権","ストレージの空き容量の逼迫状況","各リソースのCPUおよびメモリの使用率","毎月の利用料金の予算超過状況"],"a":0,"e":"IAM Access Analyzerは、外部へ公開された意図しないアクセス権を検出し、過剰な共有を見つける。ストレージの空き容量、CPUとメモリの使用率、毎月の予算超過は、別のモニタリングの対象である。","qEn":"What does IAM (Identity and Access Management) Access Analyzer detect?","oEn":["Unintended access permissions exposed externally","Tight free storage space","CPU and memory utilization of each resource","Monthly usage charges exceeding the budget"],"eEn":"IAM Access Analyzer detects unintended access permissions exposed externally and finds excessive sharing. Free storage space, CPU and memory utilization, and monthly budget overruns are subjects of other monitoring."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"クラウドにおける「ゼロトラスト」の基本方針はどれか。","o":["境界防御のみでリスクを排除する","すべてのアクセスを検証し暗黙の信頼を排除","一度の認証で以降は再検証しない","社内からのアクセスは信頼し検証を省略する"],"a":1,"e":"ゼロトラストは、すべてのアクセスを検証し、暗黙の信頼を置かない方針である。境界防御のみに頼る、一度の認証で再検証しない、社内からのアクセスを信頼するといった考え方は、ゼロトラストと逆である。","qEn":"Which of the following is the basic principle of \"zero trust\" in the cloud?","oEn":["Eliminate risk through perimeter defense alone","Verify every access and eliminate implicit trust","Authenticate once and never re-verify afterward","Trust access from inside the company and skip verification"],"eEn":"Zero trust is an approach that verifies every access and places no implicit trust. Relying on perimeter defense alone, not re-verifying after a single authentication, and trusting access from inside the company are the opposite of zero trust."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Amazon Macieが主に対象とするデータストアはどれか。","o":["S3","RDS","EBS","EFS"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon Macieは、主にS3に保存されたデータから機密情報を検出して分類し、アラートを出す。RDS、EBS、EFSといったほかのデータストアは、Macieの主な対象ではない。","qEn":"Which data store does Amazon Macie primarily target?","eEn":"Amazon Macie detects and classifies sensitive information in data stored mainly in S3 and raises alerts. Other data stores such as RDS, EBS, and EFS are not Macie's main targets."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"CIAの「認可された者のみアクセス可」に対応するものはどれか。","o":["真正性（Authenticity）","完全性（Integrity）によるデータ保護","可用性（Availability）","機密性（Confidentiality）"],"a":3,"e":"CIAの機密性(Confidentiality)は、認可された者だけがアクセスできることを指し、暗号化と権限制御で守る。完全性は改ざんされないこと、可用性は必要なときに使えること、真正性は本物であることである。","qEn":"Which CIA element corresponds to \"only authorized parties can access\"?","oEn":["Authenticity","Data protection through Integrity","Availability","Confidentiality"],"eEn":"In CIA, Confidentiality means that only authorized parties can access the data, and it is protected with encryption and access control. Integrity means data is not tampered with, Availability means it can be used when needed, and Authenticity means it is genuine."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"CIAの「必要なときに利用可能」に対応するものはどれか。","o":["完全性（Integrity）","機密性（Confidentiality）","可用性（Availability）","責任追跡性（Accountability）"],"a":2,"e":"CIAの可用性(Availability)は、必要なときにシステムを使えることで、冗長化などで守る。機密性は認可された者だけが見られること、完全性は改ざんされないこと、責任追跡性は誰が行ったかを追えることである。","qEn":"Which CIA element corresponds to \"available when needed\"?","oEn":["Integrity","Confidentiality","Availability","Accountability"],"eEn":"In CIA, Availability means the system can be used when needed, and it is protected through measures such as redundancy. Confidentiality means only authorized parties can view the data, Integrity means it is not tampered with, and Accountability means being able to trace who performed an action."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"VPC（Virtual Private Cloud）内のリソースをインターネットから隔離する基本構成はどれか。","o":["インターネットゲートウェイへの接続","プライベートサブネットへの配置","パブリックサブネットへの配置","Elastic IPアドレスの割り当て"],"a":1,"e":"直接到達の遮断。NAT経由の外向き通信。","qEn":"Which is the basic configuration for isolating resources in a VPC (Virtual Private Cloud) from the internet?","oEn":["Connection to an internet gateway","Placement in a private subnet","Placement in a public subnet","Assignment of an Elastic IP address"],"eEn":"Blocks direct reachability. Outbound communication goes through NAT."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のセキュリティで「予防的統制」に該当するものはどれか。","o":["インシデント発生後のフォレンジック分析と復旧","GuardDutyによる脅威の継続的な検知","IAMポリシーやセキュリティグループによるアクセス制限","CloudTrailによる全APIコールの継続的な記録"],"a":2,"e":"予防的統制は、問題が起きる前に防ぐもので、IAMポリシーやセキュリティグループによるアクセス制限が当たる。GuardDutyの検知とCloudTrailの記録は発見的統制、フォレンジックと復旧は事後の対応である。","qEn":"Which of the following is a \"preventive control\" in AWS (Amazon Web Services) security?","oEn":["Forensic analysis and recovery after an incident occurs","Continuous threat detection by GuardDuty","Access restrictions by IAM policies and security groups","Continuous recording of all API calls by CloudTrail"],"eEn":"Preventive controls stop problems before they occur, and access restrictions by IAM policies and security groups are an example. Detection by GuardDuty and recording by CloudTrail are detective controls, and forensics and recovery are responses after the fact."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のセキュリティで「発見的統制」に該当するものはどれか。","o":["IAMポリシーとセキュリティグループによる事前のアクセス制限","セキュリティグループでの通信の事前許可設定","CloudTrailやGuardDutyによる検知・記録","保管中および転送中のデータに対する暗号化の適用"],"a":2,"e":"発見的統制は、問題を事後に検出して可視化するもので、CloudTrailやGuardDutyによる検知・記録が当たる。IAMポリシーやセキュリティグループによる事前の制限と、暗号化の適用は、予防的統制である。","qEn":"Which of the following is a \"detective control\" in AWS (Amazon Web Services) security?","oEn":["Advance access restrictions by IAM policies and security groups","Advance permission of traffic in security groups","Detection and recording by CloudTrail and GuardDuty","Applying encryption to data at rest and in transit"],"eEn":"Detective controls detect problems after the fact and make them visible, and detection and recording by CloudTrail and GuardDuty are examples. Advance restrictions by IAM policies and security groups, and applying encryption, are preventive controls."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"クロスアカウントアクセスを安全に実現する仕組みはどれか。","o":["各アカウントに恒久的なアクセスキーを発行して共有する","IAMロールの引き受け（AssumeRole）","IAMユーザーのパスワードの共有設定","ルートユーザーの認証情報の使い回し"],"a":1,"e":"クロスアカウントアクセスは、IAMロールの引き受け(AssumeRole)で、一時的な認証情報を使って安全に実現する。恒久的なアクセスキーの共有、パスワードの共有、ルートユーザーの使い回しは、漏洩の危険が高い。","qEn":"Which mechanism enables cross-account access securely?","oEn":["Issuing and sharing permanent access keys in each account","Assuming an IAM role (AssumeRole)","Sharing the password of an IAM user","Reusing root user credentials"],"eEn":"Cross-account access is achieved securely by assuming an IAM role (AssumeRole), using temporary credentials. Sharing permanent access keys, sharing passwords, and reusing root user credentials carry a high risk of leakage."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） KMS（Key Management Service）の「カスタマー管理キー（CMK）」が提供する制御はどれか。","o":["鍵ポリシーとローテーションの利用者管理","物理HSMを占有した鍵の保管のみ","鍵素材の生成をAWSに完全に委任する運用","証明書の発行と自動更新の管理"],"a":0,"e":"KMSのカスタマー管理キー(CMK)では、利用者が鍵ポリシーやローテーションを管理でき、きめ細かく統制できる。物理HSMの占有はCloudHSM、証明書の発行と更新はACMの役割で、AWSへの完全な委任ではない。","qEn":"Which control does a \"customer managed key (CMK)\" in AWS (Amazon Web Services) KMS (Key Management Service) provide?","oEn":["Customer management of key policies and rotation","Key storage only, on dedicated physical HSMs","Operation in which AWS is fully delegated key material generation","Management of certificate issuance and automatic renewal"],"eEn":"With a KMS customer managed key (CMK), customers can manage key policies and rotation themselves, which allows fine-grained control. Dedicated physical HSMs are the role of CloudHSM, and certificate issuance and renewal are the role of ACM; it is not full delegation to AWS."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の監査証跡を全リージョン横断で収集する設定はどれか。","o":["AWS Configのマルチリージョン集約","CloudTrailの単一リージョン証跡","CloudWatch Logsのメトリクスフィルタ","CloudTrailのマルチリージョン証跡"],"a":3,"e":"CloudTrailのマルチリージョン証跡は、全リージョンの操作をまとめて記録し、網羅的な監査を可能にする。単一リージョンの証跡は他リージョンを見逃し、Configの集約やメトリクスフィルタは監査証跡の収集ではない。","qEn":"Which setting collects AWS (Amazon Web Services) audit trails across all Regions?","oEn":["Multi-Region aggregation in AWS Config","A single-Region trail in CloudTrail","A metric filter in CloudWatch Logs","A multi-Region trail in CloudTrail"],"eEn":"A CloudTrail multi-Region trail records operations in all Regions together, enabling comprehensive auditing. A single-Region trail misses other Regions, and Config aggregation and metric filters do not collect audit trails."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"「責任共有モデルの理解不足」が招く典型的事故はどれか。","o":["S3の誤った公開設定によるデータ漏洩","セキュリティグループの全開放による不正アクセス","IAM認証情報のハードコードによる流出","EC2のOSパッチ適用漏れによる侵害"],"a":0,"e":"利用者責任の見落とし。設定確認の重要性。","qEn":"Which is a typical incident caused by \"a poor understanding of the shared responsibility model\"?","oEn":["Data leakage caused by an incorrect S3 public-access setting","Unauthorized access caused by fully opening a security group","Credential leakage caused by hard-coding IAM credentials","A breach caused by missed OS patching on EC2"],"eEn":"Overlooking the customer's responsibility. The importance of checking settings."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"暗号鍵の自動ローテーションが低減するリスクはどれか。","o":["長期間同一鍵による侵害リスク","アクセスキーの漏洩による不正利用","証明書の期限切れによる通信断","鍵の紛失によるデータ復号不能"],"a":0,"e":"鍵の自動ローテーションは、長期間同じ鍵を使い続けることによる侵害リスクを減らす。アクセスキーの漏洩、証明書の期限切れ、鍵の紛失は、別の対策で扱うリスクである。","qEn":"Which risk does automatic rotation of encryption keys reduce?","oEn":["The risk of compromise from using the same key for a long time","Unauthorized use caused by leaked access keys","Communication outages caused by expired certificates","Inability to decrypt data caused by lost keys"],"eEn":"Automatic key rotation reduces the risk of compromise from using the same key for a long time. Leaked access keys, expired certificates, and lost keys are risks handled by other measures."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"多層防御（Defense in Depth）の考え方に合致するものはどれか。","o":["複数のセキュリティ層の組み合わせ","単一のファイアウォールのみで守る構成","認証を一箇所に集約する構成","境界防御のみへの集中投資"],"a":0,"e":"多層防御は、複数のセキュリティ層を組み合わせ、1つが破られても守る考え方である。単一のファイアウォールのみ、境界防御のみへの集中投資、認証を一箇所に集約する構成は、単一の対策に頼っている。","qEn":"Which matches the concept of defense in depth?","oEn":["A combination of multiple security layers","A configuration protected by a single firewall only","A configuration that consolidates authentication in one place","Concentrating investment on perimeter defense only"],"eEn":"Defense in depth is the approach of combining multiple security layers so that protection holds even if one is breached. A single firewall only, investment concentrated on perimeter defense only, and consolidating authentication in one place all rely on a single measure."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"コードをアップロードするだけで実行環境を自動構築するPaaS（Platform as a Service）的サービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Elastic Beanstalk","Amazon Lightsail コンテナ","AWS CloudFormation","Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling"],"a":0,"e":"環境構築の自動化。基盤を意識しない展開。","qEn":"Which PaaS (Platform as a Service)-like service automatically builds the runtime environment when you just upload your code?","oEn":["AWS Elastic Beanstalk","Amazon Lightsail containers","AWS CloudFormation","Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling"],"eEn":"Automates environment setup. Deployment without having to think about the underlying infrastructure."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"小規模Webサイトを簡易・定額で立ち上げるサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon EC2 オンデマンド","Amazon Lightsail","AWS Elastic Beanstalk","Amazon S3 静的ホスティング"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon Lightsailは、小規模なWebサイトを定額料金で簡単に立ち上げられるサービスである。EC2のオンデマンドは従量課金、Elastic Beanstalkはアプリの自動展開、S3の静的ホスティングはサーバーなしの配信である。","qEn":"Which service lets you launch a small website simply at a flat rate?","oEn":["Amazon EC2 On-Demand","Amazon Lightsail","AWS Elastic Beanstalk","Amazon S3 static hosting"],"eEn":"Amazon Lightsail is a service that lets you easily launch a small website at a flat rate. EC2 On-Demand is pay-as-you-go, Elastic Beanstalk automatically deploys applications, and S3 static hosting delivers content without servers."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Dockerコンテナのオーケストレーションを行うAWS（Amazon Web Services）独自サービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon ECR","AWS Fargate","Amazon ECS","Amazon EKS"],"a":2,"e":"コンテナの配置・管理。スケールの自動化。","qEn":"Which AWS (Amazon Web Services) proprietary service orchestrates Docker containers?","eEn":"Container placement and management. Automated scaling."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"オンプレミスとS3（Simple Storage Service）を連携させるハイブリッドストレージはどれか。","o":["AWS DataSync 転送サービス","Amazon FSx ファイルシステム","AWS Snowball Edge","AWS Storage Gateway（ハイブリッド）"],"a":3,"e":"既存環境とクラウドの橋渡し。段階的なデータ移行。","qEn":"Which hybrid storage service connects on-premises environments with S3 (Simple Storage Service)?","oEn":["AWS DataSync transfer service","Amazon FSx file system","AWS Snowball Edge","AWS Storage Gateway"],"eEn":"Bridges existing environments and the cloud. Gradual data migration."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service）のオブジェクトを自動的に階層移動・削除するルールはどれか。","o":["S3レプリケーション設定","S3ライフサイクルポリシー","S3バケットポリシー","S3 Storage Lens分析"],"a":1,"e":"アクセス頻度に応じた最適化。保管コストの削減。","qEn":"Which rule automatically transitions or deletes S3 (Simple Storage Service) objects between tiers?","oEn":["S3 replication configuration","S3 Lifecycle policy","S3 bucket policy","S3 Storage Lens analysis"],"eEn":"Optimization based on access frequency. Reduced storage costs."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"RDS（Relational Database Service）の読み取り負荷を分散する仕組みはどれか。","o":["フェイルオーバー","スケールアップ","マルチAZ配置","リードレプリカ"],"a":3,"e":"リードレプリカは、RDSの読み取り専用の複製を作り、参照クエリを分散して読み取り性能を高める。マルチAZ配置とフェイルオーバーは可用性の向上で、スケールアップは1台の性能を上げる方法である。","qEn":"Which mechanism distributes the read load of RDS (Relational Database Service)?","oEn":["Failover","Scale up","Multi-AZ deployment","Read replica"],"eEn":"A read replica creates a read-only copy of an RDS database and distributes read queries to improve read performance. Multi-AZ deployment and failover improve availability, and scaling up is a way to increase the performance of a single instance."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"イベント駆動でサービスを連携させるイベントバスはどれか。","o":["Amazon SNS トピック","Amazon EventBridge","Amazon SQS キュー","AWS Step Functions"],"a":1,"e":"イベントのルーティング。サービス間の自動連携。","qEn":"Which event bus connects services in an event-driven way?","oEn":["Amazon SNS topic","Amazon EventBridge","Amazon SQS queue","AWS Step Functions"],"eEn":"Event routing. Automatic integration between services."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"複数ステップの処理をワークフローとして調整するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Step Functions","Amazon SNS 通知配信","Amazon EventBridge","Amazon SQS キュー"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Step Functionsは、複数ステップの処理をワークフローとして調整し、処理フローを可視化する。SQSキューは非同期のメッセージ保管、SNS通知配信は通知の送信、EventBridgeはイベントの振り分けである。","qEn":"Which service coordinates multi-step processing as a workflow?","oEn":["AWS Step Functions","Amazon SNS notification delivery","Amazon EventBridge","Amazon SQS queue"],"eEn":"AWS Step Functions coordinates multi-step processing as a workflow and visualizes the processing flow. An SQS queue stores messages asynchronously, SNS notification delivery sends notifications, and EventBridge routes events."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ストリーミングデータをリアルタイムで収集・処理するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Athena","Amazon Kinesis","Amazon Redshift","AWS Glue ETL"],"a":1,"e":"リアルタイムデータ処理。継続的な取り込み。","qEn":"Which service collects and processes streaming data in real time?","eEn":"Real-time data processing. Continuous ingestion."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データの抽出・変換・ロード（ETL）をサーバーレスで行うサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Glue","AWS Lambda","Amazon EMR","AWS Batch"],"a":0,"e":"ETL処理の自動化。データカタログの管理。","qEn":"Which service performs data extraction, transformation, and loading (ETL) in a serverless way?","eEn":"Automated ETL processing. Data catalog management."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データを可視化しダッシュボード化するBI（Business Intelligence）サービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Managed Grafana","Amazon QuickSight","Amazon Athena","Amazon Redshift"],"a":1,"e":"ビジネスインテリジェンスの提供。分析結果の共有。（2026年11月時点：Amazon QuickSight は Amazon Quick に発展し、BI機能は Amazon Quick Sight として Quick の一機能になった。さらに2026年11月9日に AWS Quick・AWS Quick Sight へ改称された。公式試験ガイド v1.3 の出題範囲リストは Amazon Quick のまま。再確認のうえ引用すること）","qEn":"Which BI (Business Intelligence) service visualizes data and builds dashboards?","eEn":"Provides business intelligence. Sharing of analysis results. (As of November 2026: Amazon QuickSight has evolved into Amazon Quick, and its BI capability continues as Amazon Quick Sight, a feature within Quick; on November 9, 2026 they were renamed AWS Quick and AWS Quick Sight. The in-scope list of exam guide v1.3 still names Amazon Quick. Verify before citing.)"},
  {"d":"D3","q":"テキストを自然な音声へ変換するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Lex","Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Polly","Amazon Translate"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon Pollyは、テキストを自然な音声に変換する音声合成サービスである。Lexは対話ボット、Transcribeは音声からテキストへの変換、Translateはテキストの言語間翻訳である。","qEn":"Which service converts text into natural-sounding speech?","eEn":"Amazon Polly is a speech synthesis service that converts text into natural-sounding speech. Lex is for conversational bots, Transcribe converts speech to text, and Translate translates text between languages."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"音声をテキストへ変換するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Translate","Amazon Polly 音声合成"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon Transcribeは、音声をテキストに変換する音声認識サービスで、文字起こしを自動化する。Comprehendは文章の分析、Translateは言語間の翻訳、Pollyの音声合成は逆に文字を音声にする。","qEn":"Which service converts speech into text?","oEn":["Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Translate","Amazon Polly speech synthesis"],"eEn":"Amazon Transcribe is a speech recognition service that converts speech into text and automates transcription. Comprehend analyzes text, Translate translates between languages, and Polly's speech synthesis does the reverse by turning text into speech."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"テキストの言語間翻訳を行うサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Transcribe","Amazon Polly","Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Translate"],"a":3,"e":"Amazon Translateは、テキストを言語間で機械翻訳するサービスで、多言語化を支援する。Transcribeは音声の文字起こし、Pollyは音声合成、Comprehendは感情やキーフレーズの抽出である。","qEn":"Which service translates text between languages?","eEn":"Amazon Translate is a service that machine-translates text between languages and supports multilingual content. Transcribe transcribes speech, Polly synthesizes speech, and Comprehend extracts sentiment and key phrases."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"テキストから感情やキーフレーズを抽出する自然言語処理サービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Rekognition","Amazon Textract","Amazon Translate"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon Comprehendは、テキストから感情やキーフレーズなどを抽出する自然言語処理サービスである。Rekognitionは画像と動画の分析、Textractは文書の文字抽出、Translateは言語間の翻訳である。","qEn":"Which natural language processing service extracts sentiment and key phrases from text?","eEn":"Amazon Comprehend is a natural language processing service that extracts sentiment, key phrases, and more from text. Rekognition analyzes images and videos, Textract extracts text from documents, and Translate translates between languages."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）を操作するGUIを提供するものはどれか。","o":["AWS SDK for Python","AWS CloudShell ターミナル","AWS Management Console","AWS Command Line Interface"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Management Consoleは、ブラウザ上でAWSを視覚的に操作できるGUIである。AWS SDK for Pythonはコードから、AWS CLIはコマンドから、CloudShellはブラウザ上のターミナルから操作する手段である。","qEn":"Which provides a GUI for operating AWS (Amazon Web Services)?","oEn":["AWS SDK for Python","AWS CloudShell terminal","AWS Management Console","AWS Command Line Interface"],"eEn":"The AWS Management Console is a GUI for operating AWS visually in a browser. The AWS SDK for Python operates AWS from code, the AWS CLI from commands, and CloudShell from a terminal in the browser."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"プログラムからAWS（Amazon Web Services）を操作するための手段はどれか。","o":["AWS CDK","AWS CLI","REST API","AWS SDK"],"a":3,"e":"各言語からのAPI呼び出し。アプリ統合。","qEn":"What means can be used to operate AWS (Amazon Web Services) programmatically?","eEn":"API calls from each programming language. Application integration."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"複数アカウントを安全なベースラインで一括構築するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Control Tower","AWS Config ルール","AWS Organizations 単体","AWS CloudFormation"],"a":0,"e":"ガードレール付きの環境整備。ガバナンスの確立。","qEn":"Which service sets up multiple accounts at once with a secure baseline?","oEn":["AWS Control Tower","AWS Config rules","AWS Organizations alone","AWS CloudFormation"],"eEn":"Environment setup with guardrails. Establishing governance."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"承認済みのIT製品を社内へ提供するカタログサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Service Catalog","AWS Marketplace","AWS Systems Manager","AWS Control Tower"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Service Catalogは、組織が承認したIT製品をカタログ化し、利用者へ標準化して配布する。AWS Marketplaceはサードパーティ製品の購入、Systems Managerは運用管理、Control Towerはマルチアカウントの統制である。","qEn":"Which catalog service provides approved IT products within the organization?","eEn":"AWS Service Catalog catalogs IT products approved by the organization and distributes them to users in a standardized way. AWS Marketplace is for purchasing third-party products, Systems Manager is for operations management, and Control Tower is for multi-account governance."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"グラフ型データに特化したデータベースはどれか。","o":["Amazon DocumentDB","Amazon Redshift","Amazon Neptune","Amazon DynamoDB"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon Neptuneは、関係性の高速な探索に向くグラフモデルに特化したデータベースである。DocumentDBはドキュメント型、Redshiftはデータウェアハウス、DynamoDBはキー値型のNoSQLである。","qEn":"Which database specializes in graph-type data?","eEn":"Amazon Neptune is a database specialized in the graph model, which is suited to fast traversal of relationships. DocumentDB is a document database, Redshift is a data warehouse, and DynamoDB is a key-value NoSQL database."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"MongoDB互換のドキュメントデータベースはどれか。","o":["Amazon Keyspaces","Amazon DocumentDB","Amazon DynamoDB テーブル","Amazon Neptune"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon DocumentDBは、MongoDB互換でJSON文書を管理するマネージドなドキュメントDBである。KeyspacesはCassandra互換、DynamoDBテーブルはキー値型、Neptuneはグラフ型のデータベースである。","qEn":"Which is a MongoDB-compatible document database?","oEn":["Amazon Keyspaces","Amazon DocumentDB","Amazon DynamoDB table","Amazon Neptune"],"eEn":"Amazon DocumentDB is a managed document database that is MongoDB-compatible and manages JSON documents. Keyspaces is Cassandra-compatible, a DynamoDB table is key-value, and Neptune is a graph database."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"大規模なビッグデータ処理基盤（Hadoop/Spark）を提供するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Athena","Amazon EMR","AWS Glue","Amazon Kinesis"],"a":1,"e":"分散処理のマネージド化。大量データ分析。","qEn":"Which service provides a large-scale big data processing platform (Hadoop/Spark)?","eEn":"Managed distributed processing. Analysis of large volumes of data."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ビルドからデプロイまでのパイプラインを統合するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CodePipeline","AWS CodeCommit","AWS CodeDeploy","AWS CodeBuild ビルド"],"a":0,"e":"AWS CodePipelineは、ビルドからテスト、デプロイまでのパイプラインを統合して自動化するCI/CDサービスである。CodeCommitはソースの保管、CodeBuildはビルド、CodeDeployはデプロイを担う個別の部品である。","qEn":"Which service integrates the pipeline from build to deployment?","oEn":["AWS CodePipeline","AWS CodeCommit","AWS CodeDeploy","AWS CodeBuild build"],"eEn":"AWS CodePipeline is a CI/CD service that integrates and automates the pipeline from build through test to deployment. CodeCommit stores source code, CodeBuild builds, and CodeDeploy deploys; each is an individual component."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"VPC（Virtual Private Cloud）とインターネットの間の出入口として、VPCにアタッチするものはどれか。","o":["インターネットゲートウェイ（IGW）","VPCエンドポイント経由の接続","AWS Direct Connect 専用線","NATゲートウェイ経由の通信"],"a":0,"e":"パブリック通信の出入口。外部到達の実現。","qEn":"Which component is attached to a VPC (Virtual Private Cloud) as the entry and exit point between the VPC and the internet?","oEn":["Internet gateway (IGW)","Connection through a VPC endpoint","AWS Direct Connect dedicated line","Communication through a NAT gateway"],"eEn":"Entry and exit point for public communication. Enables external reachability."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"プライベートサブネットから外向き通信のみ許可する仕組みはどれか。","o":["NATゲートウェイ","Egressゲートウェイ","インターネットゲートウェイ","VPCエンドポイント"],"a":0,"e":"NATゲートウェイは、プライベートサブネットから外向きの通信だけを許可し、外からの内向き通信は遮断する。インターネットゲートウェイは双方向の通信を通し、VPCエンドポイントはAWSサービスへの閉域接続である。","qEn":"Which mechanism allows only outbound communication from a private subnet?","oEn":["NAT gateway","Egress gateway","Internet gateway","VPC endpoint"],"eEn":"A NAT gateway allows only outbound communication from a private subnet and blocks inbound communication from outside. An internet gateway passes traffic in both directions, and a VPC endpoint is a private connection to AWS services."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"VPC（Virtual Private Cloud）内のリソースをAWS（Amazon Web Services）サービスへ閉域接続する仕組みはどれか。","o":["インターネットゲートウェイ","VPCエンドポイント","NATゲートウェイ","Direct Connect"],"a":1,"e":"インターネット非経由の接続。セキュアな通信。","qEn":"Which mechanism provides a private connection from resources in a VPC (Virtual Private Cloud) to AWS (Amazon Web Services) services?","oEn":["Internet gateway","VPC endpoint","NAT gateway","Direct Connect"],"eEn":"A connection that does not go through the internet. Secure communication."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）で、OSと導入済みのソフトウェアを含むイメージを作り、同じ構成のインスタンスを素早く複製する仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS CloudFormation スタック","EC2 Auto Scaling 起動設定","Amazon Machine Image（AMI）","起動テンプレート（Launch Template）"],"a":2,"e":"AMIはOS・設定・導入済みソフトウェアをまとめたイメージで、そこから同じ構成のインスタンスを何台でも起動できる。起動テンプレートはインスタンスタイプやセキュリティグループなどの起動パラメータの雛形で、OSやソフトウェアのイメージそのものは持たない（AMIを参照する側）。CloudFormationスタックはリソース一式をコードで作る仕組み。","qEn":"Which mechanism creates an image that includes the OS and installed software in EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) so that instances with the same configuration can be quickly replicated?","oEn":["AWS CloudFormation stack","EC2 Auto Scaling launch configuration","Amazon Machine Image (AMI)","Launch template"],"eEn":"An AMI is an image that bundles the OS, settings, and installed software, and you can launch any number of instances with the same configuration from it. A launch template is a blueprint of launch parameters such as the instance type and security groups; it does not hold the OS or software image itself (it references an AMI). A CloudFormation stack is a mechanism for creating a set of resources from code."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"グローバルにユーザーを最寄りエンドポイントへ誘導し性能を高めるサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Route 53 のみ","Amazon CloudFront ディストリビューション","AWS Global Accelerator","AWS Direct Connect 接続"],"a":2,"e":"AWSネットワーク経由の高速化。可用性の向上。","qEn":"Which service directs users around the world to the nearest endpoint to improve performance?","oEn":["Amazon Route 53 only","Amazon CloudFront distribution","AWS Global Accelerator","AWS Direct Connect connection"],"eEn":"Faster performance over the AWS network. Improved availability."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"複数VPC（Virtual Private Cloud）やオンプレを集約接続するハブはどれか。","o":["VPCピアリング（Peering）","AWS Direct Connect 専用線","NATゲートウェイ経由の接続","AWS Transit Gateway"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Transit Gatewayは、複数のVPCやオンプレミスをハブとして集約接続し、ネットワーク管理を簡素にする。VPCピアリングは1対1の接続、Direct Connectは専用線、NATゲートウェイは外向き通信用である。","qEn":"Which hub aggregates connections among multiple VPCs (Virtual Private Cloud) and on-premises networks?","oEn":["VPC peering","AWS Direct Connect dedicated line","Connection through a NAT gateway","AWS Transit Gateway"],"eEn":"AWS Transit Gateway acts as a hub that aggregates connections among multiple VPCs and on-premises networks, simplifying network management. VPC peering is a one-to-one connection, Direct Connect is a dedicated line, and a NAT gateway is for outbound communication."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"アプリのユーザー認証・サインアップ機能を提供するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Directory Service","Amazon API Gateway","Amazon Cognito","AWS IAM ユーザー"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon Cognitoは、アプリのユーザー認証やサインアップ機能を提供し、外部IDとの連携もできる。AWS Directory ServiceはAD関連、API GatewayはAPI管理、IAMユーザーはAWS操作者向けである。","qEn":"Which service provides user authentication and sign-up features for applications?","oEn":["AWS Directory Service","Amazon API Gateway","Amazon Cognito","AWS IAM users"],"eEn":"Amazon Cognito provides user authentication and sign-up features for applications and can also integrate with external identities. AWS Directory Service relates to AD, API Gateway is for API management, and IAM users are for people who operate AWS."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"スケーラブルなメール送信サービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon SNS","Amazon SQS","Amazon SES","Amazon Chime"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon SESは、大量のメールを送れるスケーラブルな送信基盤で、到達性の確保にも役立つ。Amazon SNSは通知の配信、SQSはメッセージのキュー、Chimeは会議サービスで、メール送信基盤ではない。","qEn":"Which is a scalable email-sending service?","eEn":"Amazon SES is a scalable sending platform that can send large volumes of email and also helps ensure deliverability. Amazon SNS delivers notifications, SQS queues messages, and Chime is a meeting service; none of them is an email-sending platform."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"テキスト抽出（OCR）を文書から行うサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Textract","Amazon Comprehend","Amazon Rekognition","Amazon Kendra"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon Textractは、文書や画像から文字や表を抽出するOCRサービスである。Comprehendは文章の分析、Rekognitionは画像や動画の分析、Kendraは企業向けの検索サービスである。","qEn":"Which service performs text extraction (OCR) from documents?","eEn":"Amazon Textract is an OCR service that extracts text and tables from documents and images. Comprehend analyzes text, Rekognition analyzes images and videos, and Kendra is an enterprise search service."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"会話型ボットを構築するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Kendra","Amazon Lex","Amazon Connect","Amazon Polly"],"a":1,"e":"チャットボットの構築。音声・テキスト対応。","qEn":"Which service builds conversational bots?","eEn":"Building chatbots. Supports voice and text."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CloudFormationのテンプレート言語として使えるものはどれか。","o":["JSONまたはYAML","HCL専用フォーマット","JSONのみでYAMLは非対応","XMLまたはTOML"],"a":0,"e":"CloudFormationのテンプレートは、JSONまたはYAMLで書く宣言的な記述である。HCLはTerraformの形式で、JSONのみでYAML非対応とするのは誤りであり、XMLやTOMLも使わない。","qEn":"Which can be used as the template language for CloudFormation?","oEn":["JSON or YAML","An HCL-only format","JSON only, with YAML unsupported","XML or TOML"],"eEn":"CloudFormation templates are declarative descriptions written in JSON or YAML. HCL is the format of Terraform, it is incorrect to say JSON only and YAML is unsupported, and XML and TOML are not used either."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"サーバーレスデータベースとして容量を自動調整するAuroraの形態はどれか。","o":["Amazon DynamoDB On-Demand","Amazon Aurora Serverless","Amazon RDS Multi-AZ","Amazon Redshift Serverless"],"a":1,"e":"需要連動の容量調整。アイドル時のコスト削減。","qEn":"Which form of Aurora automatically adjusts capacity as a serverless database?","eEn":"Capacity adjustment that follows demand. Reduced cost when idle."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の最も基本的な無料サポートプランはどれか。","o":["開発者サポート","ベーシックサポート","ビジネスサポート","エンタープライズサポート"],"a":1,"e":"全顧客に無償提供。ドキュメントとフォーラム。","qEn":"Which is the most basic free support plan of AWS (Amazon Web Services)?","oEn":["Developer Support","Basic Support","Business Support","Enterprise Support"],"eEn":"Provided free to all customers. Documentation and forums."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"開発・テスト環境向けで業務時間内のメール対応が含まれるプランはどれか。","o":["ベーシックサポート","ビジネスサポート","エンタープライズ","開発者サポート"],"a":3,"e":"技術的な相談対応。低コストの有償プラン。（2026年11月時点：Developerは2025年12月2日に新規受付を終了し、2027年1月1日に提供終了。後継は月額29ドルからで24時間365日対応のBusiness Support+）","qEn":"Which plan is intended for development and test environments and includes email support during business hours?","oEn":["Basic Support","Business Support","Enterprise","Developer Support"],"eEn":"Technical consultation support. A low-cost paid plan. (As of November 2026: Developer Support stopped accepting new subscriptions on December 2, 2025 and will be discontinued on January 1, 2027. Its successor is Business Support+, which starts at $29 per month and offers 24/7 access.)"},
  {"d":"D4","q":"詳細な課金明細をデータとして出力する仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Cost Explorer（コスト可視化）","AWS Cost and Usage Report（CUR）","AWS Billing Conductor（請求管理）","AWS Pricing Calculator（事前見積もり）"],"a":1,"e":"最も詳細な使用・コストデータ。分析基盤への連携。","qEn":"Which mechanism outputs detailed billing statements as data?","oEn":["AWS Cost Explorer (cost visualization)","AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR)","AWS Billing Conductor (billing management)","AWS Pricing Calculator (advance estimates)"],"eEn":"The most detailed usage and cost data. Integrates with analytics platforms."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"一定期間または永続的に無料で使える枠の総称はどれか。","o":["スポットインスタンス（割引）","Savings Plans（割引）","リザーブドインスタンス（RI）","AWS無料利用枠（Free Tier）"],"a":3,"e":"AWS無料利用枠(Free Tier)は、一定期間または永続的に無料で使える枠の総称で、検証や学習に向く。AWS Creditsは付与される無料クレジット、AWS Activateはスタートアップ支援で、総称ではない。","qEn":"Which is the general term for allowances that can be used free for a limited period or permanently?","oEn":["Spot Instances (discount)","Savings Plans (long-term discount)","Reserved Instances (RI)","AWS Free Tier"],"eEn":"The AWS Free Tier is the general term for allowances that can be used free for a limited period or permanently, and it is suited to trials and learning. AWS Credits are free credits that are granted, and AWS Activate is startup support; neither is a general term."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）サービスの稼働状況や障害を確認するダッシュボードはどれか。","o":["Amazon CloudWatch Alarms","AWS Health Dashboard","AWS Trusted Advisor","AWS Systems Manager"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Health Dashboardは、AWSサービスの稼働状況や障害、自分のリソースへの影響を確認できる。CloudTrailはAPI監査ログ、CloudWatchは自分のリソースの監視、Trusted Advisorは構成の助言である。","qEn":"Which dashboard lets you check the operating status and outages of AWS (Amazon Web Services) services?","eEn":"The AWS Health Dashboard lets you check the operating status and outages of AWS services and their impact on your own resources. CloudTrail is the API audit log, CloudWatch monitors your own resources, and Trusted Advisor provides configuration advice."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"コスト最適化で「適切なサイズへ見直す」手法はどれか。","o":["スケールアップによる垂直方向の増強","ライトサイジング（Right Sizing）","Compute Savings Plansの適用","リザーブドインスタンスによる前払い"],"a":1,"e":"ライトサイジング(Right Sizing)は、過剰なリソースを実際の需要に合う大きさへ見直す手法である。スケールアウトとオートスケーリングは台数の増減、リザーブドインスタンスは割引購入で、サイズの見直しではない。","qEn":"Which technique in cost optimization means \"reviewing to the appropriate size\"?","oEn":["Vertical increase by scaling up","Right sizing","Applying Compute Savings Plans","Upfront payment with Reserved Instances"],"eEn":"Right sizing is a technique that reviews excess resources and adjusts them to a size that matches actual demand. Scaling out and Auto Scaling increase or decrease the number of instances, and Reserved Instances are a discounted purchase; neither is a review of size."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"データ転送料金で原則無料となる方向はどれか。","o":["インバウンド（AWSへの受信）","アウトバウンド（インターネットへの送信）","同一AZ内のデータ転送","リージョン間のデータ転送"],"a":0,"e":"データ転送料金では、AWSへのインバウンド(受信)は原則無料で、課金の中心はアウトバウンドである。インターネットへの送信やリージョン間のデータ転送には料金がかかる。","qEn":"Which direction of data transfer is free of charge in principle?","oEn":["Inbound (data received into AWS)","Outbound (data sent to the internet)","Data transfer within the same AZ","Data transfer between Regions"],"eEn":"For data transfer charges, inbound (data received into AWS) is free in principle, and charges are mainly for outbound. Sending data to the internet and transferring data between Regions incur charges."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"技術的な質問への自己解決を支援する公式Q&Aコミュニティはどれか。","o":["AWS re:Invent","AWS re:Post","AWS Support","AWS Forums"],"a":1,"e":"AWS re:Postは、技術的な質問を投稿して自己解決を図れる公式のQ&Aコミュニティである。Trusted Advisorは構成の助言、AWS Marketplaceはソフトの購入、AWSドキュメントは公式の資料集である。","qEn":"Which is the official Q&A community that supports self-service resolution of technical questions?","eEn":"AWS re:Post is the official Q&A community where you can post technical questions and resolve them yourself. Trusted Advisor provides configuration advice, AWS Marketplace is for purchasing software, and the AWS documentation is the official collection of reference material."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"ソフトウェアをAWS（Amazon Web Services）請求に統合して購入できる仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Data Exchange","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Marketplace","AWS License Manager"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Marketplaceは、サードパーティ製のソフトウェアをAWSの請求に統合して購入できる。AWS Service Catalogは承認済み製品の配布、AWS Artifactは監査文書、AWS Configは構成管理である。","qEn":"Which mechanism lets you purchase software with the charges integrated into your AWS (Amazon Web Services) bill?","eEn":"AWS Marketplace lets you purchase third-party software with the charges integrated into your AWS bill. AWS Service Catalog distributes approved products, AWS Artifact provides audit documents, and AWS Config manages configurations."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"コスト異常を自動で検知する機能はどれか。","o":["Amazon CloudWatch Anomaly Detection","AWS Budgets（予算アラート通知）","AWS Cost Explorer（傾向分析）","AWS Cost Anomaly Detection"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Cost Anomaly Detectionは、機械学習で通常と異なる支出を自動検知し、早期に通知する。Cost Explorerは傾向分析、Budgetsは設定したしきい値のアラート、CloudWatchはメトリクス監視である。","qEn":"Which feature automatically detects cost anomalies?","oEn":["Amazon CloudWatch Anomaly Detection","AWS Budgets (budget alert notifications)","AWS Cost Explorer (trend analysis)","AWS Cost Anomaly Detection"],"eEn":"AWS Cost Anomaly Detection uses machine learning to automatically detect unusual spending and notify you early. Cost Explorer analyzes trends, Budgets alerts on thresholds you set, and CloudWatch monitors metrics."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"SavingsPlansとリザーブドのうちサービスやAZ（Availability Zone）変更に柔軟なのはどれか。","o":["スタンダードリザーブドインスタンス","Compute Savings Plans","EC2 Instance Savings Plans","コンバーティブルリザーブドインスタンス"],"a":1,"e":"Compute Savings Plansは、インスタンスファミリーやリージョンなどが変わっても割引が適用される、柔軟な割引である。スタンダードやコンバーティブルのリザーブド、EC2 Instance Savings Plansは対象が絞られる。","qEn":"Between Savings Plans and Reserved Instances, which is flexible about changes in service or AZ (Availability Zone)?","oEn":["Standard Reserved Instances","Compute Savings Plans","EC2 Instance Savings Plans","Convertible Reserved Instances"],"eEn":"Compute Savings Plans are a flexible discount that applies even when the instance family, Region, and so on change. Standard and Convertible Reserved Instances and EC2 Instance Savings Plans have a narrower scope."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"大企業が全社的なコスト管理に使う代表的な組み合わせはどれか。","o":["CloudWatch＋SNS＋EventBridge","Cost Explorer＋Budgets＋コスト配分タグ","Auto Scaling＋ELB＋CloudFront","GuardDuty＋Security Hub＋Config"],"a":1,"e":"大企業の全社的なコスト管理には、Cost Explorerで可視化し、Budgetsで通知し、コスト配分タグで配賦する組み合わせが基本となる。CloudWatchとSNS、Auto ScalingとELB、GuardDutyとSecurity Hubは別の目的の組み合わせである。","qEn":"Which is a typical combination used by a large enterprise for company-wide cost management?","oEn":["CloudWatch + SNS + EventBridge","Cost Explorer + Budgets + cost allocation tags","Auto Scaling + ELB + CloudFront","GuardDuty + Security Hub + Config"],"eEn":"For company-wide cost management in a large enterprise, the basic combination is Cost Explorer for visualization, Budgets for notification, and cost allocation tags for allocation. CloudWatch with SNS, Auto Scaling with ELB, and GuardDuty with Security Hub are combinations for other purposes."}];

var SET3 = [
  {"d":"D1","q":"年末セールでアクセスが急増し平常時は余剰サーバーが無駄になるEC企業に最適な対応はどれか。","o":["リザーブドインスタンスで年間予約する方式","単一の大型インスタンスへ垂直増強する","ピーク台数のサーバーを固定で確保し続ける構成","Auto Scalingによる需要連動の自動増減"],"a":3,"e":"ピーク時に拡張、閑散時に縮小。過不足のないリソース確保。","qEn":"Which is the best approach for an e-commerce company whose traffic surges during year-end sales, leaving surplus servers idle during normal periods?","oEn":["Reserving capacity for a year with Reserved Instances","Scaling up vertically to a single large instance","A configuration that keeps a fixed number of servers for peak load at all times","Automatic scaling in and out based on demand with Auto Scaling"],"eEn":"Expand at peak times and shrink during quiet times. Securing resources without excess or shortage."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"世界中のユーザーへ動画を低遅延で配信したいメディア企業に最適なサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon CloudFront（CDN）","単一リージョンのEC2から直接配信","AWS Direct Connectで専用線接続","AWS Global Acceleratorのみで配信"],"a":0,"e":"エッジロケーションからの配信。レイテンシー削減。","qEn":"Which service is best for a media company that wants to deliver video to users around the world with low latency?","oEn":["Amazon CloudFront (CDN)","Delivering directly from EC2 in a single Region","A Direct Connect dedicated-line connection","Delivering with AWS Global Accelerator only"],"eEn":"Delivery from edge locations. Reduced latency."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"規制により一部データを特定国内に保管する必要がある金融企業に最適な対応はどれか。","o":["全リージョンへ自動的に複製する","エッジロケーションへ分散配置","該当法域のリージョン選択","オンプレミスへ全面回帰する"],"a":2,"e":"データ所在地の制御。コンプライアンス要件への適合。","qEn":"Which is the best approach for a financial company that must store some data within a specific country due to regulations?","oEn":["Automatically replicate to all Regions","Distribute to edge locations","Select a Region in the relevant jurisdiction","Move everything back to on-premises"],"eEn":"Control over data location. Meeting compliance requirements."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"単一AZ（Availability Zone）構成で障害時に全停止するリスクを懸念する製造業に最適な改善策はどれか。","o":["同一AZ内でインスタンスを追加する","垂直スケールで単体を増強する","複数AZへのリソース分散","利用リージョン数を減らす"],"a":2,"e":"単一障害点の排除。リージョン内での高可用性。","qEn":"Which is the best improvement for a manufacturer concerned that a single-AZ (Availability Zone) configuration will cause a complete outage during a failure?","oEn":["Add instances within the same AZ","Strengthen a single instance by scaling vertically","Distribute resources across multiple AZs","Reduce the number of Regions in use"],"eEn":"Eliminating single points of failure. High availability within a Region."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"新規アプリを最小投資で素早く検証したいスタートアップに最適な進め方はどれか。","o":["従量課金での即時構築と不要時の削除","3年分の長期契約を前払いで結ぶ","大型設備を事前に一括購入する","自社データセンターに物理サーバーを構築する"],"a":0,"e":"初期投資ゼロでの開始。低リスクな仮説検証。","qEn":"Which is the best approach for a startup that wants to quickly validate a new application with minimal investment?","oEn":["Build immediately with pay-as-you-go pricing and delete resources when no longer needed","Sign a three-year long-term contract with upfront payment","Buy large equipment in bulk in advance","Build physical servers in its own data center"],"eEn":"Starting with zero upfront investment. Low-risk hypothesis testing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"既存オンプレ資産を残しつつ一部をクラウドへ段階移行したいメーカーに最適な形態はどれか。","o":["プライベートクラウド単独","ハイブリッドクラウド","マルチクラウド構成","パブリッククラウド単独"],"a":1,"e":"既存資産とクラウドの連携。段階的な移行の実現。","qEn":"Which deployment model is best for a manufacturer that wants to keep its existing on-premises assets while gradually migrating some workloads to the cloud?","oEn":["Private cloud alone","Hybrid cloud","Multi-cloud configuration","Public cloud alone"],"eEn":"Integration of existing assets and the cloud. Enabling gradual migration."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）が推奨する「すべてを自動化」する設計思想の目的はどれか。","o":["運用ミス削減とスケールの容易化","インフラコストを増加させる","手作業を増やして個別に柔軟対応する","構成を固定し一切の変更を禁止する"],"a":0,"e":"すべてを自動化する設計は、反復作業の手作業を減らして運用ミスを防ぎ、スケールしやすくする。インフラコストの増加が目的ではなく、手作業の個別対応や構成の固定化は自動化の考え方と逆である。","qEn":"What is the purpose of the design principle \"automate everything\" recommended by AWS (Amazon Web Services)?","oEn":["Reducing operational errors and making scaling easier","Increasing infrastructure costs","Increasing manual work to respond flexibly case by case","Fixing the configuration and prohibiting any changes"],"eEn":"A design that automates everything reduces manual work on repetitive tasks, which prevents operational errors and makes scaling easier. The purpose is not to increase infrastructure costs, and handling cases manually or freezing the configuration is the opposite of the idea of automation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"ビッグデータや機械学習の試行がクラウドで容易な理由はどれか。","o":["物理機材を購入して自社データセンターに設置する","常時最大容量を固定で保有し続ける","長期予約を必須として契約する","大規模リソースの一時的な確保と即時解放"],"a":3,"e":"クラウドでは、大規模リソースを一時的に確保して使い終えたらすぐ解放できるため、ビッグデータや機械学習の試行が容易になる。物理機材の購入や最大容量の固定保有、長期予約は試行錯誤に向かない。","qEn":"Why is it easy to try out big data and machine learning in the cloud?","oEn":["Purchasing physical equipment and installing it in your own data center","Continuously holding maximum capacity at a fixed level","Requiring a long-term reservation under contract","Temporarily obtaining large-scale resources and releasing them immediately"],"eEn":"In the cloud, you can temporarily obtain large-scale resources and release them immediately after use, which makes it easy to try out big data and machine learning. Purchasing physical equipment, holding maximum capacity at a fixed level, and long-term reservations are not suited to trial and error."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"オンプレミスと比べたクラウドの導入スピードの違いはどれか。","o":["数分での環境構築","数週間の調達期間が必要","長期契約の締結が必須","物理機器の設置が前提"],"a":0,"e":"クラウドは調達や設置の工程が要らず、数分で環境を構築して始められる。数週間の調達期間、長期契約の締結、物理機器の設置はオンプレミスで必要になる手順である。","qEn":"Which describes the difference in adoption speed of the cloud compared with on-premises?","oEn":["Environments can be built in minutes","A procurement period of several weeks is required","Signing a long-term contract is mandatory","Installing physical equipment is a prerequisite"],"eEn":"The cloud does not require procurement or installation steps, so you can build an environment and get started in minutes. A procurement period of several weeks, signing a long-term contract, and installing physical equipment are steps required on-premises."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） CAF（Cloud Adoption Framework）の「セキュリティパースペクティブ」が扱う範囲はどれか。","o":["システムの運用監視とインシデント対応","従業員のスキル育成と変革を支える健全な組織文化の醸成","クラウド利用料金の最適化と予算管理","ワークロードと資産の機密性・完全性・可用性の確保"],"a":3,"e":"CAFのセキュリティパースペクティブは、ワークロードと資産の機密性・完全性・可用性を確保する領域を扱う。運用監視とインシデント対応はオペレーション、従業員のスキルと文化は人材、料金最適化はファイナンス寄りの領域である。","qEn":"What does the \"Security Perspective\" of the AWS (Amazon Web Services) CAF (Cloud Adoption Framework) cover?","oEn":["Operational monitoring and incident response for systems","Developing employee skills and fostering a healthy organizational culture that supports transformation","Optimizing cloud usage costs and managing budgets","Ensuring the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of workloads and assets"],"eEn":"The CAF Security Perspective covers the area of ensuring the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of workloads and assets. Operational monitoring and incident response belong to Operations, employee skills and culture belong to People, and cost optimization is closer to the Finance area."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"リソースのタグ付け（Tagging）が支援する管理はどれか。","o":["ネットワークトラフィックの負荷分散","保存データの自動暗号化","コスト配分とリソースの整理","ドメイン名のDNS名前解決"],"a":2,"e":"リソースのタグ付けは、部門やプロジェクトを示す印を付け、コスト配分とリソースの整理に使う。負荷分散、保存データの暗号化、DNSの名前解決は、タグ付けではなく別の機能が担う。","qEn":"Which kind of management does resource tagging support?","oEn":["Load balancing of network traffic","Automatic encryption of stored data","Cost allocation and resource organization","DNS name resolution for domain names"],"eEn":"Resource tagging attaches labels that indicate a department or project, and is used for cost allocation and resource organization. Load balancing, encryption of stored data, and DNS name resolution are handled by other features, not by tagging."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"マネージドデータベースを使う利点はどれか。","o":["物理サーバーを専有して使える","パッチ適用やバックアップの自動化","DBライセンスを自己管理する","OSやミドルウェアを自由に設定できる"],"a":1,"e":"マネージドデータベースは、パッチ適用やバックアップをクラウド側が自動で行い、運用負担を軽くする。物理サーバーの専有、DBライセンスの自己管理、OSやミドルウェアの自由な設定は、自分で管理する構成の特徴である。","qEn":"What is an advantage of using a managed database?","oEn":["You can use a dedicated physical server","Automated patching and backups","You manage database licenses yourself","You can freely configure the OS and middleware"],"eEn":"With a managed database, the cloud side automates patching and backups, which reduces the operational burden. Using a dedicated physical server, managing database licenses yourself, and freely configuring the OS and middleware are characteristics of configurations you manage yourself."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"弾力性と拡張性の違いとして正しいものはどれか。","o":["弾力性は長期的な成長への備えを指す","拡張性は短期的な負荷変動に自動対応する能力","両者は全く同じ意味の同一概念である","弾力性は自動増減、拡張性は将来の成長余地"],"a":3,"e":"弾力性は負荷に応じて自動で増減する能力、拡張性は将来の成長に応じて能力を伸ばせる余地を指す。弾力性を長期的な成長への備えとする説明や、同一概念とする説明は誤りである。","qEn":"Which correctly describes the difference between elasticity and scalability?","oEn":["Elasticity refers to preparing for long-term growth","Scalability is the ability to respond automatically to short-term load fluctuations","They are exactly the same concept","Elasticity is automatic scaling in and out, and scalability is room for future growth"],"eEn":"Elasticity is the ability to automatically scale in and out according to load, and scalability is the room to grow capacity as future growth requires. Explaining elasticity as preparation for long-term growth, or calling them the same concept, is incorrect."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドでDR（災害復旧）を低コストに実現できる理由はどれか。","o":["平常時は最小、災害時に拡張する構成","固定の予備リソースを常時フルで確保する","物理的に二重化した予備設備を持つ","常時フル稼働の待機系を維持し続ける"],"a":0,"e":"クラウドでは、平常時は最小の構成で待機し、災害時に拡張すれば済むため、DRを低コストにできる。固定の予備リソースを常時フルで確保したり、二重化した予備設備や待機系を維持し続けると費用が膨らむ。","qEn":"Why can disaster recovery (DR) be implemented at low cost in the cloud?","oEn":["A configuration that is minimal in normal times and expands during a disaster","Continuously keeping fixed spare resources at full capacity","Having physically duplicated standby facilities","Continuously maintaining a standby system running at full capacity"],"eEn":"In the cloud, you can stay on standby with a minimal configuration in normal times and simply expand during a disaster, so DR can be done at low cost. Continuously keeping fixed spare resources at full capacity, or maintaining duplicated standby facilities or a standby system, drives up costs."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のサービスを組み合わせて疎結合化する代表的な仕組みはどれか。","o":["コンポーネント間の密結合をさらに強化","メッセージキューによる非同期連携","直接的な同期API呼び出しで連携","全機能を単一プロセスへ統合する"],"a":1,"e":"メッセージキューによる非同期連携は、コンポーネント間の直接依存をなくし、障害を局所化する疎結合の代表例である。密結合の強化、同期API呼び出し、単一プロセスへの統合は、疎結合とは逆の方向である。","qEn":"Which is a typical mechanism for loosely coupling a combination of AWS (Amazon Web Services) services?","oEn":["Further strengthening tight coupling between components","Asynchronous integration through a message queue","Integration through direct synchronous API calls","Consolidating all functions into a single process"],"eEn":"Asynchronous integration through a message queue is a typical example of loose coupling, which removes direct dependencies between components and localizes failures. Strengthening tight coupling, synchronous API calls, and consolidating into a single process go in the opposite direction from loose coupling."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"グローバルインフラの「ローカルゾーン」が解決する課題はどれか。","o":["広域災害に備えた冗長化対策","単なるコスト削減のみを目的とした構成","データ所在地規制への準拠","特定都市での超低レイテンシー要件"],"a":3,"e":"ユーザー近傍での計算配置。応答性の向上。","qEn":"Which challenge do Local Zones in the global infrastructure solve?","oEn":["Redundancy measures against wide-area disasters","A configuration aimed solely at cost reduction","Compliance with data residency regulations","Ultra-low-latency requirements in a specific city"],"eEn":"Placing compute close to users. Improved responsiveness."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「使った分だけ支払う」モデルが小規模スタートアップに有利な理由はどれか。","o":["大量購入による大規模割引が前提","初期投資なしでの事業開始","固定費で毎月の支出が安定する","長期契約による価格の保証"],"a":1,"e":"使った分だけ払うモデルは、初期投資なしで事業を始められるため、資金に乏しいスタートアップに有利である。大量購入の割引や長期契約の価格保証、固定費の安定は、この従量課金の利点ではない。","qEn":"Why does the \"pay for what you use\" model benefit small startups?","oEn":["It presupposes large discounts from bulk purchasing","They can start a business with no upfront investment","Fixed costs keep monthly spending stable","Long-term contracts guarantee prices"],"eEn":"The pay-for-what-you-use model lets a business start with no upfront investment, which benefits startups with limited funds. Bulk-purchase discounts, price guarantees from long-term contracts, and stable fixed costs are not benefits of this pay-as-you-go pricing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"リージョンを跨いだ冗長構成が主に備える事象はどれか。","o":["単一AZ内の軽微な障害","一時的なネットワークの応答遅延","リージョン全体に及ぶ広域障害","単一インスタンスの障害のみ"],"a":2,"e":"リージョンをまたぐ冗長構成は、リージョン全体に及ぶ広域障害に備える。単一AZ内の軽微な障害は複数AZ構成で足り、一時的なネットワークの遅延や単一インスタンスの障害にはより小さな対策で対応できる。","qEn":"Which event does a cross-Region redundant configuration mainly prepare for?","oEn":["A minor failure within a single AZ","A temporary network response delay","A wide-area failure affecting an entire Region","A failure of a single instance only"],"eEn":"A cross-Region redundant configuration prepares for a wide-area failure affecting an entire Region. A minor failure within a single AZ can be handled with a multi-AZ configuration, and temporary network delays or a single-instance failure can be handled with smaller measures."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Well-Architected Toolの役割はどれか。","o":["リソースを自動でプロビジョニングし構築する","月々の課金明細を集計して表示する","ワークロードを6本柱で評価し改善点を提示","DDoS攻撃を自動的に検知し緩和する"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Well-Architected Toolは、ワークロードを6本柱の観点で評価し、改善点を提示する。リソースの自動構築はCloudFormation、課金明細はBilling、DDoSの検知と緩和はShieldの役割である。","qEn":"What is the role of the AWS (Amazon Web Services) Well-Architected Tool?","oEn":["Automatically provisioning and building resources","Aggregating and displaying monthly billing statements","Evaluating workloads against the six pillars and presenting improvements","Automatically detecting and mitigating DDoS attacks"],"eEn":"The AWS Well-Architected Tool evaluates workloads from the perspective of the six pillars and presents improvements. Automatic resource building is the role of CloudFormation, billing statements are Billing, and DDoS detection and mitigation is Shield."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） CAF（Cloud Adoption Framework）の「ガバナンスパースペクティブ」が扱うものはどれか。","o":["リスク・コンプライアンスの統制と投資最適化","クラウド技術基盤の設計と構築を担う","システムの運用監視と障害対応を行う","変化に対応する従業員のスキル育成と文化変革"],"a":0,"e":"CAFのガバナンスパースペクティブは、リスクとコンプライアンスの統制、投資の最適化を扱う。技術基盤の設計はプラットフォーム、運用監視と障害対応はオペレーション、スキル育成と文化変革は人材の領域である。","qEn":"What does the \"Governance Perspective\" of the AWS (Amazon Web Services) CAF (Cloud Adoption Framework) cover?","oEn":["Control of risk and compliance and investment optimization","Designing and building the cloud technology foundation","Operational monitoring and incident response for systems","Developing employee skills and driving cultural change to adapt to change"],"eEn":"The CAF Governance Perspective covers control of risk and compliance and optimization of investment. Designing the technology foundation belongs to Platform, operational monitoring and incident response belong to Operations, and skill development and cultural change belong to People."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの「俊敏性」が研究開発（R&D）に向く理由はどれか。","o":["必要容量を事前に確定させる","大規模計算の一時利用と即時解放","固定設備を長期にわたり保有する","物理機材をあらかじめ購入する"],"a":1,"e":"クラウドの俊敏性は、大規模計算を一時的に使って即座に解放できるため、試行錯誤の多いR&Dに向く。必要容量の事前確定、固定設備の長期保有、物理機材の事前購入は、試行のコストを高める。","qEn":"Why does cloud \"agility\" suit research and development (R&D)?","oEn":["The required capacity must be determined in advance","Large-scale computing can be used temporarily and released immediately","Fixed facilities are held over the long term","Physical equipment is purchased in advance"],"eEn":"Cloud agility lets you use large-scale computing temporarily and release it immediately, which suits R&D, where there is a lot of trial and error. Fixing required capacity in advance, holding fixed facilities long term, and buying physical equipment in advance raise the cost of experimentation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"オンプレミスと比べクラウドが下げる主なコストはどれか。","o":["アプリケーションソフトの開発費","設備投資と運用保守の固定費","ネットワーク回線の従量料金","従業員への人材教育費"],"a":1,"e":"クラウドは、オンプレミスで必要な設備投資と運用保守の固定費を下げ、変動費に変える。アプリケーションの開発費、回線の従量料金、人材教育費は、クラウドへ移しても主に下がる費用ではない。","qEn":"Which cost does the cloud mainly reduce compared with on-premises?","oEn":["Application software development costs","Fixed costs of capital investment and operations and maintenance","Pay-as-you-go charges for network lines","Employee training costs"],"eEn":"The cloud reduces the fixed costs of capital investment and operations and maintenance required on-premises, and turns them into variable costs. Application development costs, network line usage charges, and training costs are not mainly reduced even after moving to the cloud."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドネイティブ設計が前提とする考え方はどれか。","o":["単一の巨大なサーバーへ全機能を集約する構成","すべての運用や保守を手作業で徹底する","マネージド・サーバーレスを活用した拡張前提の設計","物理ハードウェアへの依存を一層強める"],"a":2,"e":"クラウドネイティブ設計は、マネージドサービスやサーバーレスを活用し、拡張を前提に作る考え方である。単一の巨大サーバーへの集約、手作業での運用保守、物理ハードウェア依存の強化は、その逆である。","qEn":"Which idea does cloud-native design assume?","oEn":["A configuration that consolidates all functions on one huge server","Thoroughly performing all operations and maintenance manually","A design built for growth that uses managed and serverless services","Further increasing dependence on physical hardware"],"eEn":"Cloud-native design is the approach of building for growth by using managed services and serverless. Consolidating onto one huge server, manual operations and maintenance, and increasing dependence on physical hardware are the opposite."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「差別化につながらない重労働」をAWS（Amazon Web Services）へ委ねる典型例はどれか。","o":["自社製品のUXデザインと企画立案","サーバー調達や保守などの定型作業","独自アルゴリズムのコード実装と改良","顧客データに基づく事業戦略の策定"],"a":1,"e":"差別化につながらない重労働とは、サーバー調達や保守といった定型作業で、AWSに任せて本業に集中する。UXデザインや独自アルゴリズムの実装、事業戦略の策定は、自社の価値を生む仕事である。","qEn":"Which is a typical example of handing \"undifferentiated heavy lifting\" over to AWS (Amazon Web Services)?","oEn":["UX design and planning for your own products","Routine tasks such as server procurement and maintenance","Coding and improving proprietary algorithms","Formulating business strategy based on customer data"],"eEn":"Undifferentiated heavy lifting means routine tasks such as server procurement and maintenance, which you leave to AWS so you can focus on your core business. UX design, implementing proprietary algorithms, and formulating business strategy are work that creates your own value."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"開発者にアクセスキーを直接配布せずEC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）からS3（Simple Storage Service）へ安全にアクセスさせたい場合の最適手段はどれか。","o":["S3バケットポリシーで全公開設定","EC2へのIAMロール割り当て","認証情報をEC2の環境変数に格納","IAMユーザーのアクセスキーを発行"],"a":1,"e":"長期キー不要の一時認証。漏洩リスクの低減。","qEn":"Which is the best way to let EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) access S3 (Simple Storage Service) securely without distributing access keys directly to developers?","oEn":["Make everything public with an S3 bucket policy","Assign an IAM role to EC2","Store credentials in EC2 environment variables","Issue access keys for an IAM user"],"eEn":"Temporary credentials with no long-term keys. Reduced risk of leakage."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service）内に個人情報が混入していないか継続的に検査したい医療企業に最適なサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Macie","Amazon GuardDuty","Amazon Detective","Amazon Inspector"],"a":0,"e":"機械学習による機密データ検出。漏洩リスクの可視化。","qEn":"Which service is best for a healthcare company that wants to continuously check whether personal information has been mixed into S3 (Simple Storage Service)?","eEn":"Detects sensitive data using machine learning. Makes leakage risk visible."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"Webアプリへの不正な攻撃通信を遮断したいSaaS（Software as a Service）企業に最適な組み合わせはどれか。","o":["AWS WAF＋AWS Shield","Amazon Macie＋GuardDuty","Amazon Cognito＋AWS IAM","AWS Config＋AWS CloudTrail"],"a":0,"e":"レイヤー7攻撃とDDoSの緩和。可用性の確保。","qEn":"Which combination is best for a SaaS (Software as a Service) company that wants to block malicious attack traffic to its web application?","eEn":"Mitigation of Layer 7 attacks and DDoS. Ensuring availability."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"誰がどのリソースを操作したかを監査要件として記録したい場合に最適なサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Systems Manager","AWS Config Rules","AWS CloudTrail","Amazon CloudWatch"],"a":2,"e":"AWS CloudTrailは、誰がどのリソースを操作したかをAPI操作履歴として記録し、監査証跡になる。Systems Managerは運用管理、Config Rulesは構成の評価、CloudWatchはメトリクスと稼働の監視を担う。","qEn":"Which service is best when you want to record who operated which resources as an audit requirement?","eEn":"AWS CloudTrail records who operated which resources as an API operation history and serves as an audit trail. Systems Manager handles operations management, Config Rules evaluate configurations, and CloudWatch handles monitoring of metrics and operations."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"パスワードポリシー（長さ・複雑性）を強制する場所はどれか。","o":["IAMのアカウントパスワードポリシー","AWS OrganizationsのSCP","IAMユーザーのインラインポリシー","セキュリティグループの受信ルール"],"a":0,"e":"パスワードの長さや複雑性は、IAMのアカウントパスワードポリシーで強制する。OrganizationsのSCPはアカウントの権限の上限を決め、インラインポリシーは個別の権限、セキュリティグループは通信を制御する。","qEn":"Where do you enforce a password policy (length and complexity)?","oEn":["The IAM account password policy","An SCP in AWS Organizations","An inline policy of an IAM user","Inbound rules of a security group"],"eEn":"Password length and complexity are enforced with the IAM account password policy. An Organizations SCP sets the upper limit of an account's permissions, an inline policy defines individual permissions, and a security group controls traffic."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ルートユーザーでのみ実行すべき作業の例はどれか。","o":["アカウントの解約や支払い情報の変更","日常的なEC2インスタンスの起動","IAMユーザーの作成と権限付与","CloudWatchでのメトリクス監視設定"],"a":0,"e":"アカウントの解約は、ルートユーザーでのみ実行すべき特権操作である。EC2の起動、IAMユーザーの作成と権限付与、CloudWatchの監視設定は、日常的な操作としてIAMユーザーで行う。","qEn":"Which is an example of a task that should be performed only by the root user?","oEn":["Closing the account or changing payment information","Routinely launching EC2 instances","Creating IAM users and granting permissions","Configuring metric monitoring in CloudWatch"],"eEn":"Closing the account is a privileged operation that should be performed only by the root user. Launching EC2, creating IAM users and granting permissions, and configuring CloudWatch monitoring are everyday operations performed by IAM users."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Artifactで取得できる代表的な文書はどれか。","o":["課金明細やコスト配分レポート","CloudFormationのテンプレート","CloudWatchのメトリクスとログ","SOC報告書やISO認証などの監査資料"],"a":3,"e":"コンプライアンス証跡。監査対応の効率化。","qEn":"Which is a typical document that you can obtain from AWS (Amazon Web Services) Artifact?","oEn":["Billing statements and cost allocation reports","CloudFormation templates","CloudWatch metrics and logs","Audit materials such as SOC reports and ISO certifications"],"eEn":"Compliance evidence. More efficient audit response."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティグループで「拒否ルール」を設定できない理由はどれか。","o":["許可ルールのみを定義する仕様","ルールを番号順に評価するから","サブネット単位で適用するから","ステートレスに動作するから"],"a":0,"e":"セキュリティグループは許可ルールのみを定義する仕様で、拒否ルールは書けない。番号順の評価やサブネット単位の適用、ステートレスな動作はNACLの特徴で、拒否が必要ならNACLで補う。","qEn":"Why can't you configure \"deny rules\" in a security group?","oEn":["It is designed to define allow rules only","Because rules are evaluated in numerical order","Because it is applied at the subnet level","Because it operates statelessly"],"eEn":"A security group is designed to define allow rules only, so deny rules cannot be written. Evaluation in numerical order, application at the subnet level, and stateless operation are characteristics of NACLs, and if you need to deny traffic, you supplement with a NACL."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ルートユーザーのアクセスキーに対する推奨はどれか。","o":["作成しない・削除する","チーム全員で共有する","定期的に複数発行する","平文でS3に保管する"],"a":0,"e":"ルートユーザーのアクセスキーは、強力で漏洩の被害が大きいため、作成せず、あれば削除するのが推奨である。チーム全員で共有する、複数発行する、平文でS3に保管するのは危険な扱いである。","qEn":"What is recommended for root user access keys?","oEn":["Do not create them, and delete them if they exist","Share them with the entire team","Issue multiple keys periodically","Store them in plain text in S3"],"eEn":"Root user access keys are powerful and a leak would cause great damage, so it is recommended not to create them and to delete them if they exist. Sharing them with the entire team, issuing multiple keys, and storing them in plain text in S3 are dangerous practices."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の暗号化で「保管中データのデフォルト保護」に近い例はどれか。","o":["通信経路のTLSによる暗号化","新規S3バケットのデフォルト暗号化","ACMによる証明書の自動更新","CloudFrontでのDDoS緩和対策"],"a":1,"e":"新規のS3バケットのデフォルト暗号化は、保管中のデータが自動で暗号化される例である。TLSによる通信の暗号化は転送中、ACMの証明書更新は証明書管理、CloudFrontのDDoS緩和は攻撃対策である。","qEn":"Which is an example close to \"default protection of data at rest\" in AWS (Amazon Web Services) encryption?","oEn":["Encrypting the communication path with TLS","Default encryption of new S3 buckets","Automatic renewal of certificates by ACM","DDoS mitigation measures in CloudFront"],"eEn":"Default encryption of new S3 buckets is an example of data at rest being encrypted automatically. Encrypting communication with TLS applies to data in transit, ACM certificate renewal is certificate management, and CloudFront DDoS mitigation is an attack countermeasure."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"アクセス権の定期的な棚卸し（レビュー）が必要な理由はどれか。","o":["コンプライアンス監査を省くため","不要権限の蓄積による攻撃面拡大の防止","ストレージコストの削減のため","アプリケーション性能の向上のため"],"a":1,"e":"アクセス権の定期的な棚卸しは、不要な権限が溜まって攻撃面が広がるのを防ぐために行う。監査を不要にする、ストレージコストを減らす、アプリの性能を上げることが目的ではない。","qEn":"Why is it necessary to periodically review access permissions?","oEn":["To make compliance audits unnecessary","To prevent the accumulation of unnecessary permissions from expanding the attack surface","To reduce storage costs","To improve application performance"],"eEn":"Periodic review of access permissions is performed to prevent unnecessary permissions from piling up and widening the attack surface. The purpose is not to eliminate audits, reduce storage costs, or improve application performance."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティ自動化でInfrastructure as Code（IaC）が貢献する点はどれか。","o":["手作業の増加と属人化","構成の標準化と監査可能性","インフラ構成のドリフト放置","リアルタイムの脅威検知"],"a":1,"e":"IaCは、インフラ構成をコードで標準化し、変更履歴も残るため、監査しやすくなる。手作業の増加と属人化、構成ドリフトの放置は逆の効果で、リアルタイムの脅威検知はGuardDutyなどの役割である。","qEn":"What does Infrastructure as Code (IaC) contribute to security automation?","oEn":["More manual work and dependence on individuals","Standardized configurations and auditability","Leaving infrastructure configuration drift unaddressed","Real-time threat detection"],"eEn":"IaC standardizes infrastructure configurations as code and keeps a change history, which makes auditing easier. More manual work and dependence on individuals, and leaving configuration drift unaddressed, have the opposite effect; real-time threat detection is the role of services such as GuardDuty."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ログを長期保管しコスト最適化する保存先の例はどれか。","o":["EFSファイルシステムへ常時保存","EBSの汎用SSDボリュームに保存","ElastiCacheのインメモリ領域に保持","S3（必要に応じGlacierへ階層化）"],"a":3,"e":"ログの長期保管には、低コストなS3に置き、必要に応じてGlacierへ階層化する方法が向く。EFSへの常時保存、EBSの汎用SSD、ElastiCacheのインメモリ領域は、長期保管には割高か不向きである。","qEn":"Which is an example of a storage destination for retaining logs long term while optimizing costs?","oEn":["Constantly storing them in an EFS file system","Storing them on an EBS General Purpose SSD volume","Holding them in ElastiCache in-memory storage","S3 (tiered to Glacier as needed)"],"eEn":"For long-term log retention, placing logs in low-cost S3 and tiering them to Glacier as needed is a good fit. Constant storage in EFS, EBS General Purpose SSD, and ElastiCache in-memory storage are expensive or unsuitable for long-term retention."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Security HubがCISなどの基準で行うことはどれか。","o":["SSL/TLS証明書の発行と管理","暗号鍵の定期的な自動ローテーション","DDoS攻撃のリアルタイムな検知と緩和","ベストプラクティスへの準拠スコア評価"],"a":3,"e":"Security Hubは、CISなどの基準に照らして設定を自動チェックし、ベストプラクティスへの準拠スコアを評価する。証明書の発行はACM、鍵のローテーションはKMS、DDoSの緩和はShieldが担う。","qEn":"What does AWS (Amazon Web Services) Security Hub do against standards such as CIS?","oEn":["Issues and manages SSL/TLS certificates","Automatically rotates encryption keys on a regular basis","Detects and mitigates DDoS attacks in real time","Evaluates compliance scores against best practices"],"eEn":"Security Hub automatically checks configurations against standards such as CIS and evaluates compliance scores against best practices. Certificate issuance is handled by ACM, key rotation by KMS, and DDoS mitigation by Shield."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"一時的な外部協力者へ安全にアクセスを与える方法はどれか。","o":["ルートユーザーのアクセスキーを共有","管理者権限のIAMユーザーの恒久的な発行","共有アカウントのパスワードを教える","期限付きのIAMロールまたはフェデレーション"],"a":3,"e":"一時的な外部協力者には、期限付きのIAMロールまたはフェデレーションで、一時認証情報を渡す。ルートのアクセスキーの共有、管理者の恒久IAMユーザー、共有パスワードは、失効せず漏洩の危険がある。","qEn":"Which is a way to safely grant access to a temporary external collaborator?","oEn":["Share the root user's access keys","Permanently issue an IAM user with administrator privileges","Tell them the password of a shared account","A time-limited IAM role or federation"],"eEn":"For a temporary external collaborator, you provide temporary credentials through a time-limited IAM role or federation. Sharing the root access keys, a permanent administrator IAM user, and a shared password do not expire and risk leakage."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の侵入テスト（ペネトレーションテスト）に関する方針として正しいものはどれか。","o":["対象サービスを問わず必ず事前の書面申請と承認が必須","一部の許可されたサービスは事前申請なしで実施可","いかなる場合も全面的に禁止されている","AWSの担当者による代行のみ許可される"],"a":1,"e":"ポリシー範囲内の許容。利用者責任での実施。","qEn":"Which correctly describes the policy on penetration testing for AWS (Amazon Web Services)?","oEn":["Written prior application and approval are always required, regardless of the target service","Some permitted services can be tested without prior approval","It is prohibited entirely in all cases","It is permitted only when performed by AWS representatives on your behalf"],"eEn":"Permitted within the policy scope. Performed under the customer's responsibility."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"暗号化されていないS3（Simple Storage Service）バケットを検出する手段はどれか。","o":["AWS Direct Connectによる専用線接続","AWS ConfigルールやSecurity Hub","Amazon Route 53によるDNSルーティング","Amazon CloudFrontによるコンテンツ配信"],"a":1,"e":"暗号化されていないS3バケットは、AWS ConfigルールやSecurity Hubで構成違反として検出できる。Direct Connectは専用線、Route 53はDNSルーティング、CloudFrontはコンテンツ配信で、構成の検査はしない。","qEn":"Which method detects unencrypted S3 (Simple Storage Service) buckets?","oEn":["A dedicated-line connection with AWS Direct Connect","AWS Config rules or Security Hub","DNS routing with Amazon Route 53","Content delivery with Amazon CloudFront"],"eEn":"Unencrypted S3 buckets can be detected as configuration violations with AWS Config rules or Security Hub. Direct Connect is a dedicated line, Route 53 is DNS routing, and CloudFront is content delivery; none of them inspects configurations."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の責任共有モデルにおける「設定の責任」が利用者にある例はどれか。","o":["データセンターの物理的な警備","ハイパーバイザーとホストOS","物理サーバーのハードウェア保守","セキュリティグループやS3公開設定"],"a":3,"e":"セキュリティグループやS3の公開設定は、利用者の設定責任にあたる。データセンターの物理的な警備、ハイパーバイザーとホストOSの管理、物理サーバーのハードウェア保守は、AWSが担う。","qEn":"Which is an example in which the customer is responsible for \"configuration\" in the AWS (Amazon Web Services) shared responsibility model?","oEn":["Physical security of the data center","Management of the hypervisor and host OS","Hardware maintenance of physical servers","Security groups and S3 public-access settings"],"eEn":"Security groups and S3 public-access settings fall under the customer's configuration responsibility. Physical security of the data center, management of the hypervisor and host OS, and hardware maintenance of physical servers are handled by AWS."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"IAM（Identity and Access Management）ポリシーで複数アカウントの権限上限を超えられない理由はどれか。","o":["NACLのサブネット制御","リソースベースのポリシー設定","保管データの暗号化の有無","SCPによる許可上限の制約"],"a":3,"e":"組織レベルの上限優先。アカウント内権限の制限。","qEn":"Why can't an IAM (Identity and Access Management) policy exceed the permission limit across multiple accounts?","oEn":["Subnet control by NACLs","Resource-based policy settings","Whether stored data is encrypted","The constraint on the permissions ceiling imposed by SCPs"],"eEn":"Organization-level limits take priority. Restricts permissions within the account."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"未使用の認証情報やアクセスキーへの推奨対応はどれか。","o":["アクセスキーを暗号化して保管する","変更せずにそのまま保持し続ける","無効化・削除と定期的なローテーション","チーム全体で共有して使い回す"],"a":2,"e":"未使用の認証情報やアクセスキーは、無効化・削除し、使うものは定期的にローテーションする。長期保管や変更せず保持し続ける、チーム全体で使い回すといった扱いは、漏洩時の被害を広げる。","qEn":"What is the recommended action for unused credentials and access keys?","oEn":["Encrypt the access keys and store them long term","Keep them as they are without changing them","Disable and delete them, and rotate them regularly","Share them across the whole team and reuse them"],"eEn":"Unused credentials and access keys should be disabled and deleted, and the ones in use should be rotated regularly. Storing them long term, keeping them unchanged, and sharing them across the whole team all increase the damage if they leak."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のセキュリティで「コンプライアンスは共有責任」が示すものはどれか。","o":["コンプライアンスは全て利用者が負う","第三者の監査機関が全ての責任を負う","AWSがOSより上の層も全て準拠する","基盤はAWS、ワークロードは利用者が準拠"],"a":3,"e":"コンプライアンスは共有責任で、基盤部分はAWSが準拠し、その上のワークロードは利用者が準拠する。すべて利用者が負う、第三者の監査機関が全責任を負う、AWSがOS上の層まで準拠するという説明は誤りである。","qEn":"What does \"compliance is a shared responsibility\" indicate in AWS (Amazon Web Services) security?","oEn":["The customer bears all compliance","A third-party audit body bears all responsibility","AWS complies for everything, including layers above the OS","AWS complies for the infrastructure, and the customer complies for the workload"],"eEn":"Compliance is a shared responsibility: AWS complies for the infrastructure, and the customer complies for the workload on top of it. Explanations that the customer bears everything, that a third-party audit body bears all responsibility, or that AWS complies up to the layers above the OS are incorrect."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Trusted Advisorのセキュリティチェックが指摘する例はどれか。","o":["CPU使用率などの性能指標","EBSボリュームのストレージ残量","MFA未設定や過剰に開放されたポート","ネットワークの帯域幅の使用状況"],"a":2,"e":"Trusted Advisorのセキュリティチェックは、MFA未設定や過剰に開放されたポートのような設定リスクを指摘する。CPU使用率などの性能指標、EBSの残量、ネットワーク帯域の使用状況はセキュリティ項目ではない。","qEn":"Which is an example flagged by the AWS (Amazon Web Services) Trusted Advisor security checks?","oEn":["Performance metrics such as CPU utilization","Remaining storage capacity of an EBS volume","MFA not enabled or excessively open ports","Network bandwidth usage"],"eEn":"The Trusted Advisor security checks flag configuration risks such as MFA not being enabled or excessively open ports. Performance metrics such as CPU utilization, remaining EBS capacity, and network bandwidth usage are not security items."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"WAF（Web Application Firewall）とShieldの組み合わせが守る主な脅威はどれか。","o":["EC2 インスタンスのハードウェア故障やディスク障害","WebアプリへのDDoSおよびレイヤー7攻撃","データセンターへの物理的な不正侵入","内部関係者による情報の持ち出しのみ"],"a":1,"e":"WAF と Shield の組み合わせは、Web アプリへの DDoS とレイヤー7攻撃を防ぐ。インスタンスのハードウェア故障は冗長構成で備えるもの、データセンターへの物理的な不正侵入は AWS の施設側の対策で、内部関係者による持ち出しも WAF や Shield の対象ではない。","qEn":"Which threats mainly does the combination of WAF (Web Application Firewall) and Shield protect against?","oEn":["Hardware failures and disk faults on EC2 instances","DDoS and Layer 7 attacks on web applications","Physical unauthorized entry into data centers","Information exfiltration by insiders only"],"eEn":"Combining WAF and Shield protects web apps against DDoS and layer 7 attacks. Instance hardware failures are handled with redundancy, physical intrusion into data centers is covered by AWS facility controls, and insider data theft is outside what WAF and Shield address."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） KMS（Key Management Service）の鍵を使う他サービスの例はどれか。","o":["CloudFrontのコンテンツ配信","S3・EBS・RDSの暗号化","ELBによるトラフィック分散","Route 53のDNSレコード解決"],"a":1,"e":"AWS KMSの鍵は、S3、EBS、RDSなどの保存データの暗号化に利用される。CloudFrontの配信、ELBの負荷分散、Route 53のDNSレコード解決は、鍵を使う暗号化が主目的の機能ではない。","qEn":"Which is an example of other services that use AWS (Amazon Web Services) KMS (Key Management Service) keys?","oEn":["Content delivery by CloudFront","Encryption of S3, EBS, and RDS","Traffic distribution by ELB","DNS record resolution by Route 53"],"eEn":"AWS KMS keys are used to encrypt stored data in services such as S3, EBS, and RDS. CloudFront delivery, ELB load balancing, and Route 53 DNS record resolution are not features whose main purpose is encryption using keys."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"「データ暗号化キーを利用者が完全管理したい」要件に最も適すサービスはどれか。","o":["ACM（証明書管理）","AWS CloudHSM","AWS KMS（マネージド型）","Secrets Manager"],"a":1,"e":"AWS CloudHSMは、利用者が専有するHSMで鍵を完全に管理でき、最高水準の統制を求める要件に向く。KMSはAWSが管理するマネージド型、ACMは証明書の管理、Secrets Managerは秘密情報の保管である。","qEn":"Which service best meets the requirement that the customer fully manage their own data encryption keys?","oEn":["ACM (certificate management)","AWS CloudHSM","AWS KMS (managed)","Secrets Manager"],"eEn":"AWS CloudHSM lets the customer fully manage keys in a dedicated HSM, which suits requirements for the highest level of control. KMS is a managed service run by AWS, ACM manages certificates, and Secrets Manager stores secrets."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"クレデンシャル（認証情報）のハードコーディングを避けるべき理由はどれか。","o":["漏洩時の不正利用リスク","実行性能が低下するため","課金額が増加するため","コードの行数が増えるため"],"a":0,"e":"認証情報をコードに直接書くと、ソースが流出した際に不正利用されるリスクがある。実行性能の低下や課金額の増加、コードの行数の増加は、ハードコーディングを避ける理由ではない。","qEn":"Why should credentials not be hardcoded?","oEn":["Risk of unauthorized use if leaked","Execution performance degrades","Billing charges increase","The number of lines of code increases"],"eEn":"If credentials are written directly in code, they can be misused when the source is leaked. Lower performance, higher charges, and more lines of code are not reasons to avoid hardcoding."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティ事故発生時にまず参照すべきログサービスはどれか。","o":["Health Dashboard（稼働状況）","CloudWatch（メトリクス監視）","Cost Explorer（費用分析）","CloudTrail（操作履歴）"],"a":3,"e":"セキュリティ事故では、誰が何をしたかを特定するため、まずCloudTrailの操作履歴を参照する。Health Dashboardは稼働状況、CloudWatchはメトリクス監視、Cost Explorerは費用分析で、調査の起点ではない。","qEn":"Which log service should you consult first when a security incident occurs?","oEn":["Health Dashboard (service status)","CloudWatch (metrics monitoring)","Cost Explorer (cost analysis)","CloudTrail (operation history)"],"eEn":"In a security incident, you first consult the CloudTrail operation history to identify who did what. Health Dashboard shows service status, CloudWatch monitors metrics, and Cost Explorer analyzes costs; none of them is the starting point for an investigation."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"機密ワークロードのネットワーク分離に有効なVPC（Virtual Private Cloud）機能はどれか。","o":["サブネット分割とルーティング制御","ELBによる負荷分散処理","Route 53によるDNS名前解決","CloudFrontによるコンテンツ配信"],"a":0,"e":"VPCのサブネット分割とルーティング制御により、公開と非公開を分け、機密ワークロードの境界を明確にできる。ELBは負荷分散、Route 53はDNSの名前解決、CloudFrontはコンテンツ配信で、ネットワーク分離ではない。","qEn":"Which VPC (Virtual Private Cloud) feature is effective for network isolation of sensitive workloads?","oEn":["Subnet segmentation and routing control","Load balancing with ELB","DNS name resolution with Route 53","Content delivery with CloudFront"],"eEn":"Subnet segmentation and routing control in a VPC separate public from private resources and clarify the boundary of sensitive workloads. ELB provides load balancing, Route 53 provides DNS name resolution, and CloudFront provides content delivery; none of them isolates networks."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"個人データの取り扱いで「データ所在地」を制御する手段はどれか。","o":["リージョンの選択","エッジの活用","CDNのキャッシュ","AZの追加増設"],"a":0,"e":"データの所在地は、リージョンを選ぶことで制御でき、規制への適合に使える。エッジの活用やCDNのキャッシュは配信を速める手段で、AZの追加増設は同じリージョン内の冗長化にすぎない。","qEn":"Which measure controls \"data residency\" when handling personal data?","oEn":["Choosing the Region","Using the edge","CDN caching","Adding more AZs"],"eEn":"Data residency is controlled by choosing the Region, which helps meet regulatory requirements. Using the edge and CDN caching speed up delivery, and adding AZs only provides redundancy within the same Region."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティイベントの通知・自動対応に使える組み合わせはどれか。","o":["VPC＋AWS Direct Connectによる専用線接続","Amazon S3＋Amazon CloudFrontによる静的配信","GuardDuty検出＋EventBridgeによる自動修復","Amazon RDS＋ElastiCacheによる高速化"],"a":2,"e":"GuardDutyが脅威を検出し、EventBridgeで自動修復を起動すれば、検知から対処までを自動化できる。Direct Connect、CloudFrontの静的配信、RDSとElastiCacheの高速化は、セキュリティイベントの対応ではない。","qEn":"Which combination can be used for notification and automated response to security events?","oEn":["VPC + dedicated-line connection with AWS Direct Connect","Amazon S3 + static delivery with Amazon CloudFront","GuardDuty findings + automated remediation with EventBridge","Amazon RDS + acceleration with ElastiCache"],"eEn":"If GuardDuty detects a threat and EventBridge triggers automated remediation, everything from detection to response can be automated. Direct Connect, static delivery with CloudFront, and acceleration with RDS and ElastiCache do not respond to security events."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"サーバーレスアーキテクチャの代表的な組み合わせはどれか。","o":["Elastic Beanstalk＋Amazon Aurora＋VPC","Lambda＋API Gateway＋DynamoDB","EC2＋Elastic Load Balancing＋RDS","Amazon ECS＋Amazon EBS＋Amazon S3"],"a":1,"e":"Lambda、API Gateway、DynamoDBは、サーバー管理が不要で自動スケールするサーバーレスの代表的な組み合わせである。EC2、Elastic Beanstalk、ECSを使う構成はサーバーやコンテナの運用が残る。","qEn":"Which is a typical combination for a serverless architecture?","eEn":"Lambda, API Gateway, and DynamoDB are a typical serverless combination that requires no server management and scales automatically. Configurations using EC2, Elastic Beanstalk, and ECS still require operating servers or containers."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"大量の静的コンテンツ配信に最適な組み合わせはどれか。","o":["AWS Lambda＋Amazon SQS（キュー）","S3（ホスティング）＋CloudFront（CDN）","Amazon RDS＋ElastiCache（キャッシュ）","EC2（Webサーバー）＋EBS（ストレージ）"],"a":1,"e":"S3でホスティングし、CloudFrontのエッジから配信すれば、静的コンテンツを高速かつ低コストで届けられる。LambdaとSQS、RDSとElastiCache、EC2とEBSの組み合わせは、静的配信の最適解ではない。","qEn":"Which combination is best for delivering large amounts of static content?","oEn":["AWS Lambda + Amazon SQS (queue)","S3 (hosting) + CloudFront (CDN)","Amazon RDS + ElastiCache (cache)","EC2 (web server) + EBS (storage)"],"eEn":"Hosting on S3 and delivering from CloudFront edge locations delivers static content quickly and at low cost. Lambda with SQS, RDS with ElastiCache, and EC2 with EBS are not the best fit for static delivery."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"障害時に別リージョンへ切り替えるルーティングを担うサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Auto Scaling（自動スケーリング）","Amazon Route 53（フェイルオーバールーティング）","Elastic Load Balancing（負荷分散）","Amazon CloudFront（エッジロケーションでのキャッシュ配信）"],"a":1,"e":"ヘルスチェック連動の切替。可用性の確保。","qEn":"Which service handles routing that switches to another Region during a failure?","oEn":["AWS Auto Scaling (automatic scaling)","Amazon Route 53 (failover routing)","Elastic Load Balancing (load balancing)","Amazon CloudFront (cached delivery from edge locations)"],"eEn":"Switchover driven by health checks. Ensures availability."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"EBS（Elastic Block Store）スナップショットの保存先はどれか。","o":["Amazon EFS（ファイルストレージ）","Amazon S3（内部的に保管）","インスタンスストア（一時領域）","Amazon Glacier専用の保管庫"],"a":1,"e":"EBSスナップショットは、増分バックアップとして内部的にAmazon S3に保管される。EFSはファイルストレージ、インスタンスストアは一時領域、Glacier専用の保管庫が保存先ではない。","qEn":"Where are EBS (Elastic Block Store) snapshots stored?","oEn":["Amazon EFS (file storage)","Amazon S3 (stored internally)","Instance store (temporary storage)","A dedicated Amazon Glacier vault"],"eEn":"EBS snapshots are incremental backups stored internally in Amazon S3. EFS is file storage, the instance store is temporary storage, and a dedicated Glacier vault is not where they are stored."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）インスタンスタイプを選ぶ際の主要な観点はどれか。","o":["選択するリージョンとアベイラビリティゾーンの物理的な位置","インスタンス名の色とサイズ表記の見やすさ","インスタンスの累計起動回数と課金の合計額","CPU・メモリ・ストレージ・ネットワーク性能のバランス"],"a":3,"e":"ワークロード適合の選択。コストと性能の両立。","qEn":"What is a key consideration when choosing an EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) instance type?","oEn":["The physical location of the selected Region and Availability Zone","The color of the instance name and the readability of its size notation","The instance's cumulative launch count and total billed amount","The balance of CPU, memory, storage, and network performance"],"eEn":"Choose to fit the workload. Balances cost and performance."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Batchが適するワークロードはどれか。","o":["常時稼働するWebサーバーの運用","大量のバッチコンピューティングジョブ","DNSの名前解決とルーティング","低レイテンシが求められるリアルタイム処理"],"a":1,"e":"ジョブの自動スケジューリング。リソースの最適配分。","qEn":"Which workload is AWS Batch suited for?","oEn":["Operating always-on web servers","Large numbers of batch computing jobs","DNS name resolution and routing","Real-time processing that requires low latency"],"eEn":"Automatic job scheduling. Optimal allocation of resources."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データレイクの中心的なストレージとして使われるサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Snowball","Amazon EFS","Amazon S3","Amazon FSx"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon S3は、大量のデータを低コストで集約でき、多様な分析の基盤になるため、データレイクの中心に使われる。AWS Snowballはデータ移送、EFSとFSxはファイルシステムで、データレイクの中核ではない。","qEn":"Which service is used as the central storage for a data lake?","eEn":"Amazon S3 can store large amounts of data at low cost and serves as the foundation for diverse analytics, so it is used at the center of a data lake. AWS Snowball transfers data, and EFS and FSx are file systems; none is the core of a data lake."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"サーバーレスでファイル変換などを自動実行する典型構成はどれか。","o":["Step Functions＋RDS","API Gateway＋EC2","ECS Fargate＋ALB","S3イベント＋Lambda"],"a":3,"e":"アップロード起点の自動処理。運用不要の実行。","qEn":"Which is a typical configuration that automatically runs tasks such as file conversion in a serverless way?","oEn":["Step Functions + RDS","API Gateway + EC2","ECS Fargate + ALB","S3 events + Lambda"],"eEn":"Automatic processing triggered by uploads. Runs with no operations work."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"グローバルなDynamoDBの複製機能はどれか。","o":["DynamoDB Accelerator","DynamoDBグローバルテーブル","DynamoDB Streams","クロスリージョンスナップショット"],"a":1,"e":"複数リージョンへの自動複製。低遅延アクセス。","qEn":"Which feature provides global replication for DynamoDB?","oEn":["DynamoDB Accelerator","DynamoDB global tables","DynamoDB Streams","Cross-Region snapshots"],"eEn":"Automatic replication to multiple Regions. Low-latency access."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ステートレスなWebサーバーのセッション情報を外部保持する適切な先はどれか。","o":["アプリサーバーのローカルメモリ","ElastiCacheやDynamoDB","Amazon S3 Glacier","各Webサーバーのローカルディスク"],"a":1,"e":"セッションの外部分離。水平スケールの実現。","qEn":"Where is the appropriate place to store session information externally for stateless web servers?","oEn":["The application server's local memory","ElastiCache or DynamoDB","Amazon S3 Glacier","Each web server's local disk"],"eEn":"Separate sessions externally. Enables horizontal scaling."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のマネージドメッセージブローカー（MQ互換）はどれか。","o":["Amazon SQS","Amazon SNS","Amazon MQ","Amazon MSK"],"a":2,"e":"標準プロトコル対応。既存アプリの移行支援。","qEn":"Which is the AWS managed message broker (MQ compatible)?","eEn":"Supports standard protocols. Helps migrate existing applications."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"IoTデバイスとクラウドを接続するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Kinesis","AWS IoT Analytics","AWS IoT Greengrass","AWS IoT Core"],"a":3,"e":"AWS IoT Coreは、IoTデバイスをクラウドに接続し、接続管理とデータ収集を担う。Kinesisはストリーミング処理、IoT Analyticsはデータ分析、IoT Greengrassはデバイス側で動くエッジ実行環境である。","qEn":"Which service connects IoT devices to the cloud?","eEn":"AWS IoT Core connects IoT devices to the cloud and handles connection management and data collection. Kinesis is for stream processing, IoT Analytics is for data analysis, and IoT Greengrass is an edge runtime that runs on the device side."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"レコメンデーションを機械学習で生成するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Personalize","Amazon Rekognition","Amazon Comprehend","Amazon SageMaker"],"a":0,"e":"個別化推薦の提供。エンゲージメント向上。（2026年11月時点：公式試験ガイド v1.3（2026年10月29日）は Amazon Personalize を出題範囲外のサービスに挙げている。再確認のうえ引用すること）","qEn":"Which service generates recommendations using machine learning?","eEn":"Provides personalized recommendations. Improves engagement. (As of November 2026: the official exam guide v1.3 (October 29, 2026) lists Amazon Personalize as an out-of-scope service. Verify before citing.)"},
  {"d":"D3","q":"複数AZ（Availability Zone）にまたがるRDS（Relational Database Service）構成が提供するものはどれか。","o":["複数リージョンへのリードレプリカ展開による読み取り分散","マルチAZ配置による高可用性と自動フェイルオーバー","保存データと転送中データの自動暗号化の適用","ストレージ容量の自動的な無制限スケーリング"],"a":1,"e":"自動フェイルオーバー。障害時の継続稼働。","qEn":"What does an RDS (Relational Database Service) configuration spanning multiple AZs (Availability Zones) provide?","oEn":["Read distribution through read replicas deployed across multiple Regions","High availability and automatic failover through Multi-AZ placement","Automatic encryption of data at rest and in transit","Automatic unlimited scaling of storage capacity"],"eEn":"Automatic failover. Continued operation during failures."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）サービスの上限（クォータ）を確認・引き上げ申請する仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Trusted Advisor","Amazon CloudWatch","Service Quotas","AWS Systems Manager"],"a":2,"e":"Service Quotasは、AWSサービスの上限を確認し、引き上げを申請する仕組みである。Trusted Advisorは構成の助言、CloudWatchは監視、Systems Managerは運用管理で、上限の申請窓口ではない。","qEn":"Which mechanism lets you check and request increases to AWS service limits (quotas)?","eEn":"Service Quotas lets you check AWS service limits and request increases. Trusted Advisor gives configuration advice, CloudWatch provides monitoring, and Systems Manager handles operations management; none is the place to request limits."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"開発者向けのクラウドIDE（統合開発環境）はどれか。","o":["AWS CodeBuild","AWS Cloud9","AWS CodeStar","AWS CodeCommit"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Cloud9は、ブラウザ上で使える開発者向けのクラウドIDEで、共同編集もできる。CodeBuildはビルド、CodeStarは開発の統合管理、CodeCommitはソース管理で、エディタ環境ではない。（2026年11月時点：AWS Cloud9 は新規顧客の受付を終了し、既存顧客のみ利用できる。公式試験ガイド v1.3 の出題範囲内・範囲外のどちらのリストにも Cloud9 は載っていない（旧版 v1.0 では範囲内）。再確認のうえ引用すること）","qEn":"Which is a cloud IDE (integrated development environment) for developers?","eEn":"AWS Cloud9 is a cloud IDE for developers that runs in the browser and supports collaborative editing. CodeBuild is for builds, CodeStar is for integrated management of development, and CodeCommit is for source control; none is an editor environment. (As of November 2026: AWS Cloud9 is no longer available to new customers; existing customers can keep using it. Cloud9 appears in neither the in-scope nor the out-of-scope list of exam guide v1.3 (it was in scope in the older v1.0 guide). Verify before citing.)"},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CI/CDのソース管理を担うサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CodePipeline","AWS CodeCommit","AWS CodeDeploy","AWS CodeBuild"],"a":1,"e":"Gitリポジトリの提供。ソースの集中管理。","qEn":"Which service handles source control in CI/CD?","eEn":"Provides Git repositories. Centralized management of source code."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ソースコードのビルドを自動化するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CodePipeline","AWS CodeCommit","AWS CodeBuild","AWS CodeDeploy"],"a":2,"e":"ビルド工程の自動化。スケーラブルな実行。","qEn":"Which service automates building source code?","eEn":"Automates the build process. Scalable execution."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"アプリのデプロイを自動化するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CodePipeline","AWS CodeCommit","AWS CodeBuild","AWS CodeDeploy"],"a":3,"e":"無停止デプロイの実現。ロールバック対応。（2026年11月時点：公式試験ガイド v1.3（2026年10月29日）は AWS CodeDeploy を出題範囲外のサービスに挙げている（旧版 v1.0 では出題範囲内）。再確認のうえ引用すること）","qEn":"Which service automates application deployment?","eEn":"Enables zero-downtime deployment. Supports rollback. (As of November 2026: the official exam guide v1.3 (October 29, 2026) lists AWS CodeDeploy as an out-of-scope service (it was in scope in the older v1.0 guide). Verify before citing.)"},
  {"d":"D3","q":"RDS（Relational Database Service）とDynamoDBの選択基準として正しいものはどれか。","o":["ミリ秒単位の低レイテンシが必要ならRDS、複雑なトランザクションならDynamoDB","アクセス頻度が高い場合はRDS、低い場合はDynamoDBを選択する","初期コストのみを基準として常に料金が安価な方のサービスを選択する","構造化・トランザクション重視ならRDS、高スケールのキー値ならDynamoDB"],"a":3,"e":"データモデルでの使い分け。要件適合の判断。","qEn":"Which statement correctly describes the criteria for choosing between RDS (Relational Database Service) and DynamoDB?","oEn":["Choose RDS if millisecond-level low latency is required, and DynamoDB for complex transactions","Choose RDS when access frequency is high and DynamoDB when it is low","Always choose whichever service is cheaper, based on initial cost alone","Choose RDS for structured, transaction-focused workloads and DynamoDB for high-scale key-value workloads"],"eEn":"Choose based on the data model. Judge by fit to requirements."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CloudFrontがオリジンとして指定できる代表例はどれか。","o":["DynamoDBテーブルのみ","Amazon RDSデータベースインスタンスのみ","S3バケットやELB、独自サーバー","プライベートVPCサブネットのみ"],"a":2,"e":"配信元の柔軟な指定。多様なオリジン対応。","qEn":"Which is a typical example of an origin that CloudFront can specify?","oEn":["DynamoDB tables only","Amazon RDS database instances only","S3 buckets, ELBs, or custom servers","Private VPC subnets only"],"eEn":"Flexible choice of the content source. Supports diverse origins."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"EFS（Elastic File System）とEBS（Elastic Block Store）の違いとして正しいものはどれか。","o":["EFSは共有ファイル、EBSは単一インスタンス用ブロック","EFSは自動でリージョン間レプリケーションを行う","EFSはブロックストレージ、EBSはオブジェクトストレージ","EFSは単一AZ専用、EBSは複数AZで共有可能"],"a":0,"e":"EFSは複数のインスタンスから共有できるファイルストレージで、EBSは単一インスタンス用のブロックストレージである。EFSをブロック型とする説明や、単一AZ専用とする説明、自動でリージョン間複製を行う説明は誤りである。","qEn":"Which statement correctly describes the difference between EFS (Elastic File System) and EBS (Elastic Block Store)?","oEn":["EFS is shared files; EBS is block storage for a single instance","EFS automatically replicates across Regions","EFS is block storage; EBS is object storage","EFS is limited to a single AZ; EBS can be shared across multiple AZs"],"eEn":"EFS is file storage that multiple instances can share, and EBS is block storage for a single instance. Describing EFS as block storage, as limited to a single AZ, or as automatically replicating across Regions is incorrect."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"動画のエンコード・配信処理に使う代表的サービス群はどれか。","o":["AWS Elemental（メディアサービス群）","AWS Glue（データ統合・ETLサービス）","Amazon Redshift（データウェアハウス）","Amazon Kinesis Video Streams"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Elementalは、動画のエンコードや配信処理を担うメディアサービス群である。Glueはデータ統合のETL、Redshiftはデータウェアハウス、Kinesis Video Streamsは映像のストリーム取り込みである。（2026年11月時点：公式試験ガイド v1.3（2026年10月29日）は AWS Elemental の各メディアサービス（MediaConvert・MediaLive など）を出題範囲外のサービスに挙げている。再確認のうえ引用すること）","qEn":"Which group of services is typically used for video encoding and delivery processing?","oEn":["AWS Elemental (media services)","AWS Glue (data integration and ETL service)","Amazon Redshift (data warehouse)","Amazon Kinesis Video Streams"],"eEn":"AWS Elemental is a group of media services that handle video encoding and delivery processing. Glue is ETL for data integration, Redshift is a data warehouse, and Kinesis Video Streams ingests video streams. (As of November 2026: the official exam guide v1.3 (October 29, 2026) lists the AWS Elemental media services (MediaConvert, MediaLive and others) as an out-of-scope service. Verify before citing.)"},
  {"d":"D3","q":"データベースの自動バックアップとポイントインタイム復元を提供するのはどれか。","o":["S3バージョニングとライフサイクル","Amazon RDSの自動バックアップ","EBSスナップショットの手動取得","DynamoDB Streamsによる変更キャプチャ"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon RDSの自動バックアップは、ポイントインタイム復元を提供し、任意の時点へDBを戻せる。S3バージョニングはオブジェクトの履歴、EBSスナップショットの手動取得は人の操作、DynamoDB Streamsは変更の取得である。","qEn":"Which provides automatic database backups and point-in-time recovery?","oEn":["S3 versioning and lifecycle","Amazon RDS automated backups","Manual EBS snapshots","Change capture with DynamoDB Streams"],"eEn":"Amazon RDS automated backups provide point-in-time recovery, letting you restore the DB to any point in time. S3 versioning keeps object history, manual EBS snapshots depend on human action, and DynamoDB Streams captures changes."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"オンプレからの大規模一括移行で回線が細い場合の最適手段はどれか。","o":["AWS DataSyncによるオンライン転送","Site-to-Site VPN接続の利用","AWS Direct Connectの新規敷設","AWS Snowball等の物理移送"],"a":3,"e":"ネットワーク制約の回避。安全な大容量移送。","qEn":"What is the best approach for a large-scale bulk migration from on-premises when the network line is narrow?","oEn":["Online transfer with AWS DataSync","Using a Site-to-Site VPN connection","Installing a new AWS Direct Connect line","Physical transfer such as AWS Snowball"],"eEn":"Avoids network constraints. Secure transfer of large volumes."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Lambdaの課金根拠となる要素はどれか。","o":["常時起動しているインスタンス時間","リクエスト数と実行時間（メモリ×時間）","割り当てたストレージの容量とIOPS","アウトバウンドのネットワーク転送量のみ"],"a":1,"e":"Lambdaの料金は、リクエスト数と実行時間(割り当てメモリ×時間)で決まり、使わないときは課金されない。常時起動のインスタンス時間、ストレージ容量とIOPS、転送量だけの課金は、Lambdaの課金根拠ではない。","qEn":"Which factors form the basis of AWS Lambda billing?","oEn":["Instance hours for always-running instances","Number of requests and execution time (memory x time)","Allocated storage capacity and IOPS","Outbound network transfer volume only"],"eEn":"Lambda pricing is based on the number of requests and execution time (allocated memory x time), and nothing is charged when it is not used. Always-on instance hours, storage capacity and IOPS, and transfer volume alone are not the basis of Lambda billing."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"CloudWatch Logsが担う役割はどれか。","o":["メトリクスの収集とダッシュボード表示","アプリやシステムのログ収集・保管・検索","API操作の履歴記録と監査証跡の一元的な提供","リソース構成の変更追跡と評価"],"a":1,"e":"CloudWatch Logsは、アプリやシステムのログを収集、保管、検索する役割を持つ。メトリクスの収集とダッシュボードはCloudWatchの別機能、API操作の記録はCloudTrail、構成の追跡はConfigである。","qEn":"What role does CloudWatch Logs play?","oEn":["Collecting metrics and displaying dashboards","Collecting, storing, and searching logs from applications and systems","Recording API operation history and providing a centralized audit trail","Tracking and evaluating resource configuration changes"],"eEn":"CloudWatch Logs collects, stores, and searches logs from applications and systems. Metrics collection and dashboards are separate CloudWatch features, API operation records are handled by CloudTrail, and configuration tracking is handled by Config."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"短時間の高負荷バッチに中断耐性があるとき最適な購入オプションはどれか。","o":["Savings Plans","スポットインスタンス","リザーブドインスタンス","オンデマンドインスタンス"],"a":1,"e":"短時間の高負荷バッチで中断に耐えられるなら、余剰容量を大幅な割引で使えるスポットインスタンスが最適である。Savings Plansとリザーブドインスタンスは長期契約向け、オンデマンドは割引がない。","qEn":"Which purchasing option is best for short-duration, high-load batch jobs that can tolerate interruption?","oEn":["Savings Plans","Spot Instances","Reserved Instances","On-Demand Instances"],"eEn":"For short, high-load batch jobs that can tolerate interruption, Spot Instances, which use spare capacity at a large discount, are the best fit. Savings Plans and Reserved Instances are for long-term commitments, and On-Demand has no discount."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"サーバーレスでイベント連携を構築する際のSQS（Simple Queue Service）とSNS（Simple Notification Service）の違いはどれか。","o":["SQSはキュー（プル型）、SNSは通知（プッシュ型）","両者ともにメッセージを永続化して順序を保証する","SQSはファンアウト通知、SNSはメッセージの一時保管","SQSは複数の購読者へ同時にプッシュ配信、SNSはプル型"],"a":0,"e":"非同期保管と即時配信の対比。用途の使い分け。","qEn":"What is the difference between SQS (Simple Queue Service) and SNS (Simple Notification Service) when building serverless event integration?","oEn":["SQS is a queue (pull); SNS is notification (push)","Both persist messages and guarantee ordering","SQS is fan-out notification; SNS is temporary message storage","SQS pushes to multiple subscribers at once; SNS is pull-based"],"eEn":"Contrast between asynchronous storage and immediate delivery. Use each for its own purpose."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"リソースのプロビジョニングをテンプレートで繰り返し可能にする利点はどれか。","o":["設定内容のブラックボックス化","構成の標準化と再現性（IaC）","個別の手作業による柔軟な設定変更","環境ごとに異なる構成の許容"],"a":1,"e":"テンプレートによるプロビジョニングは、構成を標準化して再現性を高める(IaC)。設定のブラックボックス化、個別の手作業による変更、環境ごとに異なる構成の許容は、テンプレート化の利点ではない。","qEn":"What is the benefit of making resource provisioning repeatable with templates?","oEn":["Making configuration contents a black box","Standardized and reproducible configurations (IaC)","Flexible changes through individual manual settings","Allowing different configurations in each environment"],"eEn":"Template-based provisioning standardizes configurations and improves reproducibility (IaC). Black-boxing settings, individual manual changes, and allowing different configurations per environment are not benefits of templating."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"キャッシュにより動的コンテンツも高速配信するCloudFrontの利点はどれか。","o":["全リクエストを単一リージョンに集約","オリジンとの物理的距離を拡大する","通信の暗号化を省略して高速化する","エッジでのキャッシュとオリジン負荷軽減"],"a":3,"e":"CloudFrontは、エッジでコンテンツをキャッシュして配信し、オリジンの負荷を減らす。全リクエストを単一リージョンに集約したり、オリジンとの距離を広げたり、暗号化を省いたりすることは利点ではない。","qEn":"What is the benefit of CloudFront, which caches content to deliver even dynamic content quickly?","oEn":["Consolidating all requests into a single Region","Increasing the physical distance to the origin","Skipping encryption of communications for speed","Caching at the edge and reducing load on the origin"],"eEn":"CloudFront caches and delivers content at the edge, reducing the load on the origin. Consolidating all requests into one Region, increasing the distance to the origin, or omitting encryption are not benefits."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）リソースの構成図を扱い設計レビューを効率化するのに役立つものはどれか。","o":["AWS Cost Explorerによる費用の可視化と予測","Trusted Advisorによる推奨事項の確認","CloudFormation設計やアーキテクチャ可視化","AWS Health Dashboardでの障害状況把握"],"a":2,"e":"CloudFormationでは構成をテンプレートとして記述でき、構成図のように可視化して設計レビューを効率化できる。Cost Explorerは費用、Trusted Advisorは推奨事項、Health Dashboardは障害状況の把握である。","qEn":"Which helps you work with architecture diagrams of AWS resources and make design reviews more efficient?","oEn":["Visualizing and forecasting costs with AWS Cost Explorer","Checking recommendations with Trusted Advisor","CloudFormation design and architecture visualization","Understanding outage status in the AWS Health Dashboard"],"eEn":"With CloudFormation you can describe a configuration as a template and visualize it like an architecture diagram, making design reviews more efficient. Cost Explorer covers costs, Trusted Advisor covers recommendations, and Health Dashboard covers outage status."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service）標準とS3 Glacierの選択基準として正しいものはどれか。","o":["コスト差はないので用途を問わず同一に扱う","アクセス頻度に関わらず常に標準を選ぶ","頻繁アクセスは標準、長期保管はGlacier","取り出し速度が最優先でも常にGlacierを選ぶ"],"a":2,"e":"アクセス頻度での使い分け。コスト最適化。","qEn":"Which statement correctly describes the criteria for choosing between S3 (Simple Storage Service) Standard and S3 Glacier?","oEn":["There is no cost difference, so treat them the same regardless of use","Always choose Standard regardless of access frequency","Standard for frequent access, Glacier for long-term storage","Always choose Glacier even when retrieval speed is the top priority"],"eEn":"Choose by access frequency. Cost optimization."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"VPC（Virtual Private Cloud）エンドポイントを使う主な利点はどれか。","o":["DNSの名前解決を高速化して遅延を減らす","インターネット経由での通信を高速化する","オンプレミスとの専用線接続を確立する","インターネットを経由せずAWSサービスへ閉域接続"],"a":3,"e":"VPCエンドポイントは、インターネットを経由せずにAWSサービスへ閉域で接続でき、攻撃面を小さくする。DNSの高速化、公開インターネット経由の高速化、専用線の確立は、VPCエンドポイントの目的ではない。","qEn":"What is the main benefit of using a VPC (Virtual Private Cloud) endpoint?","oEn":["Speeding up DNS name resolution to reduce latency","Speeding up communication over the public internet","Establishing a dedicated-line connection to on-premises","Private connectivity to AWS services without traversing the internet"],"eEn":"A VPC endpoint connects to AWS services privately without traversing the internet, reducing the attack surface. Faster DNS, faster communication over the public internet, and establishing a dedicated line are not the purpose of a VPC endpoint."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"24時間365日稼働の本番システムで予測可能な定常負荷に最もコスト効率の良い購入方式はどれか。","o":["スポットインスタンスによる大規模な並列処理","専有ホスト（Dedicated Hosts）予約","リザーブドインスタンスまたはSavings Plans","オンデマンドインスタンスのみによる従量課金運用"],"a":2,"e":"24時間365日動く予測可能な定常負荷には、長期コミットで割引を得られるリザーブドインスタンスやSavings Plansが最もコスト効率がよい。スポットは中断があり、オンデマンドのみの運用は割高になる。","qEn":"Which purchasing option is the most cost-efficient for a predictable steady-state load on a production system running 24/7?","oEn":["Large-scale parallel processing with Spot Instances","Long-term reservation of Dedicated Hosts","Reserved Instances or Savings Plans","Pay-as-you-go operation with On-Demand Instances only"],"eEn":"For a predictable steady-state load running 24/7, Reserved Instances or Savings Plans, which give discounts for a long-term commitment, are the most cost-efficient. Spot can be interrupted, and running on On-Demand only is more expensive."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"夜間にだけ実行する中断可能な解析ジョブに最適な購入方式はどれか。","o":["リザーブドインスタンス","Savings Plans","オンデマンドインスタンス","スポットインスタンス"],"a":3,"e":"夜間だけ動く中断可能な解析ジョブには、余剰容量を最大級の割引で使えるスポットインスタンスが最適である。リザーブドとSavings Plansは常時使う前提の割引で、オンデマンドは割引がない。","qEn":"Which purchasing option is best for an interruptible analysis job that runs only at night?","oEn":["Reserved Instances","Savings Plans","On-Demand Instances","Spot Instances"],"eEn":"For an interruptible analysis job that runs only at night, Spot Instances, which use spare capacity at the deepest discounts, are the best fit. Reserved Instances and Savings Plans are discounts that assume constant use, and On-Demand has no discount."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"部門別にクラウド費用を配賦したい場合に最適な手段はどれか。","o":["一括請求機能","コスト配分タグ","コストカテゴリ","請求ダッシュボード"],"a":1,"e":"部門別に費用を配賦するには、リソースにコスト配分タグを付けて集計する。一括請求は複数アカウントの請求を1つにまとめる機能、コストカテゴリはグループ化ルール、請求ダッシュボードは請求額の表示である。","qEn":"Which is the best way to allocate cloud costs by department?","oEn":["Consolidated billing","Cost allocation tags","Cost Categories","Billing dashboard"],"eEn":"To allocate costs by department, attach cost allocation tags to resources and aggregate by them. Consolidated billing combines the bills of multiple accounts into one, Cost Categories are grouping rules, and the billing dashboard displays billed amounts."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"ビジネスクリティカルなシステムの停止時に15分以内の応答と専任担当を求める場合に最適なサポートプランはどれか。","o":["エンタープライズサポート","開発者サポートプラン","ビジネスサポートプラン","ベーシックサポートプラン"],"a":0,"e":"エンタープライズサポートは、ビジネスクリティカルなシステムの停止に15分未満の応答目標を持ち（本番システムの停止は1時間未満）、専任のTAMが付く。ビジネス、開発者、ベーシックの各プランは、応答目標が長いか、専任担当が付かない。（2026年11月時点：DeveloperとBusinessは2027年1月1日に提供終了予定。現行の最上位はUnified Operationsで、専任TAMが付き、重大インシデントにはIncident Management Engineerが5分未満で応答する）","qEn":"Which support plan is best when you need a response within 15 minutes and a dedicated contact when a business-critical system is down?","oEn":["Enterprise Support","Developer Support plan","Business Support plan","Basic Support plan"],"eEn":"Enterprise Support has a target response time of under 15 minutes when a business-critical system is down (under 1 hour for a production system down) and comes with a dedicated TAM. The Business, Developer, and Basic plans have longer response targets or no dedicated contact. (As of November 2026: Developer and Business Support will be discontinued on January 1, 2027. The top plan is now Unified Operations, which includes a designated TAM, and an Incident Management Engineer responds to critical incidents in under 5 minutes.)"},
  {"d":"D4","q":"予算超過を事前に検知し通知を受けたい場合に最適な仕組みはどれか。","o":["Cost Explorer","AWS Budgets","コスト使用状況レポート","Trusted Advisor"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Budgetsは、予算のしきい値を設定し、超過を事前に検知して通知する。Cost Explorerは傾向の分析、コスト使用状況レポートは詳細データの出力、Trusted Advisorはベストプラクティスの助言である。","qEn":"Which mechanism is best for detecting budget overruns in advance and receiving notifications?","oEn":["Cost Explorer","AWS Budgets","Cost and Usage Report","Trusted Advisor"],"eEn":"AWS Budgets lets you set budget thresholds, detect overruns in advance, and send notifications. Cost Explorer analyzes trends, the Cost and Usage Report outputs detailed data, and Trusted Advisor gives best-practice advice."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"過去の利用傾向を分析し将来コストを予測したい場合に最適なツールはどれか。","o":["AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Budgetsのアラート","Cost and Usage Report"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Cost Explorerは、過去の利用傾向を可視化し、将来のコストを予測する。Pricing Calculatorは利用前の見積もり、Budgetsのアラートは超過の通知、Cost and Usage Reportは詳細データの出力である。","qEn":"Which tool is best for analyzing past usage trends and forecasting future costs?","oEn":["AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Budgets alerts","Cost and Usage Report"],"eEn":"AWS Cost Explorer visualizes past usage trends and forecasts future costs. Pricing Calculator provides estimates before use, Budgets alerts notify of overruns, and the Cost and Usage Report outputs detailed data."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のコンプライアンス報告書を監査対応で取得したい場合に最適なサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CloudTrail","AWS Artifact","AWS Config","AWS Security Hub"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Artifactは、コンプライアンス報告書や監査資料をオンデマンドで取得でき、監査対応に使う。CloudTrailは操作ログ、AWS Configは構成の記録、Security Hubは検出結果の集約で、報告書の入手先ではない。","qEn":"Which service is best for obtaining AWS compliance reports for audit purposes?","eEn":"AWS Artifact provides compliance reports and audit materials on demand for audit purposes. CloudTrail provides operation logs, AWS Config records configurations, and Security Hub aggregates findings; none is a source for reports."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"想定外のコスト急増を自動検知したい場合に最適な機能はどれか。","o":["AWS Cost Anomaly Detection","AWS Cost Explorerでの傾向分析","AWS Budgetsのしきい値アラート","Cost and Usage Report（CUR）の集計"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Cost Anomaly Detectionは、想定外のコスト急増を機械学習で自動検知して通知する。Cost Explorerは傾向分析、Budgetsは設定したしきい値のアラート、CURは詳細データの集計で、自動検知ではない。","qEn":"Which feature is best for automatically detecting unexpected cost spikes?","oEn":["AWS Cost Anomaly Detection","Trend analysis in AWS Cost Explorer","Threshold alerts in AWS Budgets","Aggregation in the Cost and Usage Report (CUR)"],"eEn":"AWS Cost Anomaly Detection uses machine learning to automatically detect and notify of unexpected cost spikes. Cost Explorer analyzes trends, Budgets alerts on thresholds you set, and the CUR aggregates detailed data; none is automatic detection."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"過剰スペックのインスタンスを見直し費用を下げたい場合に最適な手法はどれか。","o":["リザーブドインスタンスによる前払い購入枠の拡大","ライトサイジング（Compute Optimizer活用）","オンデマンドキャパシティ予約による容量の追加確保","より大きいインスタンスタイプへ変更するスケールアップによる増強"],"a":1,"e":"過剰スペックのインスタンスは、Compute Optimizerなどで適正なサイズへ見直すライトサイジングで費用を下げる。リザーブドの前払い拡大、容量予約の追加、より大きいインスタンスへのスケールアップは費用を増やす方向である。","qEn":"Which approach is best for reviewing over-provisioned instances to reduce costs?","oEn":["Expanding upfront purchase capacity with Reserved Instances","Rightsizing (using Compute Optimizer)","Securing additional capacity with On-Demand Capacity Reservations","Scaling up by changing to a larger instance type"],"eEn":"Over-provisioned instances are reviewed and resized appropriately with rightsizing, using tools such as Compute Optimizer, to reduce costs. Expanding upfront Reserved Instance purchases, adding capacity reservations, and scaling up to larger instances all increase costs."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"新規アカウントを統制ルール付きで標準展開したい大企業に最適な仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Configによる構成監査","AWS IAM Identity Center","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Control Tower"],"a":3,"e":"ガードレール付き整備。ガバナンスの確立。","qEn":"Which mechanism is best for a large enterprise that wants to deploy new accounts in a standard way with governance rules?","oEn":["Configuration auditing with AWS Config","AWS IAM Identity Center","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Control Tower"],"eEn":"Set up with guardrails. Establishes governance."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"複数アカウントの請求を統合しボリューム割引を得たい場合に最適な仕組みはどれか。","o":["AWS Cost Explorerでの費用分析","AWS Organizationsの一括請求","リザーブドインスタンスの一括購入割引","AWS Budgetsによる予算アラート"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Organizationsの一括請求は、複数アカウントの使用量を合算し、ボリューム割引を共有できる。Cost Explorerは費用分析、リザーブドの割引は購入方式、Budgetsは予算アラートで、請求を統合する機能ではない。","qEn":"Which mechanism is best for combining the billing of multiple accounts to obtain volume discounts?","oEn":["Cost analysis with AWS Cost Explorer","Consolidated billing in AWS Organizations","Bulk purchase discounts on Reserved Instances","Budget alerts with AWS Budgets"],"eEn":"Consolidated billing in AWS Organizations combines usage across multiple accounts so volume discounts can be shared. Cost Explorer analyzes costs, Reserved Instance discounts are a purchasing option, and Budgets provides budget alerts; none combines billing."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リソースの最適化推奨（適正サイズ）を提供するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Trusted Advisor","AWS Compute Optimizer","AWS Cost Anomaly Detection","Amazon CloudWatch"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Compute Optimizerは、利用実績から適正サイズを推奨し、コストと性能の過不足を是正する。Trusted Advisorは広い範囲の助言、Cost Anomaly Detectionは異常支出の検知、CloudWatchは監視である。","qEn":"Which service provides optimization recommendations (rightsizing) for resources?","eEn":"AWS Compute Optimizer recommends right sizes based on actual usage and corrects over- or under-provisioning in cost and performance. Trusted Advisor gives advice across a broad range, Cost Anomaly Detection detects abnormal spending, and CloudWatch provides monitoring."}];

var SET4 = [
  {"d":"D1","q":"オンプレTCOが3年で900万円、AWS（Amazon Web Services）移行後が3年で540万円の場合、削減率はいくらか。","o":["33%","45%","約40%","36%"],"a":2,"e":"削減額360万円÷900万円＝40%。総保有コストでの比較。","qEn":"If the on-premises TCO is 9 million yen over 3 years and the TCO after migrating to AWS is 5.4 million yen over 3 years, what is the percentage reduction?","eEn":"Savings of 3.6 million yen / 9 million yen = 40%. A comparison of total cost of ownership."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"単一AZ（Availability Zone）構成のリスクとして正しいものはどれか。","o":["そのAZ障害でのサービス全停止","ストレージ容量の上限に達する","他リージョンへの自動フェイルオーバー","データが自動的に複数AZへ複製される"],"a":0,"e":"単一AZ構成では、そのAZに障害が起きるとサービス全体が停止する。他リージョンへの自動フェイルオーバーや複数AZへの自動複製は、単一AZ構成にはない利点で、容量の上限とは別の話である。","qEn":"Which statement correctly describes the risk of a single-AZ (Availability Zone) configuration?","oEn":["The whole service stops if that AZ fails","The storage capacity limit is reached","Automatic failover to another Region","Data is automatically replicated across multiple AZs"],"eEn":"In a single-AZ configuration, if that AZ fails, the entire service stops. Automatic failover to another Region and automatic replication across multiple AZs are benefits a single-AZ configuration does not have, and a capacity limit is a separate matter."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの「セルフサービス」が示す調達方法はどれか。","o":["AWSサポートへの申請による調達","利用者自身による即時のリソース取得","営業担当との契約手続きを経た調達","管理者の承認ワークフローを通じた取得"],"a":1,"e":"承認待ちの排除。コンソール・APIでの操作。","qEn":"Which procurement method does cloud \"self-service\" refer to?","oEn":["Procurement by submitting a request to AWS Support","Immediate acquisition of resources by the users themselves","Procurement through a contract process with a sales representative","Acquisition through an administrator approval workflow"],"eEn":"No waiting for approval. Operated through the console and APIs."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"弾力的なリソース運用がコストへ及ぼす効果はどれか。","o":["需要に合わせた支出の最適化","初期投資の増加と長期契約","使用量に関係なく一定の固定料金","ピーク需要に合わせた容量の常時確保"],"a":0,"e":"弾力的な運用は、需要に合わせてリソースを増減でき、支出を最適化できる。初期投資の増加と長期契約、使用量に関係ない固定料金、ピークに合わせた常時の確保は、弾力性と逆のコスト構造である。","qEn":"What is the effect of elastic resource operation on costs?","oEn":["Optimizing spending to match demand","Higher upfront investment and long-term contracts","A fixed fee regardless of usage","Always reserving capacity for peak demand"],"eEn":"Elastic operation lets you scale resources up and down with demand and optimize spending. Higher upfront investment with long-term contracts, a fixed fee regardless of usage, and always reserving capacity for peak are cost structures opposite to elasticity."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウド移行の「リテイン（Retain）」が指すものはどれか。","o":["既存資産を廃止する判断","別のクラウドへ移設する判断","当面オンプレに残す判断","アプリを完全に再構築する判断"],"a":2,"e":"リテイン(Retain)は、移行の優先度が低い資産を当面オンプレミスに残す判断を指す。廃止はリタイア、別クラウドへの移設はリロケートなどの別の手法、完全な再構築はリファクタリングである。","qEn":"What does \"Retain\" refer to in cloud migration?","oEn":["A decision to decommission existing assets","A decision to move to another cloud","A decision to keep it on-premises for now","A decision to completely rebuild the application"],"eEn":"Retain refers to the decision to keep low-priority assets on-premises for the time being. Decommissioning is Retire, moving to another cloud is a different strategy such as Relocate, and a complete rebuild is Refactor."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の責任範囲に含まれるインフラ管理の例はどれか。","o":["物理ハードウェアとデータセンターの運用","アプリケーションデータの暗号化設定","IAMによるユーザーアクセス権の管理","ゲストOS上のミドルウェアへのパッチ適用"],"a":0,"e":"ネットワーク基盤の維持。利用者の管理外。","qEn":"Which is an example of infrastructure management within the scope of AWS responsibility?","oEn":["Operating physical hardware and data centers","Configuring encryption of application data","Managing user access permissions with IAM","Applying patches to middleware on the guest OS"],"eEn":"Maintaining the network infrastructure. Outside the customer's control."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウド設計の原則「需要に応じてスケールする」の前提条件はどれか。","o":["コンポーネント間の密な依存関係","ステートレスかつ疎結合な構成","各サーバーが状態を保持する構成","単一の大型サーバーへの集約"],"a":1,"e":"水平拡張の容易さ。自動スケールへの適合。","qEn":"Which is a prerequisite for the cloud design principle \"scale in response to demand\"?","oEn":["Tight dependencies between components","A stateless, loosely coupled architecture","An architecture where each server holds state","Consolidation onto a single large server"],"eEn":"Easy horizontal scaling. Fits automatic scaling."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドでの「実験の失敗コスト」が下がる理由はどれか。","o":["不要になったリソースの即時削除","物理サーバーの事前購入と保有","使わなくても発生する固定費の安定性","長期契約による割引の適用"],"a":0,"e":"短期利用での試行が可能。低リスクな検証。","qEn":"Why does the cost of \"failed experiments\" go down in the cloud?","oEn":["Immediate deletion of resources that are no longer needed","Purchasing and owning physical servers in advance","Stable fixed costs incurred even when unused","Applying discounts through long-term contracts"],"eEn":"Short-term trials are possible. Low-risk validation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"デプロイの自動化が品質に与える効果はどれか。","o":["環境ごとの構成のばらつき増大","デプロイ手順が担当者に依存する","手作業による構成ドリフトの発生","人的ミスの削減と再現性の確保"],"a":3,"e":"デプロイの自動化は、人的ミスを減らし、再現性を確保して品質を高める。環境ごとの構成のばらつきの増大、担当者への手順の依存、手作業による構成ドリフトは、自動化されていない場合に起きる問題である。","qEn":"What effect does automating deployment have on quality?","oEn":["Greater variation in configuration between environments","Deployment procedures depend on the person in charge","Configuration drift caused by manual work","Fewer human errors and ensured reproducibility"],"eEn":"Deployment automation improves quality by reducing human errors and ensuring reproducibility. Greater variation between environments, procedures depending on the person in charge, and configuration drift from manual work are problems that occur without automation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の料金が継続的に下がってきた主因はどれか。","o":["利用者数の減少に伴う需要の大幅な縮小","規模の経済と運用効率化による還元","競合他社の撤退による独占化","データセンター設備の老朽化"],"a":1,"e":"利用者増加による単価低下。値下げの繰り返し。","qEn":"What is the main reason AWS prices have continued to fall?","oEn":["A sharp contraction in demand as the number of users declines","Passing on savings from economies of scale and operational efficiency","Monopolization after competitors withdrew","Aging of data center equipment"],"eEn":"Unit costs fall as the number of users grows. Repeated price reductions."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"高可用性を高める最も直接的な設計はどれか。","o":["単一サーバーのスペック増強","冗長化による単一障害点の排除","複数AZから単一AZへの集約","利用リージョン数の削減"],"a":1,"e":"複数AZでの構成。一部故障時の継続稼働。","qEn":"Which design most directly improves high availability?","oEn":["Increasing the specifications of a single server","Eliminating single points of failure through redundancy","Consolidating from multiple AZs into a single AZ","Reducing the number of Regions used"],"eEn":"Configuration across multiple AZs. Continued operation when part of the system fails."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Well-Architected Frameworkの「信頼性の柱」が要求するものはどれか。","o":["常時の手動運用と監視","垂直スケールのみへの依存","単一構成の固定と据え置き","自動復旧と水平スケール"],"a":3,"e":"信頼性の柱は、障害から自動で復旧し、水平スケールで需要の変化に対応することを求める。常時の手動運用と監視、垂直スケールのみへの依存、単一構成の固定と据え置きは、信頼性を下げる設計である。","qEn":"What does the \"Reliability pillar\" of the AWS Well-Architected Framework require?","oEn":["Constant manual operations and monitoring","Reliance on vertical scaling only","Fixing and leaving a single configuration unchanged","Automatic recovery and horizontal scaling"],"eEn":"The Reliability pillar calls for recovering automatically from failures and responding to changes in demand through horizontal scaling. Constant manual operations and monitoring, reliance on vertical scaling only, and fixing a single configuration unchanged are designs that reduce reliability."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの「グローバルリーチ」を活用する代表的サービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon EC2（単一AZ配置）","オンプレミスのデータベース","Amazon EBS（ブロックストレージ）","CloudFront（エッジ配信）"],"a":3,"e":"ユーザー近傍からの配信。レイテンシー削減。","qEn":"Which is a typical service that takes advantage of the cloud's \"global reach\"?","oEn":["Amazon EC2 (single-AZ placement)","An on-premises database","Amazon EBS (block storage)","CloudFront (edge delivery)"],"eEn":"Delivery from close to users. Reduces latency."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） CAF（Cloud Adoption Framework）の「プラットフォームパースペクティブ」が扱う領域はどれか。","o":["投資対効果の分析とビジネス価値の実証","クラウド環境とアーキテクチャの構築・運用基盤","組織の人材育成とクラウド文化の醸成","リスク管理とコンプライアンス統制の徹底"],"a":1,"e":"CAFのプラットフォームパースペクティブは、クラウド環境とアーキテクチャの構築・運用基盤を扱う。投資対効果の分析はビジネス、人材育成と文化はピープル、リスクとコンプライアンスはガバナンスの領域である。","qEn":"Which area does the \"Platform perspective\" of the AWS CAF (Cloud Adoption Framework) cover?","oEn":["Return-on-investment analysis and quantitative demonstration of business value","The foundation for building and operating cloud environments and architectures","Developing the organization's people and fostering a cloud culture","Rigorous risk management and compliance control"],"eEn":"The CAF Platform perspective covers the foundation for building and operating cloud environments and architectures. Return-on-investment analysis falls under Business, people development and culture under People, and risk and compliance under Governance."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） CAF（Cloud Adoption Framework）の「オペレーションパースペクティブ」が扱う領域はどれか。","o":["暗号鍵とアクセス権限の管理","従業員のスキル育成と組織変革","サービスの運用・監視・継続的改善","投資判断とビジネス価値の継続的な正当化"],"a":2,"e":"CAFのオペレーションパースペクティブは、サービスの運用、監視、継続的な改善を扱う。暗号鍵とアクセス権限はセキュリティ、スキル育成と組織変革はピープル、投資判断はビジネスやガバナンスの領域である。","qEn":"Which area does the \"Operations perspective\" of the AWS CAF (Cloud Adoption Framework) cover?","oEn":["Management of encryption keys and access permissions","Employee skill development and organizational change","Operating, monitoring, and continuously improving services","Investment decisions and ongoing justification of business value"],"eEn":"The CAF Operations perspective covers operating, monitoring, and continuously improving services. Encryption keys and access permissions fall under Security, skill development and organizational change under People, and investment decisions under Business or Governance."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"複数リージョン構成が主に高めるシステム特性はどれか。","o":["災害復旧能力と広域可用性","単一AZ内での処理性能","ネットワークのレイテンシー削減","ストレージの単価の低下"],"a":0,"e":"複数リージョン構成は、リージョン全体の障害に備え、災害復旧能力と広域の可用性を高める。単一AZ内の処理性能やストレージ単価の低下は直接の効果ではなく、レイテンシー削減は主目的ではない。","qEn":"Which system characteristic is mainly improved by a multi-Region configuration?","oEn":["Disaster recovery capability and wide-area availability","Processing performance within a single AZ","Reduced network latency","Lower storage unit prices"],"eEn":"A multi-Region configuration prepares for a failure of an entire Region and improves disaster recovery capability and wide-area availability. Processing performance within a single AZ and lower storage unit prices are not direct effects, and reducing latency is not the main purpose."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"「キャパシティの推測が不要」になることが直接もたらす効果はどれか。","o":["長期予約による容量固定","過剰調達や不足の回避","物理的な予備機材の購入","固定容量の事前確定"],"a":1,"e":"キャパシティを推測しなくてよいと、需要に応じて増減でき、過剰調達や不足を避けられる。長期予約による容量固定、物理的な予備機材の購入、固定容量の事前確定は、推測が必要な従来のやり方である。","qEn":"What is the direct effect of no longer having to \"guess capacity\"?","oEn":["Fixing capacity through long-term reservations","Avoiding over-provisioning and shortages","Purchasing spare physical equipment","Determining fixed capacity in advance"],"eEn":"When you do not have to guess capacity, you can scale up and down with demand and avoid over-provisioning and shortages. Fixing capacity through long-term reservations, buying spare physical equipment, and determining fixed capacity in advance are traditional approaches that require guessing."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドのデプロイで「使い捨て可能なリソース」を前提にする利点はどれか。","o":["構成ドリフトの許容と蓄積","手作業による柔軟な個別修正","サーバー個体への設定作り込み","不変インフラによる構成の一貫性"],"a":3,"e":"問題のあるリソースの即時置換。手作業修正の回避。","qEn":"What is the benefit of assuming \"disposable resources\" in cloud deployments?","oEn":["Tolerating and accumulating configuration drift","Flexible individual fixes made manually","Crafting settings into individual servers","Consistent configuration through immutable infrastructure"],"eEn":"Problem resources are replaced immediately. Avoids manual fixes."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウド導入で「ガバナンス」を扱うCAF（Cloud Adoption Framework）の観点はどれか。","o":["セキュリティパースペクティブ","ガバナンスパースペクティブ","ビジネスパースペクティブ","オペレーションパースペクティブ"],"a":1,"e":"リスク・コンプライアンスの統制。投資の最適化。","qEn":"Which CAF (Cloud Adoption Framework) perspective addresses \"governance\" in cloud adoption?","oEn":["Security perspective","Governance perspective","Business perspective","Operations perspective"],"eEn":"Control of risk and compliance. Optimization of investment."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"オンプレと比べたクラウドの俊敏性の価値はどれか。","o":["長期契約による調達の固定化","固定資産の増加と減価償却","物理保守作業の継続的な負担","調達期間の短縮による機会創出"],"a":3,"e":"クラウドの俊敏性は、調達期間が短くなり、新しい機会を素早くつかめる価値を生む。長期契約による調達の固定化、固定資産の増加と減価償却、物理保守の負担は、オンプレミス側の特徴である。","qEn":"What is the value of cloud agility compared with on-premises?","oEn":["Fixed procurement through long-term contracts","More fixed assets and depreciation","An ongoing burden of physical maintenance work","Creating opportunities through shorter procurement times"],"eEn":"Cloud agility creates value by shortening procurement time and letting you seize new opportunities quickly. Fixed procurement through long-term contracts, more fixed assets and depreciation, and the burden of physical maintenance are characteristics of on-premises."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの「自動復旧」設計が要求するものはどれか。","o":["予備系を常時停止しておく設計","手作業による復旧介入の徹底","障害時も単一構成を維持する","障害検知と自動的な置換の仕組み"],"a":3,"e":"自動復旧の設計は、障害を検知し、自動的に置き換える仕組みを求める。予備系を常時停止しておく、手作業による復旧介入の徹底、障害時も単一構成を維持する運用は、復旧に時間がかかる設計である。","qEn":"What does a cloud \"automatic recovery\" design require?","oEn":["Keeping standby systems permanently stopped","Relying thoroughly on manual recovery intervention","Operations that keep a single configuration even during failures","A mechanism for detecting failures and automatically replacing resources"],"eEn":"An automatic recovery design requires a mechanism that detects failures and replaces resources automatically. Keeping standby systems permanently stopped, relying thoroughly on manual recovery intervention, and keeping a single configuration during failures are designs that make recovery slow."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの「俊敏性」が新規事業の検証に向く理由はどれか。","o":["大規模な初期投資が前提となる","低コストで素早く試せる環境","物理機材の調達と設置が必要","長期契約による利用の保証"],"a":1,"e":"クラウドの俊敏性により、新規事業を低コストで素早く試せ、失敗時の損失も小さくできる。大規模な初期投資、物理機材の調達と設置、長期契約は、検証のハードルを上げる要因である。","qEn":"Why does cloud \"agility\" suit validating a new business?","oEn":["It requires a large upfront investment","An environment where you can try things quickly at low cost","It requires procuring and installing physical equipment","Usage is guaranteed through long-term contracts"],"eEn":"Cloud agility lets you try a new business quickly at low cost and keep losses small if it fails. A large upfront investment, procuring and installing physical equipment, and long-term contracts raise the barrier to validation."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の「世界規模のネットワーク」が支えるサービス特性はどれか。","o":["単一地域内のみに限定された低速通信","オンプレミス回線への依存","拠点間の低速な相互接続","高速かつ安定したグローバル通信"],"a":3,"e":"AWSの世界規模のネットワークは、拠点間を高速で安定して結び、低遅延のグローバル通信を支える。単一地域内の低速通信、オンプレミス回線への依存、拠点間の低速な相互接続は、その特性と逆である。","qEn":"Which service characteristic is supported by the AWS \"global network\"?","oEn":["Slow communication limited to a single area","Dependence on on-premises lines","Slow interconnection between sites","Fast and stable global communication"],"eEn":"The AWS global network connects sites quickly and reliably and supports low-latency global communication. Slow communication within a single area, dependence on on-premises lines, and slow interconnection between sites are the opposite of this characteristic."},
  {"d":"D1","q":"クラウドのスケーラビリティが「予測困難な需要」に強い理由はどれか。","o":["容量の事前確定と固定","長期予約による容量確保","需要発生時の即時拡張","物理機材の調達待ち"],"a":2,"e":"クラウドのスケーラビリティは、需要が発生した時点で即座に拡張でき、予測困難な需要に強い。容量の事前確定、長期予約による容量確保、物理機材の調達待ちは、急な需要増に間に合わない。","qEn":"Why is cloud scalability well suited to \"unpredictable demand\"?","oEn":["Fixing capacity in advance","Securing capacity through long-term reservations","Immediate expansion when demand arises","Waiting for physical equipment to be procured"],"eEn":"Cloud scalability can expand immediately when demand arises, so it handles unpredictable demand well. Fixing capacity in advance, securing capacity through long-term reservations, and waiting for physical equipment cannot keep up with sudden demand increases."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）が第三者機関の監査を受ける目的はどれか。","o":["利用料金の請求内容の透明化","サービス性能とスループットの継続的な向上","コンプライアンス準拠の客観的証明","管理コンソールの操作性の改善"],"a":2,"e":"AWSが第三者機関の監査を受けるのは、コンプライアンスへの準拠を客観的に証明するためである。料金の透明化、性能の向上、管理コンソールの操作性の改善は、第三者監査の目的ではない。","qEn":"What is the purpose of AWS undergoing audits by third-party organizations?","oEn":["Making billing details transparent","Continuously improving service performance and throughput","Objective proof of compliance","Improving the usability of the management console"],"eEn":"AWS undergoes third-party audits to objectively prove its compliance. Transparent billing, better performance, and a more usable management console are not the purposes of third-party audits."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の「セキュリティのベストプラクティス」で推奨される認証強化はどれか。","o":["すべての特権ユーザーへのMFA適用","長期的なアクセスキーの共有と再利用","全ユーザーで共通パスワードの使用","ルートユーザーのアクセスキーの常用"],"a":0,"e":"セキュリティのベストプラクティスでは、すべての特権ユーザーにMFAを適用し、不正アクセスを防ぐ。長期的なアクセスキーの共有、共通パスワードの使用、ルートユーザーのアクセスキーの常用は、推奨されない。","qEn":"Which authentication hardening is recommended in AWS \"security best practices\"?","oEn":["Applying MFA to all privileged users","Sharing and reusing long-term access keys","Using a common password for all users","Routine use of the root user's access keys"],"eEn":"Security best practices apply MFA to all privileged users to prevent unauthorized access. Sharing long-term access keys, using a common password, and routinely using the root user's access keys are not recommended."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"データを完全に消去する際にKMS（Key Management Service）で行う操作はどれか。","o":["暗号鍵の削除によるデータの無効化","スナップショットの取得と保管","CloudTrailログの完全な削除","S3バケットの非公開化の設定"],"a":0,"e":"暗号鍵を削除すれば、その鍵で暗号化したデータは復号できなくなり、データを無効化できる。スナップショットの取得、CloudTrailログの削除、S3バケットの非公開化では、データ自体は消えない。","qEn":"Which operation is performed in KMS (Key Management Service) when you want to completely erase data?","oEn":["Invalidating data by deleting the encryption key","Taking and keeping snapshots","Completely deleting CloudTrail logs","Making the S3 bucket private"],"eEn":"Deleting the encryption key makes data encrypted with that key impossible to decrypt, effectively invalidating the data. Taking snapshots, deleting CloudTrail logs, or making an S3 bucket private does not erase the data itself."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） WAF（Web Application Firewall）とShieldの組み合わせが守る主な脅威はどれか。","o":["電源設備の故障による突然のサービス停止","データセンターへの物理的な侵入行為","WebアプリへのDDoSおよびレイヤー7攻撃","内部の従業員による誤操作や意図しない設定ミス"],"a":2,"e":"WAFとShieldの組み合わせは、WebアプリへのDDoSとレイヤー7攻撃を防ぐ。電源設備の故障やデータセンターへの物理的な侵入はAWSの施設の対策で、従業員の誤操作や設定ミスにはIAMや監査で備える。","qEn":"Which main threats does the combination of AWS WAF (Web Application Firewall) and Shield protect against?","oEn":["Sudden service outages caused by power equipment failure","Physical intrusion into data centers","DDoS and layer 7 attacks on web applications","Mistaken operations or unintended misconfigurations by internal employees"],"eEn":"The combination of WAF and Shield protects web applications against DDoS and layer 7 attacks. Power equipment failures and physical intrusion into data centers are handled by AWS facility measures, and employee mistakes and misconfigurations are addressed with IAM and auditing."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"IAM（Identity and Access Management）ポリシーの評価で「明示的な許可がない場合」の既定動作はどれか。","o":["条件付きの許可","明示的な許可","暗黙的な許可","暗黙的な拒否"],"a":3,"e":"IAMは評価の既定が暗黙的な拒否で、Allowが明示された場合にだけアクセスが通る。「暗黙的な許可」という既定は存在せず、「明示的な許可」は許可が書かれた状態であり、許可がない場合の動作ではない。","qEn":"What is the default behavior in IAM (Identity and Access Management) policy evaluation when there is \"no explicit allow\"?","oEn":["Conditional allow","Explicit allow","Implicit allow","Implicit deny"],"eEn":"The default in IAM evaluation is an implicit deny, and access is granted only when an Allow is explicitly stated. There is no \"implicit allow\" default, and an \"explicit allow\" is the state where an allow is written, not the behavior when there is none."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のコンプライアンス責任分担で「クラウド本体の認証取得」を担う主体はどれか。","o":["監査法人","AWS","利用者","第三者"],"a":1,"e":"クラウド基盤そのものの安全性はAWSの責任で、データセンターやサービスの第三者認証はAWSが取得する。利用者が担うのは自分のアプリの準拠で、「監査法人」は審査する側であり認証の取得主体ではない。","qEn":"In the AWS compliance responsibility split, who is responsible for \"obtaining certifications for the cloud itself\"?","oEn":["Audit firm","AWS","Customer","Third party"],"eEn":"The security of the cloud infrastructure itself is AWS's responsibility, and AWS obtains third-party certifications for its data centers and services. The customer is responsible for the compliance of their own applications, and an \"audit firm\" is the party that audits, not the one that obtains certifications."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"「データの所有権は利用者にある」原則が示すものはどれか。","o":["第三者ベンダーによる一元管理","AWSによるデータへの自由なアクセス","利用者によるデータの完全な管理権","AWSと利用者による共同所有"],"a":2,"e":"AWSは無断アクセスせず。暗号化と削除の制御。","qEn":"What does the principle \"the customer owns their data\" indicate?","oEn":["Centralized management by a third-party vendor","Free access to data by AWS","Full control of the data by the customer","Joint ownership by AWS and the customer"],"eEn":"AWS does not access data without authorization. The customer controls encryption and deletion."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）のセキュリティで「自動でセキュリティ更新が適用される」マネージドサービスの利点はどれか。","o":["脆弱性対応の自動化","ライセンスの自己管理","設定自由度の最大化","物理サーバーの占有"],"a":0,"e":"マネージドサービスでは基盤のパッチ適用や更新をAWSが行うため、脆弱性対応が自動化される。「ライセンスの自己管理」は利用者の負担が増える側の話で、「物理サーバーの占有」は専有ホストの特徴でありマネージドの利点ではない。","qEn":"What is the benefit of managed services in AWS security, where \"security updates are applied automatically\"?","oEn":["Automated vulnerability remediation","Self-management of licenses","Maximum configuration flexibility","Exclusive use of physical servers"],"eEn":"In managed services, AWS applies patches and updates to the underlying platform, so vulnerability remediation is automated. \"Self-management of licenses\" adds to the customer's burden, and \"exclusive use of physical servers\" is a characteristic of Dedicated Hosts, not a benefit of managed services."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Macieが主に対象とするデータストアはどれか。","o":["S3","EFS","EBS","RDS"],"a":0,"e":"Macieは機械学習でS3バケット内の個人情報などの機密データを検出し、分類してアラートを出す。EFSやEBS、RDSは対象のデータストアではない。","qEn":"Which data store does Amazon Macie mainly target?","eEn":"Macie uses machine learning to detect and classify sensitive data such as personal information in S3 buckets and raises alerts. EFS, EBS, and RDS are not target data stores."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） KMS（Key Management Service）の鍵を使う他サービスの代表例はどれか。","o":["S3・EBS・RDSの暗号化","Route 53のDNSルーティング","Amazon SNSの通知配信","CloudFrontのキャッシュ配信"],"a":0,"e":"KMSの鍵はS3・EBS・RDSなどのデータ保存系サービスの暗号化に使われる。Route 53のDNSルーティング、SNSの通知配信、CloudFrontのキャッシュ配信は、主機能が暗号化ではなく代表例にならない。","qEn":"Which are typical examples of other services that use AWS KMS (Key Management Service) keys?","oEn":["Encryption of S3, EBS, and RDS","DNS routing with Route 53","Notification delivery with Amazon SNS","Cached delivery with CloudFront"],"eEn":"KMS keys are used to encrypt data storage services such as S3, EBS, and RDS. DNS routing in Route 53, notification delivery in SNS, and cached delivery in CloudFront are not primarily about encryption and are not typical examples."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"VPC（Virtual Private Cloud）内のリソースをインターネットから隔離する基本構成はどれか。","o":["Elastic IPアドレスの付与","プライベートサブネットへの配置","インターネットゲートウェイの直接アタッチ","パブリックサブネットへの配置と自動割当"],"a":1,"e":"直接到達の遮断。NAT経由の外向き通信。","qEn":"Which is the basic configuration for isolating resources in a VPC (Virtual Private Cloud) from the internet?","oEn":["Assigning an Elastic IP address","Placement in a private subnet","Directly attaching an internet gateway","Placement in a public subnet with automatic assignment"],"eEn":"Blocks direct access. Outbound communication goes through NAT."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の暗号化で「鍵の自動ローテーション」が低減するリスクはどれか。","o":["長期間同一鍵による侵害リスク","暗号アルゴリズムの脆弱化リスク","鍵の紛失によるデータ復号不能","アクセスキー漏洩による侵入リスク"],"a":0,"e":"鍵を定期的に更新すれば、同じ鍵を長期間使い続けることで侵害される確率と被害を抑えられる。アルゴリズムの脆弱化は鍵を替えても直らず、鍵の紛失による復号不能やアクセスキー漏洩はローテーションの対象外。","qEn":"Which risk does \"automatic key rotation\" reduce in AWS encryption?","oEn":["Risk of compromise from using the same key for a long time","Risk of weakening of the cryptographic algorithm","Inability to decrypt data because a key is lost","Risk of intrusion from leaked access keys"],"eEn":"Regularly rotating keys reduces the likelihood and impact of compromise from using the same key for a long time. Algorithm weakening is not fixed by changing keys, and inability to decrypt due to a lost key and access key leaks are outside the scope of rotation."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の責任共有モデルが提供形態で変化する点はどれか。","o":["提供形態に関わらず利用者の責任範囲は変化せず常に一定である","IaaS・PaaS・SaaSで利用者責任の範囲が変動","AWS側の責任範囲のみが提供形態によって変動する","オンプレミス環境と同様に利用者が全て管理する"],"a":1,"e":"抽象度に応じた分担。SaaSほど利用者負担小。","qEn":"What aspect of the AWS shared responsibility model changes by service delivery model?","oEn":["The customer's scope of responsibility is constant regardless of delivery model","The customer's scope of responsibility varies across IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS","Only AWS's scope of responsibility varies by delivery model","The customer manages everything, as in an on-premises environment"],"eEn":"Responsibility is divided according to the level of abstraction. The more SaaS-like the service, the smaller the customer's burden."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の「予防的統制」に該当するものはどれか。","o":["IAMポリシーやセキュリティグループによるアクセス制限","GuardDutyによる脅威の検知と通知","AWS Configによる構成変更の追跡と評価","CloudTrailによるAPI操作履歴のログ記録と保存"],"a":0,"e":"予防的統制は問題が起きる前にアクセスを制限して防ぐもので、IAMポリシーやセキュリティグループが該当する。GuardDutyの検知と通知、Configの変更追跡、CloudTrailのログ記録は事後に把握する発見的統制。","qEn":"Which corresponds to an AWS \"preventive control\"?","oEn":["Access restriction with IAM policies and security groups","Threat detection and notification with GuardDuty","Tracking and evaluating configuration changes with AWS Config","Logging and storing API operation history with CloudTrail"],"eEn":"Preventive controls restrict access to prevent problems before they occur, and IAM policies and security groups fit this. Detection and notification by GuardDuty, change tracking by Config, and log recording by CloudTrail are detective controls that identify things after the fact."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の「発見的統制」に該当するものはどれか。","o":["KMSによる保管中データの暗号化と鍵の保護","セキュリティグループによる通信の事前許可制御","IAMポリシーやセキュリティグループによる事前のアクセス制限","CloudTrailやGuardDutyによる検知・記録"],"a":3,"e":"発見的統制は起きた事象を検出し記録するもので、CloudTrailのAPI記録やGuardDutyの脅威検知が該当する。KMSによる暗号化は保護策で、セキュリティグループやIAMによる事前制限は予防的統制。","qEn":"Which corresponds to an AWS \"detective control\"?","oEn":["Encryption of data at rest and key protection with KMS","Pre-approved traffic control with security groups","Advance access restriction with IAM policies and security groups","Detection and recording with CloudTrail and GuardDuty"],"eEn":"Detective controls detect and record events that have occurred, and CloudTrail API recording and GuardDuty threat detection fit this. Encryption with KMS is a protective measure, and advance restrictions with security groups or IAM are preventive controls."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Trusted Advisorのセキュリティチェックが指摘する例はどれか。","o":["MFA未設定や過剰に開放されたポート","リザーブドインスタンスの購入推奨","EC2インスタンスのCPU使用率の低下","未使用のリソースによるコスト超過"],"a":0,"e":"Trusted Advisor のセキュリティチェックは、MFA 未設定や過剰に開放されたポートのような設定リスクを指摘する。リザーブドインスタンスの購入推奨、CPU 使用率の低いインスタンス、未使用リソースによるコスト超過は、コスト最適化の観点の指摘で、セキュリティ項目ではない。","qEn":"Which is an example of what AWS Trusted Advisor security checks flag?","oEn":["MFA not set up or overly open ports","A recommendation to purchase Reserved Instances","Low CPU utilization on EC2 instances","Cost overruns from unused resources"],"eEn":"Trusted Advisor security checks flag configuration risks such as missing MFA and overly open ports. Reserved Instance purchase recommendations, low-utilization instances and costs from unused resources are cost optimization findings, not security items."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"セキュリティグループの「ステートフル」が意味するものはどれか。","o":["戻りトラフィックの自動許可","サブネット単位で適用される","拒否ルールを明示的に設定","往復それぞれにルールが必要"],"a":0,"e":"セキュリティグループはステートフルで、往路の通信を許可すれば戻りのトラフィックも自動で許可される。往復それぞれにルールが必要なのはステートレスなNACLで、拒否ルールだけを設定できるわけでもない。","qEn":"What does \"stateful\" mean for a security group?","oEn":["Return traffic is automatically allowed","It is applied at the subnet level","Deny rules are explicitly configured","Rules are required for each direction"],"eEn":"Security groups are stateful: if you allow outbound traffic, the return traffic is automatically allowed too. Needing a rule for each direction applies to the stateless NACL, and it is not true that only deny rules can be set."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"NACL（Network Access Control List）の「ステートレス」が意味するものはどれか。","o":["戻りトラフィックを自動的に許可","インスタンス単位で適用される","許可ルールのみ設定できる","往復それぞれにルールが必要"],"a":3,"e":"NACLはステートレスで、戻りの通信も別に許可しなければならないため、往復それぞれにルールが必要になる。戻りトラフィックが自動で許可されるのはセキュリティグループで、NACLはサブネット単位に適用される。","qEn":"What does \"stateless\" mean for a NACL (Network Access Control List)?","oEn":["Return traffic is automatically allowed","It is applied at the instance level","Only allow rules can be set","Rules are required for each direction"],"eEn":"A NACL is stateless, so return traffic must also be allowed separately, which means rules are required for each direction. Automatic allowance of return traffic applies to security groups, and a NACL is applied at the subnet level."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"クロスアカウントアクセスを安全に実現する仕組みはどれか。","o":["IAMロールの引き受け（AssumeRole）","IAMユーザーのパスワードの相互共有","ルートユーザーのアクセスキーの共有","長期的なアクセスキーを各アカウントの利用者へ配布する"],"a":0,"e":"クロスアカウントアクセスは、IAMロールの引き受け(AssumeRole)で、一時的な認証情報を使って安全に実現する。恒久的なアクセスキーの共有、パスワードの共有、ルートユーザーの使い回しは、漏洩の危険が高い。","qEn":"Which mechanism securely enables cross-account access?","oEn":["Assuming an IAM role (AssumeRole)","Sharing IAM user passwords with each other","Sharing the root user's access keys","Distributing long-term access keys to users in each account"],"eEn":"Cross-account access is achieved securely by assuming an IAM role (AssumeRole), using temporary credentials. Sharing permanent access keys, sharing passwords, and reusing the root user are highly risky because of leakage."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の暗号化で「保管中データの保護」の例はどれか。","o":["VPN接続による転送中データの保護","TLSによるクライアントとサーバー間の通信暗号化","S3やEBSに保存されたデータの暗号化","ACMによるTLS証明書の発行と更新"],"a":2,"e":"保管中データの保護は、S3やEBSに保存したデータを暗号化すること。VPN接続やTLSによる通信の暗号化は転送中データの保護で、ACMは証明書の発行と更新を担い、データ自体は暗号化しない。","qEn":"Which is an example of \"protection of data at rest\" in AWS encryption?","oEn":["Protecting data in transit with a VPN connection","Encrypting communication between client and server with TLS","Encrypting data stored in S3 or EBS","Issuing and renewing TLS certificates with ACM"],"eEn":"Protecting data at rest means encrypting data stored in S3 or EBS. Encrypting communications with a VPN connection or TLS protects data in transit, and ACM issues and renews certificates but does not encrypt the data itself."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Security HubがCISなどの基準で行うことはどれか。","o":["KMSによる暗号鍵の生成と管理","WAFによるWeb攻撃の遮断","GuardDutyによる脅威の自動検知","ベストプラクティスへの準拠スコア評価"],"a":3,"e":"Security Hub は、CIS などの基準に照らして設定を自動チェックし、ベストプラクティスへの準拠状況をスコアで評価する。暗号鍵の生成と管理は KMS、Web 攻撃の遮断は WAF、脅威の自動検知は GuardDuty が担う。","qEn":"What does AWS Security Hub do against standards such as CIS?","oEn":["Generating and managing encryption keys with KMS","Blocking web attacks with WAF","Automatic threat detection with GuardDuty","Scoring compliance with best practices"],"eEn":"Security Hub automatically checks configurations against standards such as CIS and scores compliance with best practices. Creating and managing encryption keys is KMS, blocking web attacks is WAF, and automatic threat detection is GuardDuty."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"一時的な外部協力者へ安全にアクセスを与える方法はどれか。","o":["恒久的なIAMユーザーアカウントの新規発行","期限付きのIAMロールまたはフェデレーション","ルートユーザーのアクセスキーの貸与","共有パスワードによる恒久的なアクセス権の付与"],"a":1,"e":"一時的な外部協力者には、期限付きのIAMロールまたはフェデレーションで、一時認証情報を渡す。ルートのアクセスキーの共有、管理者の恒久IAMユーザー、共有パスワードは、失効せず漏洩の危険がある。","qEn":"Which is a way to securely grant access to a temporary external collaborator?","oEn":["Issuing a new permanent IAM user account","A time-limited IAM role or federation","Lending the root user's access keys","Granting permanent access with a shared password"],"eEn":"For a temporary external collaborator, provide temporary credentials through a time-limited IAM role or federation. Sharing the root access keys, a permanent administrator IAM user, and a shared password do not expire and risk leakage."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の監査証跡を全リージョン横断で収集する設定はどれか。","o":["CloudWatchによるメトリクス監視","CloudTrailのマルチリージョン証跡","AWS Configによる構成変更の記録","CloudTrailの特定リージョンのみの単一証跡"],"a":1,"e":"CloudTrailのマルチリージョン証跡は、全リージョンの操作をまとめて記録し、網羅的な監査を可能にする。単一リージョンの証跡は他リージョンを見逃し、Configの集約やメトリクスフィルタは監査証跡の収集ではない。","qEn":"Which setting collects AWS audit trails across all Regions?","oEn":["Metrics monitoring with CloudWatch","A CloudTrail multi-Region trail","Recording configuration changes with AWS Config","A single trail for one specific Region in CloudTrail"],"eEn":"A CloudTrail multi-Region trail records operations in all Regions together and enables comprehensive auditing. A single-Region trail misses other Regions, and Config aggregation and metric filters are not audit trail collection."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"IAM（Identity and Access Management） Access Analyzerが検出するものはどれか。","o":["Inspectorによる脆弱性の自動診断","GuardDutyによる不正な通信の検知","外部へ公開された意図しないアクセス権","CloudTrailによるAPI呼び出しの記録"],"a":2,"e":"IAM Access Analyzer は、外部へ公開された意図しないアクセス権を検出し、過剰な共有を見つける。脆弱性の自動診断は Inspector、不正な通信の検知は GuardDuty、API 呼び出しの記録は CloudTrail の役割である。","qEn":"What does IAM (Identity and Access Management) Access Analyzer detect?","oEn":["Automated vulnerability scanning by Inspector","Detection of unauthorized traffic by GuardDuty","Unintended access permissions exposed externally","Recording of API calls by CloudTrail"],"eEn":"IAM Access Analyzer detects unintended access granted to external parties and finds excessive sharing. Automated vulnerability scanning is Inspector, detecting malicious traffic is GuardDuty, and recording API calls is CloudTrail."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"ゼロトラストの基本方針はどれか。","o":["社内ネットワーク内の通信を無条件に信頼する","一度認証すれば以降は検証を省略する","ネットワーク境界の防御のみに依存する","すべてのアクセスを検証し暗黙の信頼を排除"],"a":3,"e":"ゼロトラストは「何も信頼せず常に検証する」方針で、すべてのアクセスを検証し暗黙の信頼を排除する。社内ネットワーク内を無条件に信頼する、境界の防御のみに依存する、一度の認証で検証を省くのは、いずれも境界型の発想。","qEn":"What is the basic principle of zero trust?","oEn":["Unconditionally trust traffic inside the corporate network","Skip verification once authenticated","Rely only on defending the network perimeter","Verify every access and eliminate implicit trust"],"eEn":"Zero trust is the principle of \"trust nothing, always verify,\" which means verifying all access and eliminating implicit trust. Unconditionally trusting the internal network, relying only on perimeter defense, and skipping verification after one authentication are all perimeter-based thinking."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Detectiveが支援するものはどれか。","o":["セキュリティインシデントの調査と原因可視化","Security Hubによる準拠状況の評価","Shieldによる DDoS 攻撃の緩和","GuardDutyによる脅威の継続的な検知"],"a":0,"e":"Detectiveは関連するログを自動で分析して関連付け、セキュリティインシデントの原因調査を可視化で支援する。Security Hubは準拠状況の評価、ShieldはDDoSの緩和、GuardDutyは脅威の検知が役割。","qEn":"What does Amazon Detective support?","oEn":["Investigating security incidents and visualizing root causes","Assessing compliance status with Security Hub","Mitigating DDoS attacks with Shield","Continuous threat detection with GuardDuty"],"eEn":"Detective automatically analyzes and correlates related logs to support investigating the cause of security incidents through visualization. Security Hub assesses compliance status, Shield mitigates DDoS, and GuardDuty detects threats."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Firewall Managerの役割はどれか。","o":["単一のEC2インスタンスの通信のみを制御","複数アカウントへのファイアウォールルール一元管理","Elastic Load Balancingによる負荷分散","Route 53によるドメイン名の名前解決"],"a":1,"e":"Firewall ManagerはAWS Organizations配下の複数アカウントに、WAFやセキュリティグループなどのルールを一元管理して適用する。単一のEC2の通信制御はセキュリティグループ、負荷分散はElastic Load Balancing、名前解決はRoute 53の役割。","qEn":"What is the role of AWS Firewall Manager?","oEn":["Controlling traffic of a single EC2 instance only","Centrally managing firewall rules across multiple accounts","Load balancing with Elastic Load Balancing","Domain name resolution with Route 53"],"eEn":"Firewall Manager centrally manages and applies rules such as WAF and security groups across multiple accounts under AWS Organizations. Controlling a single EC2 instance's traffic is done by security groups, load balancing by Elastic Load Balancing, and name resolution by Route 53."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Systems Manager Session Managerの利点はどれか。","o":["KMSによる暗号鍵の生成と管理","Route 53によるDNSクエリの高速化","ELBによるトラフィックの負荷分散","SSH鍵管理不要で監査可能なEC2接続"],"a":3,"e":"ポート開放不要の接続。監査可能なアクセス。","qEn":"What is a benefit of AWS Systems Manager Session Manager?","oEn":["Generating and managing encryption keys with KMS","Speeding up DNS queries with Route 53","Load balancing traffic with ELB","Auditable EC2 connections without SSH key management"],"eEn":"Connects without opening ports. Auditable access."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"クレデンシャルのハードコーディングを避けるべき理由はどれか。","o":["アプリの起動時間の増大","コンパイル時のエラー増加","漏洩時の不正利用リスク","ソースコードの実行速度の低下"],"a":2,"e":"認証情報をコードに直接書くと、リポジトリやログから漏れた際に不正利用される危険がある。起動時間の増大、コンパイル時のエラー、実行速度の低下とは関係がなく、Secrets Managerなどで別管理するのが原則。","qEn":"Why should credentials not be hard-coded?","oEn":["Longer application startup time","More errors at compile time","Risk of misuse if they are leaked","Slower source code execution"],"eEn":"If credentials are written directly in code, they can be misused if they leak from a repository or logs. They have nothing to do with startup time, compile-time errors, or execution speed, and the principle is to manage them separately, for example in Secrets Manager."},
  {"d":"D2","q":"多層防御（Defense in Depth）に合致するものはどれか。","o":["単一のファイアウォール製品への依存","複数のセキュリティ層の組み合わせ","ネットワーク境界のみでの防御","認証プロセスの完全な省略"],"a":1,"e":"多層防御は複数のセキュリティ対策を重ね、一つが破られても別の層で止める考え方。単一のファイアウォール製品への依存や境界のみでの防御は単一障害点になり、認証の完全な省略は防御層の欠落。","qEn":"Which of the following matches defense in depth?","oEn":["Relying on a single firewall product","Combining multiple layers of security","Defending only at the network perimeter","Omitting the authentication process entirely"],"eEn":"Defense in depth layers multiple security measures so that if one is breached, another layer stops the attack. Relying on a single firewall product or defending only at the perimeter creates single points of failure, and omitting authentication entirely is a missing defensive layer."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"仮想化によって1台の物理サーバーを複数の論理サーバーに分ける技術の利点はどれか。","o":["物理サーバー台数の大幅な増加","リソースの効率的な共有と分離","ハードウェア障害時の完全な冗長化","アプリの実行速度の常時向上"],"a":1,"e":"物理資源の使用率向上。クラウドの基盤技術。","qEn":"What is the benefit of the technology that uses virtualization to divide one physical server into multiple logical servers?","oEn":["A large increase in the number of physical servers","Efficient sharing and isolation of resources","Complete redundancy when hardware fails","Constantly faster application execution"],"eEn":"It improves the utilization of physical resources and is a foundational technology of the cloud."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"オンデマンド・セルフサービスが意味するクラウドの特性はどれか。","o":["物理機材の納品を待つ手配","人手を介さない即時のリソース取得","管理者の承認を経てからの調達","サポート窓口への申請と承認による確保"],"a":1,"e":"管理コンソールやAPIでの調達。待ち時間のない利用。","qEn":"Which cloud characteristic does on-demand self-service describe?","oEn":["Arranging to wait for physical equipment to be delivered","Obtaining resources instantly without human interaction","Procuring resources after administrator approval","Securing resources by applying to a support desk and awaiting approval"],"eEn":"Resources are provisioned through the management console or APIs, so there is no waiting time before use."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Amazon EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）が提供するものはどれか。","o":["オブジェクトストレージの提供","仮想サーバーを立ち上げるサービス","コンテンツ配信ネットワークの提供","DNSによる名前解決のサービス"],"a":1,"e":"EC2は仮想サーバー（インスタンス）を必要なときに立ち上げて使えるコンピューティングサービス。オブジェクトストレージはS3、コンテンツ配信ネットワークはCloudFront、DNSによる名前解決はRoute 53が提供する。","qEn":"What does Amazon EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud) provide?","oEn":["Object storage","A service for launching virtual servers","A content delivery network","DNS name resolution"],"eEn":"EC2 is a compute service that lets you launch and use virtual servers (instances) whenever you need them. Object storage is provided by S3, the content delivery network by CloudFront, and DNS name resolution by Route 53."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Elastic Load Balancingが担う役割はどれか。","o":["オブジェクトの保存と取り出し","サーバーレスでのコード実行","DNSによるドメイン名の解決","EC2のトラフィックを制御し分散"],"a":3,"e":"Elastic Load Balancingは受けた通信を複数のEC2などに分散し、正常な対象にだけ振り分ける。オブジェクトの保存と取り出しはS3、サーバーレスのコード実行はLambda、ドメイン名の解決はRoute 53の役割。","qEn":"What is the role of Elastic Load Balancing?","oEn":["Storing and retrieving objects","Running code in a serverless environment","Resolving domain names through DNS","Distributing traffic across EC2 instances"],"eEn":"Elastic Load Balancing distributes incoming traffic across multiple targets such as EC2 instances and routes it only to healthy ones. Storing and retrieving objects is the role of S3, running code serverlessly is Lambda, and resolving domain names is Route 53."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Auto Scalingが担う役割はどれか。","o":["ログの収集と一元的な保管","EC2を自動で増減するスケーリング","DNSクエリの名前解決処理","受信トラフィックの複数への負荷分散"],"a":1,"e":"需要連動の自動スケール。可用性とコストの両立。","qEn":"What is the role of Auto Scaling?","oEn":["Collecting and centrally storing logs","Automatically scaling EC2 capacity in and out","Processing DNS query name resolution","Load balancing incoming traffic across multiple targets"],"eEn":"It scales automatically in line with demand, balancing availability and cost."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Lambdaが提供するものはどれか。","o":["コンテンツ配信ネットワーク機能","サーバーレスでコードを保存・実行","仮想サーバーインスタンスの起動と管理","DNSによる名前解決の提供"],"a":1,"e":"イベント駆動の関数実行。実行時間に応じた課金。","qEn":"What does AWS Lambda provide?","oEn":["A content delivery network feature","Storing and running code without servers","Launching and managing virtual server instances","DNS name resolution"],"eEn":"It runs functions in response to events and is billed according to execution time."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Amazon Lightsailが提供するものはどれか。","o":["サーバー・ストレージ・DB・NWをまとめて低価格提供","エッジロケーションからのコンテンツの高速配信","Kubernetesを実行するマネージドクラスター基盤","ペタバイト規模のデータウェアハウスの提供"],"a":0,"e":"Lightsailはサーバー、ストレージ、データベース、ネットワークをまとめて低価格の固定プランで提供する簡易なサービス。エッジからの高速配信はCloudFront、Kubernetes基盤はEKS、ペタバイト規模のデータウェアハウスはRedshiftが担う。","qEn":"What does Amazon Lightsail provide?","oEn":["Servers, storage, databases, and networking bundled at a low price","Fast content delivery from edge locations","A managed cluster platform that runs Kubernetes","A petabyte-scale data warehouse"],"eEn":"Lightsail is a simple service that bundles servers, storage, databases, and networking under low-cost fixed plans. Fast delivery from the edge is handled by CloudFront, the Kubernetes platform by EKS, and the petabyte-scale data warehouse by Redshift."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Fargateが提供するものはどれか。","o":["オブジェクトデータの保管と取り出し","仮想サーバーインスタンスを専有して利用する形態","DNSによるドメイン名の名前解決","コンテナ向けサーバーレスコンピューティング"],"a":3,"e":"Fargateはサーバーやクラスターを管理せずにコンテナを実行できる、コンテナ向けのサーバーレスコンピューティング。オブジェクトデータの保管はS3、インスタンスの専有利用はDedicated系、DNSによる名前解決はRoute 53の役割。","qEn":"What does AWS Fargate provide?","oEn":["Storing and retrieving object data","Using virtual server instances on dedicated hardware","DNS name resolution for domain names","Serverless compute for containers"],"eEn":"Fargate is serverless compute for containers that lets you run containers without managing servers or clusters. Storing object data is the role of S3, dedicated use of instances is the Dedicated family, and DNS name resolution is Route 53."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ブロックストレージの代表例はどれか。","o":["S3（オブジェクトストレージ）","CloudFront（コンテンツ配信ネットワーク）","EBS（EC2にアタッチするディスク）","S3 Glacier（長期アーカイブ）"],"a":2,"e":"ブロックストレージの代表はEBSで、EC2にディスクとしてアタッチして使う。S3はオブジェクトストレージ、CloudFrontはコンテンツ配信ネットワーク、S3 Glacierは長期保管向けのアーカイブ用ストレージ。","qEn":"Which is a typical example of block storage?","oEn":["S3 (object storage)","CloudFront (content delivery network)","EBS (a disk attached to EC2)","S3 Glacier (long-term archive)"],"eEn":"The typical block storage is EBS, which you attach to EC2 as a disk. S3 is object storage, CloudFront is a content delivery network, and S3 Glacier is archive storage for long-term retention."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"オブジェクトストレージの特性として正しいものはどれか。","o":["単一のEC2にのみ専用で接続","低レイテンシーのリレーショナルDB","安価で高耐久のオンライン大容量保管","複数サーバーでの共有ファイルマウント"],"a":2,"e":"オブジェクトストレージは、安価で高耐久な大容量データをオンラインで保管でき、S3が代表。単一のEC2専用の接続はEBS、低レイテンシーのリレーショナルDBはRDS、複数サーバーでの共有ファイルマウントはEFSの特性。","qEn":"Which statement correctly describes object storage?","oEn":["Dedicated connection to a single EC2 instance only","A low-latency relational database","Low-cost, highly durable, large-capacity online storage","Shared file mounts across multiple servers"],"eEn":"Object storage can hold large amounts of data online at low cost with high durability, and S3 is the typical example. A connection dedicated to a single EC2 instance describes EBS, a low-latency relational database describes RDS, and shared file mounts across multiple servers describe EFS."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"ファイルストレージの代表例はどれか。","o":["S3（オブジェクトストレージ）","EFS（複数EC2で同時マウント）","EBS（単一EC2に接続するディスク）","S3 Glacier（長期アーカイブ保管）"],"a":1,"e":"NFS互換。スケーラブルな共有ファイル。","qEn":"Which is a typical example of file storage?","oEn":["S3 (object storage)","EFS (mounted simultaneously by multiple EC2 instances)","EBS (a disk attached to a single EC2 instance)","S3 Glacier (long-term archive storage)"],"eEn":"It is NFS-compatible, scalable shared file storage."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service） Glacier Deep Archiveの特性はどれか。","o":["単一のEC2に専用でマウント","最安・取り出しに時間を要する長期保管","ミリ秒単位で即時に取り出し可能","頻繁なアクセスに適した標準的な保管階層"],"a":1,"e":"7〜10年以上のめったに使わないデータ。最安の保管庫。","qEn":"Which describes the characteristics of S3 Glacier Deep Archive?","oEn":["Mounted exclusively on a single EC2 instance","Lowest-cost long-term storage with slow retrieval","Instant retrieval in milliseconds","A standard storage tier suited to frequent access"],"eEn":"It is for rarely used data kept for 7 to 10 years or more, and it is the cheapest storage vault."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service） Glacier Instant Retrievalの特性はどれか。","o":["複数EC2で共有するファイルマウント","頻繁なアクセス向けの標準ストレージ","ほぼアクセスなしだがミリ秒で即時取り出し","取り出しに数時間かかる最も安価な長期保管"],"a":2,"e":"医用画像・報道など。即時取り出しが必要な低頻度データ。","qEn":"Which describes the characteristics of S3 Glacier Instant Retrieval?","oEn":["File mounts shared by multiple EC2 instances","Standard storage for frequent access","Almost never accessed, but retrievable instantly in milliseconds","The cheapest long-term storage, with retrieval taking hours"],"eEn":"It suits data such as medical images and news media, which is accessed infrequently but must be retrievable immediately."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"マネージド型サービス（RDS（Relational Database Service）等）の特徴はどれか。","o":["物理サーバーを占有して利用者自身が運用する","データベースのライセンスを利用者が自己管理する","スケーリング・可用性がサービスに組み込まれAWSが管理","OSの設定やパッチ適用からバックアップまで全て利用者が管理する"],"a":2,"e":"マネージド型のRDSなどは、スケーリングや可用性の仕組みがサービスに組み込まれ、AWSが管理を担う。OSの設定からパッチ、バックアップまで全て利用者が管理するのは、EC2上に自前でDBを構築した場合の姿。","qEn":"Which describes managed services such as RDS (Relational Database Service)?","oEn":["The customer occupies physical servers and operates them","The customer manages the database license","Scaling and availability are built into the service and managed by AWS","The customer manages everything from OS settings and patching to backups"],"eEn":"With managed services such as RDS, scaling and availability mechanisms are built into the service and AWS handles their management. Having the customer manage everything from OS settings to patching and backups is what happens when you build your own database on EC2."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"アンマネージド型（EC2（Elastic Compute Cloud）上のDB等）の特徴はどれか。","o":["設定を変更できる項目が限定的である","物理サーバーの用意や運用が不要になる","スケーリングや可用性を利用者側で設定・管理","AWSが可用性やパッチ適用を全て自動で管理する"],"a":2,"e":"アンマネージド型では、EC2上のDBのようにスケーリングや可用性を利用者が自分で設定・管理する。AWSが可用性やパッチ適用を全て自動管理するのはマネージド型の特徴で、設定項目が限定的なのもマネージド型の側。","qEn":"Which describes unmanaged services such as a database on EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)?","oEn":["Only a limited set of settings can be changed","Preparing and operating physical servers is no longer necessary","The customer configures and manages scaling and availability","AWS automatically manages all availability and patching"],"eEn":"With unmanaged services, such as a database on EC2, the customer configures and manages scaling and availability. Having AWS automatically manage all availability and patching is a characteristic of managed services, and limited configurable settings are also on the managed side."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Network Firewallの役割はどれか。","o":["VPCのトラフィックを詳細制御するファイアウォール","ACMによるTLSサーバー証明書の発行と管理","Shieldによる DDoS 攻撃の自動緩和","WAFによるWebアプリケーション層への攻撃の遮断"],"a":0,"e":"ルールベースの詳細制御。VPC境界の保護。（2026年11月時点：公式試験ガイド v1.3（2026年10月29日）は AWS Network Firewall を出題範囲外のサービスに挙げている（旧版 v1.0 では出題範囲内）。再確認のうえ引用すること）","qEn":"What is the role of AWS Network Firewall?","oEn":["A firewall that finely controls VPC traffic","Issuing and managing TLS server certificates with ACM","Automatically mitigating DDoS attacks with Shield","Blocking attacks on the web application layer with WAF"],"eEn":"It provides detailed rule-based control and protects the VPC boundary. (As of November 2026: the official exam guide v1.3 (October 29, 2026) lists AWS Network Firewall as an out-of-scope service (it was in scope in the older v1.0 guide). Verify before citing.)"},
  {"d":"D3","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service） Selectが提供する機能はどれか。","o":["Elastic Load Balancingによる負荷分散","Route 53によるDNSの名前解決","KMSによる暗号鍵の生成とローテーション","S3内で直接クエリ実行（CSV・JSON対応）"],"a":3,"e":"S3 SelectはS3内のCSVやJSONのオブジェクトに対し、SQL式で必要な部分だけを直接クエリして取り出す。負荷分散はElastic Load Balancing、名前解決はRoute 53、暗号鍵の生成とローテーションはKMSの機能。","qEn":"Which feature does S3 Select provide?","oEn":["Load balancing with Elastic Load Balancing","DNS name resolution with Route 53","Encryption key generation and rotation with KMS","Running queries directly within S3 (supports CSV and JSON)"],"eEn":"S3 Select uses SQL expressions to query CSV or JSON objects in S3 directly and retrieve only the parts you need. Load balancing is a function of Elastic Load Balancing, name resolution of Route 53, and encryption key generation and rotation of KMS."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Amazon Redshift Spectrumが提供する機能はどれか。","o":["クエリ結果をElastiCacheにキャッシュする仕組み","DynamoDBのデータをRedshiftへ自動同期する機能","S3の格納データへRedshiftから直接クエリ","オンプレのデータウェアハウスをRedshiftへ移行"],"a":2,"e":"Redshift SpectrumはS3に置いたデータをRedshiftに取り込まずに、Redshiftから直接SQLでクエリできる機能。結果のElastiCacheキャッシュ、DynamoDBの自動同期、オンプレDWHの移行は別の機能やサービスが担う。","qEn":"Which feature does Amazon Redshift Spectrum provide?","oEn":["A mechanism for caching query results in ElastiCache","A feature that automatically syncs DynamoDB data to Redshift","Querying data stored in S3 directly from Redshift","Migrating an on-premises data warehouse to Redshift"],"eEn":"Redshift Spectrum lets you query data stored in S3 directly from Redshift with SQL, without loading it into Redshift. Caching results in ElastiCache, automatic DynamoDB syncing, and migrating an on-premises data warehouse are handled by other features and services."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"Egress-Only Internet Gatewayの用途はどれか。","o":["IPv4アドレスをIPv6へ変換して通信を中継","プライベートサブネットへNATで外向き通信を提供","IPv6の内向き通信のみを許可し外向きを遮断","IPv6向けの外向き通信を許可し内向きを遮断"],"a":3,"e":"Egress-Only Internet GatewayはIPv6専用で、VPC内から外への通信を許可しつつ、外部から始まる内向き通信を遮断する。IPv6の内向きのみ許可は逆で、IPv4とIPv6の変換やNATによる外向き通信はNAT Gatewayの領域。","qEn":"What is the purpose of an Egress-Only Internet Gateway?","oEn":["Translating IPv4 addresses to IPv6 and relaying traffic","Providing outbound traffic for private subnets through NAT","Allowing only inbound IPv6 traffic and blocking outbound traffic","Allowing outbound IPv6 traffic and blocking inbound traffic"],"eEn":"An Egress-Only Internet Gateway is for IPv6 only and allows traffic from inside the VPC to go out while blocking inbound traffic initiated from outside. Allowing only inbound IPv6 is the reverse, and translating between IPv4 and IPv6 or providing outbound traffic through NAT is the domain of a NAT gateway."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"仮想プライベートゲートウェイ（VGW）の役割はどれか。","o":["Direct Connectの物理専用線を終端する","オンプレ側のVPNルーター機器の情報を保持","複数VPCをまとめて相互接続するハブ","VPN接続時のAWS側ルーター（終端）"],"a":3,"e":"仮想プライベートゲートウェイは、VPN接続でAWS側の終端となるルーター。Direct Connectの専用線の終端は別の仕組みで、オンプレ側のVPN機器の情報はカスタマーゲートウェイ、複数VPCのハブはTransit Gatewayが担う。","qEn":"What is the role of a virtual private gateway (VGW)?","oEn":["Terminating a Direct Connect physical dedicated line","Holding information about the on-premises VPN router device","A hub that interconnects multiple VPCs","The AWS-side router (endpoint) for a VPN connection"],"eEn":"A virtual private gateway is the router that serves as the AWS-side endpoint of a VPN connection. Terminating a Direct Connect dedicated line is handled by a different mechanism, information about the on-premises VPN device is held by the customer gateway, and the hub for multiple VPCs is the Transit Gateway."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"カスタマーゲートウェイが提供する情報はどれか。","o":["VPCのルートテーブルの経路情報","AWS側のVPN終端ルーターの設定情報","オンプレ接続時の利用者側機器情報","IPsecトンネルの暗号化アルゴリズム設定"],"a":2,"e":"カスタマーゲートウェイは、オンプレミス側（利用者側）のVPN機器のIPアドレスなどの情報をAWSに伝えるリソース。AWS側の終端の設定情報は仮想プライベートゲートウェイ、ルート情報はVPC側、IPsecの暗号設定はVPN接続の設定が担う。","qEn":"What information does a customer gateway provide?","oEn":["Route information from the VPC route table","Configuration information for the AWS-side VPN endpoint router","Information about the customer-side device for on-premises connections","Encryption algorithm settings for the IPsec tunnel"],"eEn":"A customer gateway is a resource that tells AWS information, such as the IP address, about the on-premises (customer-side) VPN device. Configuration for the AWS-side endpoint is handled by the virtual private gateway, route information by the VPC side, and IPsec encryption settings by the VPN connection configuration."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"グローバル／リージョン設置でAZ（Availability Zone）に紐づかないサービスの例はどれか。","o":["S3・Route 53・IAM・CloudFront","VPC・サブネット・NAT Gatewayはグローバル配置","ELB・Auto Scaling・EBSはAZに依存しない","EC2・EBS・RDS・サブネットはすべてグローバル"],"a":0,"e":"S3、Route 53、IAM、CloudFrontはリージョンまたはグローバルのサービスで、特定のAZに紐づかない。サブネットはAZに属し、EBSもAZ内に作られるため、「VPC・サブネット・NATはグローバル」「ELB・EBSはAZ非依存」は誤り。","qEn":"Which services are examples that are global or regional and are not tied to an Availability Zone (AZ)?","oEn":["S3, Route 53, IAM, and CloudFront","VPC, subnets, and NAT Gateway are deployed globally","ELB, Auto Scaling, and EBS do not depend on an AZ","EC2, EBS, RDS, and subnets are all global"],"eEn":"S3, Route 53, IAM, and CloudFront are regional or global services and are not tied to a specific AZ. Subnets belong to an AZ and EBS volumes are created within an AZ, so the statements \"VPC, subnets, and NAT are global\" and \"ELB and EBS are AZ-independent\" are incorrect."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） DataSyncの用途はどれか。","o":["物理ストレージ装置を配送して取り込む","オンプレとS3/EFS間のデータ転送を自動化","データベーススキーマを変換して移行する","SFTPプロトコルでファイルを外部と授受する"],"a":1,"e":"DataSyncはオンプレミスとS3やEFSの間のデータ転送を自動化し、高速化する。物理装置を配送して取り込むのはSnow Family、スキーマ変換はSCTやDMS、SFTPで外部とファイルを授受するのはTransfer Familyの用途。","qEn":"What is the purpose of AWS DataSync?","oEn":["Shipping physical storage devices to ingest data","Automating data transfer between on premises and S3/EFS","Converting a database schema for migration","Exchanging files with external parties over the SFTP protocol"],"eEn":"DataSync automates and accelerates data transfer between on premises and S3 or EFS. Shipping physical devices for ingestion is the Snow Family, schema conversion is SCT or DMS, and exchanging files with external parties over SFTP is the purpose of Transfer Family."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Transfer Familyの用途はどれか。","o":["オンプレとS3間の転送をエージェントで自動化","SFTP/FTP/FTPS対応のマネージド転送サービス","テープバックアップをクラウドへ仮想化して保管","HTTPS経由で大容量オブジェクトを配信する"],"a":1,"e":"S3へのアップロード処理。標準プロトコル対応。（2026年11月時点：公式試験ガイド v1.3（2026年10月29日）は AWS Transfer Family を出題範囲外のサービスに挙げている（旧版 v1.0 では出題範囲内）。再確認のうえ引用すること）","qEn":"What is the purpose of AWS Transfer Family?","oEn":["Automating transfers between on premises and S3 with an agent","A transfer service that supports SFTP, FTP, and FTPS","Virtualizing tape backups and storing them in the cloud","Delivering large objects over HTTPS"],"eEn":"It handles uploads to S3 and supports standard protocols. (As of November 2026: the official exam guide v1.3 (October 29, 2026) lists AWS Transfer Family as an out-of-scope service (it was in scope in the older v1.0 guide). Verify before citing.)"},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Outpostsが提供するものはどれか。","o":["5G通信事業者のネットワーク内にAWSを組み込む仕組み","AWSインフラをオンプレ／エッジへ提供する一貫ハイブリッド環境","大都市近郊にコンピュートを配置する低遅延ロケーション","AWSの複数リージョンを専用線で相互接続するグローバルネットワーク基盤"],"a":1,"e":"Outpostsは、AWSのインフラとサービスをオンプレミスやエッジの自社施設に置き、クラウドと一貫して使えるハイブリッド環境を提供する。5G事業者網内への配置はWavelength、大都市近郊の低遅延配置はLocal Zonesの役割。","qEn":"What does AWS Outposts provide?","oEn":["A mechanism that embeds AWS inside the networks of 5G carriers","A consistent hybrid environment that brings AWS infrastructure on premises or to the edge","Low-latency locations that place compute near large cities","A global network foundation that interconnects multiple AWS Regions with dedicated lines"],"eEn":"Outposts provides a hybrid environment that places AWS infrastructure and services in your own on-premises or edge facilities so you can use them consistently with the cloud. Placement inside 5G carrier networks is the role of Wavelength, and low-latency placement near large cities is the role of Local Zones."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Application Migration Service（MGN）の用途はどれか。","o":["データベースのスキーマを変換して移行する","各種インフラからサーバーをAWS用に変換し効率的に移行","物理サーバーの構成と依存関係を収集し計画を支援する","アプリのソースコードをコンテナ向けに書き換える近代化"],"a":1,"e":"MGNは物理・仮想・他クラウド上のサーバーをブロック単位で複製しAWS向けに変換するため、最小限の停止で移行できる。","qEn":"What is the purpose of AWS Application Migration Service (MGN)?","oEn":["Converting a database schema and migrating it to the target database","Converting servers from various infrastructures for AWS and migrating them efficiently","Collecting the configuration and dependencies of physical servers to support planning","Modernizing by rewriting application source code for containers"],"eEn":"MGN replicates servers from physical, virtual, and other cloud environments at the block level and converts them for AWS, so migration can be done with minimal downtime."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Schema Conversion Tool（SCT）の用途はどれか。","o":["実データをソースDBからターゲットDBへ継続的に複製","DBスキーマやコードをターゲットDB互換へ自動変換","サーバーイメージを変換しEC2として起動できるよう移行","オンプレの依存関係を可視化し移行計画を立案する"],"a":1,"e":"SCTは、データベースのスキーマやコードを移行先のDBに合う形へ自動変換するツール。データの継続的な複製はDMS、サーバーイメージの変換はApplication Migration Serviceなど、依存関係の可視化はApplication Discovery Serviceの役割。","qEn":"What is the purpose of the AWS Schema Conversion Tool (SCT)?","oEn":["Continuously replicating actual data from the source DB to the target DB","Automatically converting DB schemas and code to be compatible with the target DB","Converting server images and migrating them so they can be launched as EC2","Visualizing on-premises dependencies and planning the migration"],"eEn":"SCT is a tool that automatically converts database schemas and code into a form that fits the destination database. Continuous data replication is the role of DMS, server image conversion is Application Migration Service and similar tools, and visualizing dependencies is the role of Application Discovery Service."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Migration Hubの役割はどれか。","o":["オンプレ資産を検出し依存関係マップを生成する機能","移行対象サーバーのスキーマを自動変換するツール","各移行ツールの実行状況を追跡するダッシュボード","各サーバーを実際にAWSへ複製し切替を実行する処理"],"a":2,"e":"Migration Hubは各種移行ツールの進捗を一つの画面に集約し、移行プロジェクト全体の状況を横断的に追跡できるから。","qEn":"What is the role of AWS Migration Hub?","oEn":["A feature that discovers on-premises assets and generates a dependency map","A tool that automatically converts the schemas of servers to be migrated","A dashboard that tracks the execution status of each migration tool","A process that actually replicates each server to AWS and performs the cutover"],"eEn":"Migration Hub consolidates the progress of various migration tools into a single view, so you can track the status of the whole migration project across tools."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Application Discovery Serviceの用途はどれか。","o":["収集したメトリクスを基にサーバーイメージをEC2へ複製し移行を実行する","オンプレのサーバー設定・使用状況・依存関係を収集し移行計画を支援","複数の移行ツールの進捗を一元的に可視化するダッシュボードを提供する","データベーススキーマとストアドプロシージャを別エンジン向けに変換する"],"a":1,"e":"Application Discovery Serviceは、オンプレミスのサーバー設定、使用状況、依存関係を収集して移行計画を支援する。サーバーの複製と移行の実行はApplication Migration Service、進捗の一元表示はMigration Hub、スキーマ変換はSCTの役割。","qEn":"What is the purpose of AWS Application Discovery Service?","oEn":["Replicating server images to EC2 and performing the migration based on collected metrics","Collecting on-premises server configuration, usage, and dependencies to support migration planning","Providing a dashboard that visualizes the progress of multiple migration tools in one place","Converting database schemas and stored procedures for a different engine"],"eEn":"Application Discovery Service collects on-premises server configuration, usage, and dependencies to support migration planning. Replicating servers and performing the migration is the role of Application Migration Service, centralized progress display is Migration Hub, and schema conversion is SCT."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"VM Import/Exportの用途はどれか。","o":["オンプレとS3間で大量ファイルを継続的に同期転送する","データベースを無停止で別エンジンへ継続的に移行する","コンテナイメージを保管し配布するレジストリを提供する","仮想マシンイメージをEC2へインポート/エクスポートする"],"a":3,"e":"VM Import/Exportは、仮想マシンイメージをEC2へインポートし、EC2からエクスポートもできる。オンプレミスとS3間の継続同期はDataSync、無停止のDB移行はDMS、コンテナイメージの保管と配布はECRの役割。","qEn":"What is the purpose of VM Import/Export?","oEn":["Continuously synchronizing large numbers of files between on premises and S3","Continuously migrating a database to a different engine without downtime","Providing a registry that stores and distributes container images","Importing and exporting virtual machine images to and from EC2"],"eEn":"VM Import/Export lets you import virtual machine images into EC2 and also export them from EC2. Continuous synchronization between on premises and S3 is DataSync, zero-downtime database migration is DMS, and storing and distributing container images is the role of ECR."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"スポットインスタンスのリスクとして正しいものはどれか。","o":["容量不足時の中断","起動に数時間かかる","料金が変動して高騰","最低1年の利用が必須"],"a":0,"e":"スポットインスタンスは余剰容量を割安に使える代わりに、AWSが容量を必要とすると中断されることがある。起動に数時間はかからず、価格はオンデマンドが上限で、最低1年の利用が必要なのはリザーブドインスタンスなどの約定型。","qEn":"Which is a correct risk of Spot Instances?","oEn":["Interruption when capacity is short","Launch takes several hours","Prices fluctuate and surge","A minimum of one year of use is required"],"eEn":"Spot Instances let you use spare capacity at a discount, but they can be interrupted when AWS needs the capacity back. Launch does not take hours, the price is capped at the On-Demand price, and a minimum one-year term is required for committed options such as Reserved Instances."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"EFS（Elastic File System）とEBS（Elastic Block Store）の最大の違いはどれか。","o":["EFSは単一AZ限定、EBSは複数リージョンに複製","EFSは複数同時マウント可、EBSは単一インスタンス専用","EFSはブロックストレージ、EBSはファイル共有向け","どちらもオブジェクトストレージでHTTP経由でアクセス"],"a":1,"e":"EFSは複数のEC2から同時にマウントして共有できるファイルシステムで、EBSは基本的に単一インスタンス専用のブロックストレージ。EFSは複数AZに対応し、ブロックとファイルの関係も逆ではなく、どちらもオブジェクトストレージではない。","qEn":"What is the biggest difference between EFS (Elastic File System) and EBS (Elastic Block Store)?","oEn":["EFS is limited to a single AZ, while EBS is replicated across multiple Regions","EFS can be mounted by many instances at once, while EBS is dedicated to a single instance","EFS is block storage, while EBS is for file sharing","Both are object storage accessed over HTTP"],"eEn":"EFS is a file system that multiple EC2 instances can mount simultaneously and share, while EBS is block storage that is basically dedicated to a single instance. EFS supports multiple AZs, the block and file roles are not reversed, and neither is object storage."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service） Intelligent-Tieringの利点はどれか。","o":["アクセスパターンに応じ自動で階層最適化","利用者が手動でライフサイクルを設定して移動","最も安価だが取り出しに追加料金が必ずかかる","取り出しに数時間かかる長期アーカイブ専用階層"],"a":0,"e":"利用状況に応じた自動移動。手動管理の不要化。","qEn":"What is the benefit of S3 Intelligent-Tiering?","oEn":["Automatically optimizes tiers based on access patterns","Users manually configure lifecycle rules to move data","The cheapest option, but retrieval always incurs extra charges","A tier dedicated to long-term archives with retrieval taking hours"],"eEn":"Data is moved automatically according to usage, which removes the need for manual management."},
  {"d":"D3","q":"DynamoDBグローバルテーブルの利点はどれか。","o":["単一リージョン内で複数AZへ同期複製する","複数リージョンへの自動複製と低遅延アクセス","SQLによる複雑な結合クエリを高速に実行","読み取り専用のリードレプリカを他リージョンに作成"],"a":1,"e":"DynamoDBグローバルテーブルは、複数のリージョンへテーブルを自動で複製し、利用者に近いリージョンから低遅延でアクセスできる。単一リージョン内の複数AZ複製は標準機能で、SQLの結合は不得意、読み取り専用の複製とは性質が違う。","qEn":"What is the benefit of DynamoDB global tables?","oEn":["Synchronously replicating across multiple AZs within a single Region","Automatic replication to multiple Regions and low-latency access","Running complex SQL join queries quickly","Creating read-only read replicas in other Regions"],"eEn":"DynamoDB global tables automatically replicate a table to multiple Regions, so users can access it with low latency from a Region close to them. Replication across multiple AZs in a single Region is a standard feature, SQL joins are not a strength, and read-only replication is different in nature."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"オンデマンド月額100ドルをリザーブドで40%割引にした場合の月額はいくらか。","o":["40ドル","計60ドル","80ドル","66ドル"],"a":1,"e":"100×0.6＝60ドル。長期コミットでの削減。","qEn":"If an On-Demand cost of $100 per month is reduced by 40% with Reserved Instances, what is the monthly cost?","oEn":["$40","$60","$80","$66"],"eEn":"100 x 0.6 = $60. This is the savings from a long-term commitment."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"S3（Simple Storage Service）標準に500GB保存、1GBあたり0.025ドルの場合のストレージ月額はいくらか。","o":["12.5ドル","6.25ドル","125ドル","1.25ドル"],"a":0,"e":"500×0.025＝12.5ドル。容量課金の基本。","qEn":"If you store 500 GB in S3 (Simple Storage Service) Standard at $0.025 per GB, what is the monthly storage cost?","oEn":["$12.5","$6.25","$125","$1.25"],"eEn":"500 x 0.025 = $12.5. This is the basic idea of capacity-based billing."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"0.05ドル/時のオンデマンドを24時間×30日稼働させた月額はいくらか。","o":["72ドル","36ドル","1.2ドル","3.6ドル"],"a":1,"e":"0.05×24×30＝36ドル。常時稼働ならRIで削減余地。","qEn":"What is the monthly cost of running an On-Demand instance at $0.05 per hour for 24 hours a day for 30 days?","oEn":["$72","$36","$1.2","$3.6"],"eEn":"0.05 x 24 x 30 = $36. For always-on workloads, there is room for savings with RIs."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"中断耐性のあるバッチで、オンデマンド月額200ドルをスポットで最大70%割引にできる場合の月額はいくらか。","o":["70ドル","140ドル","60ドル","30ドル"],"a":2,"e":"200×0.3＝60ドル。中断許容ワークロードでの大幅削減。","qEn":"For a batch job that tolerates interruption, if an On-Demand cost of $200 per month can be cut by up to 70% with Spot, what is the monthly cost?","oEn":["$70","$140","$60","$30"],"eEn":"200 x 0.3 = $60. This is a large saving for workloads that can tolerate interruption."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"リザーブドインスタンスの支払いオプションに含まれないものはどれか。","o":["毎月後払い割引","前払いなしの月払い","全額前払い","一部前払い"],"a":0,"e":"前払い・一部前払い・前払いなしの3種。前払いほど割引大。","qEn":"Which is NOT included in the payment options for Reserved Instances?","oEn":["Monthly postpaid discount","Monthly payments with no upfront payment","All upfront","Partial upfront"],"eEn":"There are three options: All Upfront, Partial Upfront, and No Upfront. The more you pay upfront, the larger the discount."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Savings Plansの2種類に含まれるものはどれか。","o":["ComputeとEC2 Instanceの2種","全額前払いと前払いなしの支払い2種類","StandardとConvertibleの2種類","オンデマンドとスポットインスタンスの2種類"],"a":0,"e":"Savings PlansにはComputeとEC2 Instanceの種類があり、Computeは柔軟、EC2 Instanceは特定のファミリーに限定される。全額前払いと前払いなしは支払い方法、StandardとConvertibleはリザーブドインスタンスの区分、スポットはSavings Plansの種類ではない。","qEn":"Which are the two types of AWS Savings Plans?","oEn":["Compute and EC2 Instance","Two payment types: All Upfront and No Upfront","Two types: Standard and Convertible","Two types: On-Demand and Spot Instances"],"eEn":"Savings Plans come in Compute and EC2 Instance types: Compute is flexible, while EC2 Instance is limited to a specific instance family. All Upfront and No Upfront are payment options, Standard and Convertible are Reserved Instance classes, and Spot is not a Savings Plans type."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の無料利用枠の3種類に含まれないものはどれか。","o":["永久全機能無料","12か月間無料","短期間のトライアル","無期限で常に無料"],"a":0,"e":"12か月無料・常に無料・トライアルの3種。","qEn":"Which is NOT one of the three types of the AWS Free Tier?","oEn":["Permanently free with all features","Free for 12 months","Short-term trials","Always free with no expiration"],"eEn":"The three types are 12 months free, always free, and trials."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"エンタープライズサポートが提供する独自の支援はどれか。","o":["専任TAM・ウェルアーキテクチャレビュー・コンシェルジュ","24時間365日の電話サポートと1時間以内の重大障害応答保証","営業時間内にメールで受けられる一般的な技術サポート","コミュニティフォーラムと基本的なドキュメントのみ"],"a":0,"e":"Enterprise Supportに特有なのは、専任のTAM、Well-Architectedレビュー、コンシェルジュによる支援。24時間365日の電話サポート、営業時間内のメール技術サポート、フォーラムとドキュメントのみの利用は、Enterprise固有の支援ではない。（2026年11月時点：現行プランでは専任TAMとWell-ArchitectedレビューはEnterprise SupportとUnified Operationsの両方に含まれ、Enterprise Supportの請求支援は「White-glove billing concierge」と記載されている）","qEn":"Which support is unique to Enterprise Support?","oEn":["A dedicated TAM, Well-Architected reviews, and a concierge","24/7 phone support and a guaranteed response within 1 hour for critical outages","General technical support by email during business hours","Community forums and basic documentation only"],"eEn":"What is unique to Enterprise Support is a dedicated TAM, Well-Architected reviews, and concierge assistance. 24/7 phone support, email technical support during business hours, and access to forums and documentation only are not support unique to Enterprise. (As of November 2026: under the current plans, a designated TAM and Well-Architected Reviews are included in both Enterprise Support and Unified Operations, and Enterprise Support lists its billing assistance as a white-glove billing concierge.)"},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Trusted Advisorのチェックカテゴリに含まれないものはどれか。","o":["UIデザイン","サービスの制限","セキュリティ","パフォーマンス"],"a":0,"e":"Trusted Advisor のチェックは、コスト最適化・パフォーマンス・セキュリティ・回復力（レジリエンス）・運用上の優秀性・サービスの制限の6カテゴリ（2026年11月時点）。UI デザインはチェックの対象外である。","qEn":"Which is NOT a check category of AWS Trusted Advisor?","oEn":["UI design","Service limits","Security","Performance"],"eEn":"Trusted Advisor checks fall into six categories: cost optimization, performance, security, resilience, operational excellence and service limits (as of November 2026). UI design is not one of them."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"同一リージョン内・同一AZ（Availability Zone）内の通信料金の傾向はどれか。","o":["AZ内は無料または低額、リージョン跨ぎは課金","リージョン跨ぎの通信は完全に無料で提供される","同一AZ内でも常にGB単位で高額に課金される","インターネットへの受信（イン）通信に課金される"],"a":0,"e":"同一AZ内のプライベートIPでの通信は無料または低額で、リージョンをまたぐ通信は課金される。リージョン跨ぎが完全に無料とは言えず、同一AZ内が常に高額なわけでもなく、インターネットからの受信通信は通常課金されない。","qEn":"Which describes the tendency of data transfer charges within the same Region and within the same AZ (Availability Zone)?","oEn":["Free or low cost within an AZ, charged across Regions","Cross-Region traffic is provided completely free","Always billed at a high per-GB rate even within the same AZ","Inbound traffic from the internet is charged"],"eEn":"Communication using private IP addresses within the same AZ is free or low cost, and communication across Regions is charged. It cannot be said that cross-Region traffic is completely free, same-AZ traffic is not always expensive, and inbound traffic from the internet is normally not charged."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services）の料金が「リージョンによって異なる」理由はどれか。","o":["全リージョン料金は統一","為替レートが固定だから","各地のコスト構造の違い","各地の利用者数が均一だから"],"a":2,"e":"リージョンごとに電力、土地、人件費、税などのコスト構造が異なるため、同じサービスでも料金が変わる。全リージョン料金が統一という前提は誤りで、為替レートの固定や利用者数の均一は理由にならない。","qEn":"Why do AWS prices \"differ by Region\"?","oEn":["Prices are uniform in all Regions","Because exchange rates are fixed","Differences in the cost structure of each location","Because the number of users is uniform in each location"],"eEn":"Costs such as electricity, land, labor, and taxes differ by Region, so the same service is priced differently. The premise that prices are uniform in all Regions is wrong, and fixed exchange rates or a uniform number of users are not reasons."},
  {"d":"D4","q":"AWS（Amazon Web Services） Cost Categoriesの用途はどれか。","o":["設定した予算を超えるとアラートを通知する","将来のコストを事前に見積もって試算する","利用傾向から異常な支出を機械学習で検知する","コストを独自のグループに分類・集計"],"a":3,"e":"Cost Categoriesは、コストを独自のルールでチームやプロジェクトなどのグループに分類し、集計する機能。予算超過のアラートはBudgets、将来コストの試算はPricing Calculator、異常検知はCost Anomaly Detectionの役割。","qEn":"What is the purpose of AWS Cost Categories?","oEn":["Sending alerts when a set budget is exceeded","Estimating future costs in advance","Using machine learning to detect abnormal spending from usage trends","Classifying and aggregating costs into custom groups"],"eEn":"Cost Categories is a feature that classifies and aggregates costs into groups such as teams or projects using your own rules. Alerts for budget overruns are the role of Budgets, estimating future costs is the Pricing Calculator, and anomaly detection is Cost Anomaly Detection."}];

var SET5 = [{"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの「従量課金制（Pay-as-you-go）」が示す料金モデルとして最も適切なものはどれか。","o":["使った分だけ支払う","年間固定料金を前払いする","無料で無制限に使える","利用量に関わらず定額"],"a":0,"e":"従量課金制は実際に消費したリソース量に応じて課金される。事前の大きな設備投資が不要になる。","qEn":"Which best describes the pricing model indicated by the cloud's \"pay-as-you-go\" model?","oEn":["Pay only for what you use","Prepay a fixed annual fee","Unlimited use at no cost","A flat fee regardless of usage"],"eEn":"With pay-as-you-go, you are billed according to the amount of resources you actually consume. It removes the need for a large upfront capital investment."},{"d":"D1","q":"クラウド導入により、初期の設備投資（CapEx）は一般的にどのような支出へ変化するか。","o":["変動しない固定資産のまま","運用支出（OpEx）","減価償却費のみ","人件費のみ"],"a":1,"e":"サーバー購入などのCapExが、使った分を払うOpExへ移行し、キャッシュフローが柔軟になる。","qEn":"When adopting the cloud, what kind of expense does the initial capital expenditure (CapEx) generally turn into?","oEn":["It remains a fixed asset that does not change","Operating expenditure (OpEx)","Depreciation expense only","Personnel costs only"],"eEn":"CapEx such as server purchases shifts to OpEx, where you pay for what you use, which makes cash flow more flexible."},{"d":"D1","q":"多数の顧客の需要を集約することでAWSが単価を下げられる仕組みを何と呼ぶか。","o":["弾力性","フォールトトレランス","規模の経済","疎結合"],"a":2,"e":"規模の経済（economies of scale）により、大量利用で調達コストが下がり価格に還元される。","qEn":"What is the mechanism called by which AWS can lower unit prices by aggregating the demand of many customers?","oEn":["Elasticity","Fault tolerance","Economies of scale","Loose coupling"],"eEn":"Thanks to economies of scale, procurement costs fall with large-volume usage and are passed on in prices."},{"d":"D1","q":"需要の増減に応じてリソースを自動的に増減できるクラウドの特性を何というか。","o":["俊敏性","移植性","冗長性","高い弾力性"],"a":3,"e":"弾力性（elasticity）は負荷に応じてリソースを拡張・縮小する能力を指す。","qEn":"What is the cloud characteristic of automatically increasing or decreasing resources as demand rises and falls called?","oEn":["Agility","Portability","Redundancy","Elasticity"],"eEn":"Elasticity refers to the ability to expand and shrink resources according to load."},{"d":"D1","q":"新しいアイデアを短時間で試作・展開できるクラウドの利点を最もよく表す語はどれか。","o":["俊敏性（アジリティ）","長期的な持続可能性の維持","一貫性","可搬性"],"a":0,"e":"クラウドは調達の待ち時間がなく、迅速にリソースを用意できるため俊敏性が高い。","qEn":"Which term best expresses the cloud benefit of being able to prototype and deploy new ideas in a short time?","oEn":["Agility","Maintaining long-term sustainability","Consistency","Portability"],"eEn":"The cloud has no procurement wait and can prepare resources quickly, so agility is high."},{"d":"D1","q":"AWSのグローバルインフラにおける「リージョン」の説明として最も適切なものはどれか。","o":["単一の物理データセンター施設","地理的に離れた独立エリア","CDNの配信拠点","IAMの管理単位"],"a":1,"e":"リージョンは世界各地の地理的エリアで、複数のアベイラビリティーゾーンで構成される。","qEn":"Which best describes a \"Region\" in the AWS global infrastructure?","oEn":["A single physical data center facility","A geographically separate, independent area","A CDN delivery location","A management unit of IAM"],"eEn":"A Region is a geographic area around the world and consists of multiple Availability Zones."},{"d":"D1","q":"アベイラビリティーゾーン（AZ）の説明として正しいものはどれか。","o":["リージョンをまたぐ単一の物理サーバー機器","課金の単位","リージョン内の独立したデータセンター群","IAMポリシーの一種"],"a":2,"e":"AZは1つ以上のデータセンターから成り、リージョン内で物理的に分離され高可用性を実現する。","qEn":"Which correctly describes an Availability Zone (AZ)?","oEn":["A single physical server device that spans Regions","A unit of billing","A group of independent data centers within a Region","A type of IAM policy"],"eEn":"An AZ consists of one or more data centers that are physically separated within a Region to achieve high availability."},{"d":"D1","q":"エンドユーザーに近い場所でコンテンツを配信し遅延を減らすAWSの拠点を何というか。","o":["プライベートサブネット","AZ","VPC","エッジロケーション"],"a":3,"e":"エッジロケーションはCloudFrontなどが利用し、ユーザー近傍でキャッシュ配信して低遅延化する。","qEn":"What is the AWS location that delivers content close to end users to reduce latency called?","oEn":["Private subnet","AZ","VPC","Edge location"],"eEn":"Edge locations are used by services such as CloudFront to cache and deliver content near users, reducing latency."},{"d":"D1","q":"単一障害点を避け可用性を高める設計として、CLF-C02で推奨される基本方針はどれか。","o":["複数のAZに分散する","1つのAZに集約する","オンプレのみで運用する","バックアップを取らない"],"a":0,"e":"複数AZへ分散配置することで、1つのAZ障害時もサービスを継続でき高可用性が得られる。","qEn":"Which is the basic policy recommended in CLF-C02 for avoiding single points of failure and improving availability?","oEn":["Distribute across multiple AZs","Consolidate in a single AZ","Operate on premises only","Do not take backups"],"eEn":"By deploying across multiple AZs, the service can keep running even if one AZ fails, which provides high availability."},{"d":"D1","q":"AWS Well-Architected Framework の柱に含まれないものは次のうちどれか。","o":["セキュリティ","マーケティング","コスト最適化","運用上の優秀性"],"a":1,"e":"6本の柱は運用上の優秀性・セキュリティ・信頼性・パフォーマンス効率・コスト最適化・持続可能性。","qEn":"Which of the following is NOT a pillar of the AWS Well-Architected Framework?","oEn":["Security","Marketing","Cost Optimization","Operational Excellence"],"eEn":"The six pillars are Operational Excellence, Security, Reliability, Performance Efficiency, Cost Optimization, and Sustainability."},{"d":"D1","q":"クラウド移行の判断材料となる「総所有コスト（TCO）」が主に比較するものはどれか。","o":["ブランド認知度の向上率","従業員満足度","保有・運用の総コスト","市場シェア"],"a":2,"e":"TCOはハード・保守・電力・人件費など保有と運用の総費用を評価し、オンプレとクラウドを比較する。","qEn":"What does \"total cost of ownership (TCO),\" a basis for deciding on cloud migration, mainly compare?","oEn":["The rate of improvement in brand awareness","Employee satisfaction","The total cost of ownership and operation","Market share"],"eEn":"TCO evaluates the total cost of owning and operating, including hardware, maintenance, power, and personnel, and is used to compare on premises with the cloud."},{"d":"D1","q":"利用前に月額コストを見積もるためのAWS公式ツールはどれか。","o":["AWS Cost and Usage Report","Amazon Athena","AWS Glue","AWS Pricing Calculator"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Pricing Calculatorは構成に基づくおおよその費用を事前に見積もれる無料ツール。","qEn":"Which official AWS tool estimates monthly costs before you use the services?","eEn":"AWS Pricing Calculator is a free tool that lets you estimate the approximate cost of a configuration in advance."},{"d":"D1","q":"負荷に応じてEC2インスタンス数を自動調整するAWSの機能はどれか。","o":["Auto Scaling","CloudTrail","Amazon Route 53","AWS Config"],"a":0,"e":"Auto Scalingは需要に合わせてインスタンス数を増減し、可用性とコスト効率を両立する。","qEn":"Which AWS feature automatically adjusts the number of EC2 instances according to load?","eEn":"Auto Scaling increases and decreases the number of instances to match demand, balancing availability and cost efficiency."},{"d":"D1","q":"サーバーのプロビジョニングや管理なしにコードを実行できるAWSサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon EC2","AWS Lambda","Amazon EBS","AWS Direct Connect"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Lambdaはサーバーレスで、インフラ管理不要・実行時間に応じた課金でコードを実行する。","qEn":"Which AWS service lets you run code without provisioning or managing servers?","eEn":"AWS Lambda is serverless: it runs code with no infrastructure management and is billed according to execution time."},{"d":"D1","q":"IaaS・PaaS・SaaS のうち、OSやミドルウェアの管理を利用者が行わずアプリのみ使う形態はどれか。","o":["IaaS","PaaS","SaaS","オンプレミス"],"a":2,"e":"SaaSは完成されたアプリを利用する形態で、利用者はインフラや基盤を管理しない。","qEn":"Among IaaS, PaaS, and SaaS, which model lets users simply use the application without managing the OS or middleware?","oEn":["IaaS","PaaS","SaaS","On premises"],"eEn":"SaaS is a model in which you use a finished application, and the user does not manage the infrastructure or platform."},{"d":"D1","q":"オンプレミスとクラウドを組み合わせて利用するデプロイモデルを何と呼ぶか。","o":["マルチテナント","パブリッククラウドのみ","エッジコンピューティング","ハイブリッドクラウド"],"a":3,"e":"ハイブリッドクラウドはオンプレとクラウドを連携させ、要件に応じて使い分ける構成。","qEn":"What is the deployment model that combines on-premises and cloud use called?","oEn":["Multi-tenant","Public cloud only","Edge computing","Hybrid cloud"],"eEn":"Hybrid cloud is a configuration that connects on premises with the cloud and uses each according to requirements."},{"d":"D1","q":"Well-Architected Framework の「信頼性」の柱が主に目指すものはどれか。","o":["障害からの復旧と可用性維持","広告費の削減","開発言語の統一","デザインとブランドの一貫性向上"],"a":0,"e":"信頼性の柱は、障害からの復旧や需要変化への対応など、期待どおり機能し続ける能力を扱う。","qEn":"What does the \"Reliability\" pillar of the Well-Architected Framework mainly aim for?","oEn":["Recovering from failures and maintaining availability","Reducing advertising costs","Standardizing development languages","Improving consistency of design and branding"],"eEn":"The Reliability pillar deals with the ability to keep functioning as expected, including recovering from failures and adapting to changes in demand."},{"d":"D1","q":"一部のコンポーネントが故障してもシステム全体が動作を続けられる特性を何というか。","o":["課金モデル","フォールトトレランス","垂直統合","シングルテナント構成"],"a":1,"e":"フォールトトレランスは冗長化により部分故障時もサービスを継続できる設計特性。","qEn":"What is the characteristic called that allows the whole system to keep operating even if some components fail?","oEn":["Billing model","Fault tolerance","Vertical integration","Single-tenant configuration"],"eEn":"Fault tolerance is a design characteristic in which redundancy lets the service continue even when part of the system fails."},{"d":"D1","q":"クラウドがグローバル展開のスピードで優れる主な理由として最も適切なものはどれか。","o":["専用線が不要になるため","各国へ物理サーバーを郵送して設置するため","世界中のリージョンに数分で展開できる","法律が不要になるため"],"a":2,"e":"AWSの世界規模のインフラを使えば、数クリックで各地リージョンにアプリを展開できる。","qEn":"Which is the best reason the cloud excels in the speed of global expansion?","oEn":["Because dedicated lines become unnecessary","Because physical servers are mailed to each country and installed","Because you can deploy to Regions around the world in minutes","Because laws become unnecessary"],"eEn":"With AWS's worldwide infrastructure, you can deploy applications to Regions in different locations with a few clicks."},{"d":"D1","q":"マネージドサービスを利用する主な利点として最も適切なものはどれか。","o":["法令遵守が免除される","料金が必ず無料になる","セキュリティ対策が一切不要になる","運用管理の負担が軽減される"],"a":3,"e":"マネージドサービスはパッチ適用や運用の多くをAWSが担い、利用者は本業に集中できる。","qEn":"Which is the best statement of the main benefit of using managed services?","oEn":["Exemption from legal compliance","Prices are always free","No security measures are needed at all","A reduced operational management burden"],"eEn":"With managed services, AWS handles much of the patching and operations, so customers can focus on their core business."},{"d":"D1","q":"垂直スケーリング（スケールアップ）の説明として正しいものはどれか。","o":["インスタンスの性能を上げる","インスタンスの台数を増やす","リージョンを増やす","ストレージを削除する"],"a":0,"e":"スケールアップは単一インスタンスのCPUやメモリを増強すること。数を増やすのはスケールアウト。","qEn":"Which correctly describes vertical scaling (scaling up)?","oEn":["Increasing the performance of an instance","Increasing the number of instances","Adding more Regions","Deleting storage"],"eEn":"Scaling up means increasing the CPU and memory of a single instance. Increasing the number of instances is scaling out."},{"d":"D1","q":"クラウドの利点として「キャパシティの推測が不要になる」とはどういう意味か。","o":["容量のことを一切考えなくてよい","必要な分だけ動的に確保できる","無限に無料","監視が不要"],"a":1,"e":"需要に応じてリソースを調達・解放できるため、事前の過剰・過少な容量見積もりが不要になる。","qEn":"What does the cloud benefit \"stop guessing capacity\" mean?","oEn":["You do not need to think about capacity at all","You can allocate just what you need dynamically","Unlimited and free","Monitoring is not needed"],"eEn":"Because you can acquire and release resources according to demand, there is no need to estimate capacity in advance and risk over- or under-provisioning."},{"d":"D1","q":"AWSのグローバルインフラを活用してユーザーに近い拠点から配信する主な効果はどれか。","o":["IAMの不要化","課金の停止","レイテンシー（遅延）の低減","通信の暗号化が不要になること"],"a":2,"e":"ユーザー近傍のリージョンやエッジから配信することで通信遅延を抑え、体験を向上できる。","qEn":"What is the main effect of using the AWS global infrastructure to deliver from locations close to users?","oEn":["IAM becomes unnecessary","Billing stops","Reduced latency","Encrypting communication becomes unnecessary"],"eEn":"Delivering from Regions or edge locations near users reduces communication delay and improves the user experience."},{"d":"D1","q":"Well-Architected Framework の「持続可能性」の柱が主に重視するものはどれか。","o":["開発者の人数","広告収益の最大化と拡大","UIの美しさ","環境への影響の低減"],"a":3,"e":"持続可能性の柱は、エネルギー消費など環境負荷を最小化する設計・運用を重視する。","qEn":"What does the \"Sustainability\" pillar of the Well-Architected Framework mainly emphasize?","oEn":["The number of developers","Maximizing and expanding advertising revenue","The beauty of the UI","Reducing environmental impact"],"eEn":"The Sustainability pillar emphasizes design and operation that minimize environmental impact, such as energy consumption."},{"d":"D1","q":"複数の小さな独立した部品でシステムを構成し依存を減らす設計原則を何というか。","o":["疎結合","密結合","単一障害点化","垂直統合"],"a":0,"e":"疎結合（loose coupling）は各コンポーネントの依存を弱め、障害の波及を抑え拡張性を高める。","qEn":"What is the design principle called that builds a system from multiple small, independent parts to reduce dependencies?","oEn":["Loose coupling","Tight coupling","Making a single point of failure","Vertical integration"],"eEn":"Loose coupling weakens the dependencies between components, limiting the spread of failures and improving scalability."},{"d":"D2","q":"AWS責任共有モデルにおいて、AWSが責任を負う範囲として最も適切なものはどれか。","o":["ゲストOSのパッチ適用","クラウドの物理インフラ","IAMユーザーの権限設定","アプリのソースコード"],"a":1,"e":"AWSは「クラウドのセキュリティ」（物理施設・ハード・基盤）を担う。設定やデータは利用者責任。","qEn":"In the AWS shared responsibility model, which best describes what AWS is responsible for?","oEn":["Patching the guest OS","The cloud's physical infrastructure","Setting IAM user permissions","The application's source code"],"eEn":"AWS is responsible for \"security of the cloud\" (physical facilities, hardware, and the underlying infrastructure). Configuration and data are the customer's responsibility."},{"d":"D2","q":"責任共有モデルで、利用者（顧客）が責任を負う典型例はどれか。","o":["データセンターの警備","ハイパーバイザーの保守","IAMの権限管理とデータ暗号化","物理ネットワーク機器の保守管理"],"a":2,"e":"利用者は「クラウド内のセキュリティ」（データ・アクセス管理・OS設定など）を担う。","qEn":"In the shared responsibility model, which is a typical example of what the customer is responsible for?","oEn":["Data center security guards","Hypervisor maintenance","IAM permission management and data encryption","Maintenance of physical network equipment"],"eEn":"Customers are responsible for \"security in the cloud\" (data, access management, OS settings, and so on)."},{"d":"D2","q":"AWSリソースへのアクセスを人やグループ単位で管理するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon SQS","Amazon S3","AWS Lambda","AWS IAM"],"a":3,"e":"IAM（Identity and Access Management）はユーザー・グループ・ロール・ポリシーで権限を制御する。","qEn":"Which service manages access to AWS resources by person or group?","eEn":"IAM (Identity and Access Management) controls permissions using users, groups, roles, and policies."},{"d":"D2","q":"EC2などのAWSサービスに一時的な権限を委譲する際に用いる仕組みはどれか。","o":["IAMロール","IAMパスワード","ルートキー","アクセスログ"],"a":0,"e":"IAMロールは一時的な認証情報を付与し、長期的なアクセスキーの埋め込みを避けられる。","qEn":"Which mechanism is used to delegate temporary permissions to AWS services such as EC2?","oEn":["IAM role","IAM password","Root key","Access log"],"eEn":"An IAM role grants temporary credentials, which avoids embedding long-term access keys."},{"d":"D2","q":"IAMで推奨される「最小権限の原則」の説明として正しいものはどれか。","o":["全ての利用者に管理者権限を与える","業務に必要な権限のみ付与する","権限を一切与えない","ルートで全操作する"],"a":1,"e":"最小権限の原則は、タスク遂行に必要な最小限の権限だけを付与しリスクを抑える考え方。","qEn":"Which correctly describes the IAM-recommended \"principle of least privilege\"?","oEn":["Give administrator permissions to all users","Grant only the permissions needed for the job","Grant no permissions at all","Perform all operations as root"],"eEn":"The principle of least privilege is the idea of granting only the minimum permissions needed to perform a task, which reduces risk."},{"d":"D2","q":"AWSアカウントのルートユーザーの扱いとして最も適切なものはどれか。","o":["日常業務で常用する","全社員に共有する","MFAを有効化し限定的に使う","アクセスキーを社外に公開する"],"a":2,"e":"ルートユーザーは強力なため、MFAで保護し日常はIAMユーザー/ロールを使うのが推奨される。","qEn":"Which best describes how to handle the root user of an AWS account?","oEn":["Use it routinely for daily work","Share it with all employees","Enable MFA and use it only in limited cases","Publish the access keys outside the company"],"eEn":"The root user is very powerful, so it is recommended to protect it with MFA and use IAM users or roles for daily work."},{"d":"D2","q":"パスワードに加えワンタイムコードなどで本人確認を強化する仕組みを何というか。","o":["ロードバランシング機能","単一サインオン","暗号化","多要素認証（MFA）"],"a":3,"e":"MFAはパスワードに加え第2の要素を要求し、認証情報漏えい時の不正アクセスを防ぐ。","qEn":"What is the mechanism called that strengthens identity verification by using a one-time code or similar in addition to a password?","oEn":["Load balancing feature","Single sign-on","Encryption","Multi-factor authentication (MFA)"],"eEn":"MFA requires a second factor in addition to the password, which prevents unauthorized access if credentials are leaked."},{"d":"D2","q":"複数のAWSアカウントを一元管理し、SCPで権限を制御できるサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Organizations","Amazon Route 53","Amazon CloudWatch","Amazon EFS"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Organizationsは複数アカウントを統合管理し、SCPで組織全体の権限上限を設定できる。","qEn":"Which service centrally manages multiple AWS accounts and can control permissions with SCPs?","eEn":"AWS Organizations manages multiple accounts in a unified way and can set the maximum permissions for the whole organization with SCPs."},{"d":"D2","q":"暗号化キーの作成・管理・使用制御を一元的に行うAWSサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Athena","AWS KMS","AWS Glue","Amazon SNS"],"a":1,"e":"AWS KMS（Key Management Service）は暗号鍵を管理し、各サービスの暗号化を統合的に扱える。","qEn":"Which AWS service centrally creates, manages, and controls the use of encryption keys?","eEn":"AWS KMS (Key Management Service) manages encryption keys and handles encryption across services in an integrated way."},{"d":"D2","q":"専用ハードウェアで暗号鍵を管理し、厳格なコンプライアンス要件に対応するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CodeCommit","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS CloudHSM","Amazon Comprehend"],"a":2,"e":"CloudHSMは専用のハードウェアセキュリティモジュールを提供し、利用者が鍵を単独管理できる。","qEn":"Which service manages encryption keys on dedicated hardware and supports strict compliance requirements?","eEn":"CloudHSM provides dedicated hardware security modules, and the customer can manage the keys exclusively."},{"d":"D2","q":"DDoS攻撃からアプリケーションを保護するAWSのマネージドサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon EFS","Amazon Redshift","AWS Glue","AWS Shield"],"a":3,"e":"AWS ShieldはDDoS攻撃を検知・緩和する。StandardとAdvancedの2階層がある。","qEn":"Which AWS managed service protects applications from DDoS attacks?","eEn":"AWS Shield detects and mitigates DDoS attacks. It has two tiers, Standard and Advanced."},{"d":"D2","q":"SQLインジェクション等の一般的なWeb攻撃をルールでブロックできるサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS WAF","Amazon EBS","AWS Snowball","Amazon Polly"],"a":0,"e":"AWS WAF（Web Application Firewall）はHTTP/Sリクエストを検査し悪意ある通信を遮断する。","qEn":"Which service can block common web attacks such as SQL injection using rules?","eEn":"AWS WAF (Web Application Firewall) inspects HTTP/S requests and blocks malicious traffic."},{"d":"D2","q":"機械学習で不審なアクティビティや脅威を継続的に検出するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon QuickSight","Amazon GuardDuty","AWS Amplify","Amazon MQ"],"a":1,"e":"GuardDutyはログを分析し、異常なAPI呼び出しや不正アクセスなどの脅威を検出する。","qEn":"Which service uses machine learning to continuously detect suspicious activity and threats?","eEn":"GuardDuty analyzes logs and detects threats such as abnormal API calls and unauthorized access."},{"d":"D2","q":"EC2やコンテナの脆弱性・意図しない公開を自動評価するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Step Functions","Amazon Kinesis","Amazon Inspector","Amazon Lightsail"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon Inspectorはワークロードの脆弱性やネットワーク到達性を自動でスキャン評価する。","qEn":"Which service automatically assesses EC2 instances and containers for vulnerabilities and unintended exposure?","eEn":"Amazon Inspector automatically scans and assesses workloads for vulnerabilities and network reachability."},{"d":"D2","q":"S3内の個人情報（PII）などの機密データを機械学習で検出・分類するサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS DataSync","AWS Fargate","Amazon Neptune","Amazon Macie"],"a":3,"e":"Amazon MacieはS3の機密データを自動検出・分類し、データ保護のリスクを可視化する。","qEn":"Which service uses machine learning to detect and classify sensitive data such as personally identifiable information (PII) in S3?","eEn":"Amazon Macie automatically discovers and classifies sensitive data in S3 and visualizes data protection risks."},{"d":"D2","q":"アカウント内のAPI呼び出し履歴を記録し、監査やガバナンスに用いるサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CloudTrail","Amazon SES","AWS Outposts","Amazon Cognito"],"a":0,"e":"CloudTrailは誰がいつ何のAPIを呼んだかを記録し、監査・コンプライアンスに活用される。","qEn":"Which service records the history of API calls in an account and is used for auditing and governance?","eEn":"CloudTrail records who called which API and when, and is used for auditing and compliance."},{"d":"D2","q":"AWSリソースの構成変更を記録し、望ましい設定への準拠を評価するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Aurora","AWS Config","AWS Glue","Amazon Rekognition"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Configはリソース構成の変更履歴を追跡し、ルールに基づく準拠状況を評価する。","qEn":"Which service records configuration changes to AWS resources and evaluates compliance with desired settings?","eEn":"AWS Config tracks the configuration change history of resources and evaluates compliance status based on rules."},{"d":"D2","q":"SOCやISOなどのコンプライアンス報告書をオンデマンドで入手できるサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS CloudFormation","Amazon EMR","AWS Artifact","Amazon FSx"],"a":2,"e":"AWS ArtifactはAWSの第三者監査レポートやコンプライアンス文書をダウンロードできるポータル。","qEn":"Which service lets you obtain compliance reports such as SOC and ISO on demand?","eEn":"AWS Artifact is a portal where you can download AWS's third-party audit reports and compliance documents."},{"d":"D2","q":"データベースの認証情報などのシークレットを安全に保存し自動ローテーションできるサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS Certificate Manager","Amazon CloudFront","AWS Direct Connect","AWS Secrets Manager"],"a":3,"e":"Secrets Managerはパスワードやトークンを暗号化保管し、定期的な自動ローテーションに対応する。","qEn":"Which service securely stores secrets such as database credentials and can rotate them automatically?","eEn":"Secrets Manager stores passwords and tokens in encrypted form and supports regular automatic rotation."},{"d":"D2","q":"Webやモバイルアプリにサインアップ・サインインなどのユーザー認証を追加するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Cognito","AWS Snowmobile","Amazon Athena","AWS Glue"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon Cognitoはユーザープールで認証を提供し、アプリのサインイン/サインアップを実現する。","qEn":"Which service adds user authentication, such as sign-up and sign-in, to web and mobile apps?","eEn":"Amazon Cognito provides authentication through user pools and enables sign-in and sign-up for apps."},{"d":"D2","q":"コスト・パフォーマンス・セキュリティなどをベストプラクティスに照らして助言するサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Kinesis Data Streams","AWS Trusted Advisor","AWS CodeBuild","Amazon Textract"],"a":1,"e":"Trusted Advisor は、コスト最適化・パフォーマンス・回復力・セキュリティ・運用上の優秀性・サービスの制限の6カテゴリ（2026年11月時点）でベストプラクティスに照らして環境を点検し、改善の推奨事項を示す。","qEn":"Which service gives advice on cost, performance, security, and more against best practices?","eEn":"Trusted Advisor checks your environment against best practices in six categories (cost optimization, performance, resilience, security, operational excellence and service limits, as of November 2026) and recommends improvements."},{"d":"D2","q":"EC2インスタンスへの通信をポート・プロトコル単位で制御する仮想ファイアウォールはどれか。","o":["KMSキー","IAMポリシー","セキュリティグループ","Amazon Route 53"],"a":2,"e":"セキュリティグループはインスタンスレベルで許可ルールを定義するステートフルなファイアウォール。","qEn":"Which virtual firewall controls traffic to an EC2 instance by port and protocol?","oEn":["KMS key","IAM policy","Security group","Amazon Route 53"],"eEn":"A security group is a stateful firewall that defines allow rules at the instance level."},{"d":"D2","q":"データを「保存時（at rest）」と「転送時（in transit）」に守る方法として適切な組み合わせはどれか。","o":["ログ削除と匿名化なし","公開バケットと平文","権限共有とHTTP","暗号化とTLS通信"],"a":3,"e":"保存時はストレージ暗号化、転送時はTLS/SSLで通信を暗号化し、データを両面で保護する。","qEn":"Which combination is appropriate for protecting data \"at rest\" and \"in transit\"?","oEn":["Deleting logs and no anonymization","Public buckets and plaintext","Shared permissions and HTTP","Encryption and TLS communication"],"eEn":"Data at rest is protected with storage encryption and data in transit with TLS/SSL-encrypted communication, so the data is protected in both states."},{"d":"D2","q":"複数アカウント・アプリへのシングルサインオン（SSO）を提供するAWSサービスはどれか。","o":["AWS IAM Identity Center","Amazon Elastic File System","AWS Glue","Amazon SQS"],"a":0,"e":"IAM Identity Center（旧AWS SSO）は複数アカウントやアプリへのSSOと一元的なアクセス管理を提供する。","qEn":"Which AWS service provides single sign-on (SSO) to multiple accounts and applications?","eEn":"IAM Identity Center (formerly AWS SSO) provides SSO to multiple accounts and applications along with centralized access management."},{"d":"D2","q":"複数のセキュリティサービスの検出結果を集約し、全体像を一元的に把握できるサービスはどれか。","o":["Amazon Polly","AWS Security Hub","AWS Data Pipeline","Amazon Lightsail"],"a":1,"e":"Security HubはGuardDutyやInspectorなどの結果を統合し、セキュリティ状態を一元管理する。","qEn":"Which service aggregates the findings of multiple security services so you can see the overall picture in one place?","eEn":"Security Hub integrates the results of services such as GuardDuty and Inspector and manages security posture centrally."},{"d":"D3","q":"仮想サーバーをクラウド上で起動し、必要に応じて台数を増減できるAWSのコンピューティングサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon EC2","Amazon S3","Amazon RDS","Amazon VPC"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon EC2はスケーラブルな仮想サーバー（インスタンス）を提供する中核的なコンピューティングサービスです。","qEn":"Which AWS compute service lets you launch virtual servers in the cloud and increase or decrease their number as needed?","eEn":"Amazon EC2 is a core compute service that provides scalable virtual servers (instances)."},{"d":"D3","q":"サーバーの管理を意識せずにコードを実行でき、実行時間に対して課金されるAWSのサーバーレスサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon EC2","AWS Lambda（関数）","Amazon EBS","Amazon EFS"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Lambdaはサーバー管理不要でコードを実行し、実行時間とリクエスト数に応じて課金されます。","qEn":"Which AWS serverless service lets you run code without thinking about server management and is billed for execution time?","eEn":"AWS Lambda runs code without server management and is billed according to execution time and the number of requests."},{"d":"D3","q":"耐久性が非常に高く、静的ファイルや画像などを保存するAWSのオブジェクトストレージはどれですか？","o":["Amazon EBS","Amazon EFS","Amazon S3","Amazon FSx"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon S3はオブジェクトストレージで、99.999999999%（イレブンナイン）の高い耐久性を提供します。","qEn":"Which AWS object storage has very high durability and stores static files, images, and the like?","eEn":"Amazon S3 is object storage that provides a high durability of 99.999999999% (eleven nines)."},{"d":"D3","q":"EC2インスタンスにアタッチして使う、永続的なブロックストレージボリュームを提供するサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon S3 Glacier","Amazon CloudFront","Amazon Route 53","Amazon EBS"],"a":3,"e":"Amazon EBSはEC2にアタッチするブロックストレージで、インスタンス停止後もデータを保持します。","qEn":"Which service provides persistent block storage volumes that you attach to EC2 instances?","eEn":"Amazon EBS is block storage that attaches to EC2 and retains data even after the instance is stopped."},{"d":"D3","q":"アクセス頻度が低く長期アーカイブ向けで、取り出しに時間がかかる代わりに安価なS3のストレージクラスはどれですか？","o":["S3 Glacier Deep Archive","S3 標準","S3 標準-IA","S3 Intelligent-Tiering 自動階層化"],"a":0,"e":"S3 Glacier Deep Archiveは最も低コストで、めったにアクセスしない長期アーカイブデータに適します。","qEn":"Which S3 storage class is for long-term archives that are rarely accessed, and is cheap in exchange for slow retrieval?","oEn":["S3 Glacier Deep Archive","S3 Standard","S3 Standard-IA","S3 Intelligent-Tiering automatic tiering"],"eEn":"S3 Glacier Deep Archive has the lowest cost and is suited to long-term archive data that is rarely accessed."},{"d":"D3","q":"MySQLやPostgreSQLなどのリレーショナルデータベースをマネージドで運用できるAWSのサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon RDS","Amazon Redshift","Amazon ElastiCache"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon RDSはパッチ適用やバックアップを自動化するマネージドなリレーショナルデータベースサービスです。","qEn":"Which AWS service lets you run relational databases such as MySQL and PostgreSQL as a managed service?","eEn":"Amazon RDS is a managed relational database service that automates patching and backups."},{"d":"D3","q":"ミリ秒単位の応答を求められるキーバリュー型・ドキュメント型のフルマネージドNoSQLデータベースはどれですか？","o":["Amazon Aurora","Amazon RDS for MySQL","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon Neptune"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon DynamoDBは高速で予測可能な性能を持つサーバーレスのNoSQLデータベースです。","qEn":"Which fully managed NoSQL database, of the key-value and document types, is required for millisecond responses?","eEn":"Amazon DynamoDB is a serverless NoSQL database with fast, predictable performance."},{"d":"D3","q":"ペタバイト規模のデータを高速に分析できる、AWSのフルマネージドなデータウェアハウスサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon Athena","Amazon RDS","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon Redshift（DWH）"],"a":3,"e":"Amazon Redshiftは大規模データの分析（OLAP）に最適化されたデータウェアハウスサービスです。","qEn":"Which AWS fully managed data warehouse service can analyze petabyte-scale data quickly?","eEn":"Amazon Redshift is a data warehouse service optimized for large-scale data analysis (OLAP)."},{"d":"D3","q":"AWS上に論理的に分離された自分専用の仮想ネットワーク空間を構築できるサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon VPC","Amazon Route 53","AWS Direct Connect","Amazon CloudFront"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon VPC（Virtual Private Cloud）はユーザー専用の隔離された仮想ネットワークを提供します。","qEn":"Which service lets you build your own logically isolated virtual network space on AWS?","eEn":"Amazon VPC (Virtual Private Cloud) provides an isolated virtual network dedicated to the user."},{"d":"D3","q":"ドメイン名をIPアドレスに変換する、AWSのDNS（ドメインネームシステム）サービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon CloudFront","Amazon Route 53","AWS Global Accelerator","Amazon VPC"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon Route 53はスケーラブルなDNSサービスで、ドメイン登録やルーティングも行えます。","qEn":"Which AWS DNS (Domain Name System) service converts domain names into IP addresses?","eEn":"Amazon Route 53 is a scalable DNS service that can also handle domain registration and routing."},{"d":"D3","q":"世界中のエッジロケーションを利用してコンテンツを低遅延で配信する、AWSのCDNサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon Route 53","AWS Direct Connect","Amazon CloudFront","Amazon VPC"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon CloudFrontはエッジロケーションでコンテンツをキャッシュし、低遅延で配信するCDNです。","qEn":"Which AWS CDN service uses edge locations around the world to deliver content with low latency?","eEn":"Amazon CloudFront is a CDN that caches content at edge locations and delivers it with low latency."},{"d":"D3","q":"オンプレミスとAWSの間に専用の物理回線を確立し、安定した接続を提供するサービスはどれですか？","o":["AWS Site-to-Site VPN","Amazon CloudFront","Amazon Route 53","AWS Direct Connect"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Direct Connectはインターネットを介さない専用線接続で、安定した帯域と低遅延を実現します。","qEn":"Which service establishes a dedicated physical connection between on premises and AWS and provides a stable connection?","eEn":"AWS Direct Connect is a dedicated line connection that does not go over the internet and achieves stable bandwidth and low latency."},{"d":"D3","q":"複数のEC2インスタンスに受信トラフィックを自動的に振り分ける、AWSの負荷分散サービスはどれですか？","o":["Elastic Load Balancing","Amazon CloudFront","AWS Auto Scaling","Amazon Route 53 Resolver"],"a":0,"e":"Elastic Load Balancing（ELB）はトラフィックを複数ターゲットに分散し、可用性を高めます。","qEn":"Which AWS load balancing service automatically distributes incoming traffic across multiple EC2 instances?","eEn":"Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) distributes traffic across multiple targets and improves availability."},{"d":"D3","q":"需要に応じてEC2インスタンス数を自動的に増減させ、コストと性能を最適化する機能はどれですか？","o":["Elastic Load Balancing","Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling","Amazon CloudWatch メトリクス","AWS Lambda"],"a":1,"e":"EC2 Auto Scalingは負荷に応じてインスタンス数を自動調整し、可用性とコスト効率を両立します。","qEn":"Which feature automatically increases or decreases the number of EC2 instances according to demand to optimize cost and performance?","oEn":["Elastic Load Balancing","Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling","Amazon CloudWatch metrics","AWS Lambda"],"eEn":"EC2 Auto Scaling automatically adjusts the number of instances according to load, balancing availability and cost efficiency."},{"d":"D3","q":"AWSリソースやアプリケーションのメトリクスを収集・監視し、アラームを設定できるサービスはどれですか？","o":["AWS CloudTrail","AWS Config","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Trusted Advisor"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon CloudWatchはメトリクスやログを監視し、閾値超過でアラームを発報できます。","qEn":"Which service collects and monitors metrics for AWS resources and applications and lets you set alarms?","eEn":"Amazon CloudWatch monitors metrics and logs and can raise an alarm when a threshold is exceeded."},{"d":"D3","q":"誰がいつどのAPIを呼び出したかなど、AWSアカウント内の操作履歴を記録・監査するサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Config","Amazon Inspector","AWS CloudTrail"],"a":3,"e":"AWS CloudTrailはAPI呼び出しなどのアカウントアクティビティを記録し、監査やトラブルシューティングに使います。","qEn":"Which service records and audits the history of operations in an AWS account, such as who called which API and when?","eEn":"AWS CloudTrail records account activity such as API calls and is used for auditing and troubleshooting."},{"d":"D3","q":"Dockerコンテナを実行・管理できる、AWSのフルマネージドなコンテナオーケストレーションサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon ECS","AWS Lambda","Amazon EC2","Amazon S3"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon ECS（Elastic Container Service）はコンテナの実行やスケーリングを管理するサービスです。","qEn":"Which AWS fully managed container orchestration service can run and manage Docker containers?","eEn":"Amazon ECS (Elastic Container Service) is a service that manages running and scaling containers."},{"d":"D3","q":"複数のEC2インスタンスから同時にアクセスできる、フルマネージドな共有ファイルストレージはどれですか？","o":["Amazon S3","Amazon EFS","Amazon EBS","Amazon Glacier"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon EFS（Elastic File System）は複数インスタンスから同時マウントできる共有ファイルストレージです。","qEn":"Which fully managed shared file storage can be accessed simultaneously from multiple EC2 instances?","eEn":"Amazon EFS (Elastic File System) is shared file storage that multiple instances can mount at the same time."},{"d":"D3","q":"MySQLやPostgreSQLと互換性を持ち、高性能・高可用性を狙って設計されたAWS独自のDBエンジンはどれですか？","o":["Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon Redshift","Amazon Aurora","Amazon Neptune"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon AuroraはMySQL/PostgreSQL互換で、商用DB並みの性能をより低コストで提供するAWS製エンジンです。","qEn":"Which AWS-built database engine, compatible with MySQL and PostgreSQL, is designed for high performance and high availability?","eEn":"Amazon Aurora is an AWS-built engine compatible with MySQL/PostgreSQL that delivers performance comparable to commercial databases at lower cost."},{"d":"D3","q":"インフラ構成をコード（テンプレート）として記述し、自動でプロビジョニングできるAWSのサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon CloudWatch Logs","AWS Config","AWS CloudTrail","AWS CloudFormation"],"a":3,"e":"AWS CloudFormationはIaCの仕組みで、テンプレートからリソースを自動作成・管理できます。","qEn":"Which AWS service lets you describe infrastructure configuration as code (templates) and provision it automatically?","eEn":"AWS CloudFormation is an infrastructure as code (IaC) mechanism that can automatically create and manage resources from templates."},{"d":"D3","q":"大量データを物理デバイスに保存してAWSへ輸送し、ネットワーク転送を避けて移行する仕組みはどれですか？","o":["AWS Snowball","AWS Direct Connect","Amazon S3 Transfer Acceleration","AWS DataSync"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Snowballは物理ストレージデバイスを用い、大容量データを物理的にAWSへ移送します。","qEn":"Which mechanism stores large amounts of data on physical devices and ships them to AWS, migrating without network transfer?","eEn":"AWS Snowball uses physical storage devices to physically move large volumes of data to AWS."},{"d":"D3","q":"S3に保存したデータに対し、標準SQLで直接クエリを実行できるサーバーレスの分析サービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon Redshift","Amazon Athena","Amazon EMR","Amazon QuickSight"],"a":1,"e":"Amazon Athenaはサーバー不要でS3上のデータにSQLクエリを実行できるサービスです。","qEn":"Which serverless analytics service lets you run queries with standard SQL directly on data stored in S3?","eEn":"Amazon Athena is a service that lets you run SQL queries on data in S3 without servers."},{"d":"D3","q":"アプリケーション間でメッセージを非同期に受け渡す、AWSのフルマネージドなメッセージキューサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon SNS","Amazon EventBridge","Amazon SQS","Amazon MQ"],"a":2,"e":"Amazon SQS（Simple Queue Service）はコンポーネント間を疎結合にするメッセージキューサービスです。","qEn":"Which AWS fully managed message queue service passes messages between applications asynchronously?","eEn":"Amazon SQS (Simple Queue Service) is a message queue service that loosely couples components."},{"d":"D3","q":"データベースを別のDBエンジンやAWSへ、稼働を続けたまま移行するのを支援するサービスはどれですか？","o":["AWS Application Migration Service","AWS DataSync","Amazon RDS","AWS Database Migration Service"],"a":3,"e":"AWS DMS（Database Migration Service）は最小限のダウンタイムでデータベースを移行できます。","qEn":"Which service helps you migrate a database to a different database engine or to AWS while it keeps running?","eEn":"AWS DMS (Database Migration Service) can migrate databases with minimal downtime."},{"d":"D3","q":"RDBやDynamoDBの前段に置き、頻繁に参照するデータをメモリに保持して高速化するサービスはどれですか？","o":["Amazon ElastiCache","Amazon S3","Amazon EFS","Amazon Redshift Spectrum"],"a":0,"e":"Amazon ElastiCacheはRedisやMemcachedを用いたインメモリキャッシュで、読み取りを高速化します。","qEn":"Which service sits in front of an RDB or DynamoDB and speeds things up by keeping frequently read data in memory?","eEn":"Amazon ElastiCache is an in-memory cache that uses Redis or Memcached and speeds up reads."},{"d":"D4","q":"使った分だけ料金を支払い、初期費用や長期契約が不要というAWSの基本的な料金の考え方はどれですか？","o":["従量課金制（Pay-as-you-go）","毎月定額を支払う定額サブスクリプション制","前払い一括制","無料使い放題"],"a":0,"e":"AWSは従量課金制が基本で、実際に使用したリソース量に応じて料金が発生します。","qEn":"Which is the basic AWS pricing approach in which you pay only for what you use, with no upfront cost or long-term contract?","oEn":["Pay-as-you-go","A flat monthly subscription","A lump-sum prepayment model","Free unlimited use"],"eEn":"AWS is basically pay-as-you-go, and charges are incurred according to the amount of resources actually used."},{"d":"D4","q":"1年または3年の利用を約束することで、オンデマンドより大幅な割引を受けられるEC2の購入方法はどれですか？","o":["スポットインスタンス","リザーブドインスタンス","オンデマンドインスタンス","Dedicated Host"],"a":1,"e":"リザーブドインスタンス（RI）は1年または3年の契約で最大約72%割引を受けられます。","qEn":"Which EC2 purchasing option offers a significant discount compared with On-Demand if you commit to 1 or 3 years of use?","oEn":["Spot Instances","Reserved Instances","On-Demand Instances","Dedicated Host"],"eEn":"Reserved Instances (RIs) offer a discount of up to about 72% with a 1-year or 3-year commitment."},{"d":"D4","q":"AWSの空きキャパシティを大幅割引で利用でき、中断される可能性があるEC2の購入オプションはどれですか？","o":["オンデマンド","リザーブドインスタンス","スポットインスタンス","Savings Plans"],"a":2,"e":"スポットインスタンスは未使用キャパシティを最大約90%割引で使えますが、AWS都合で中断されることがあります。","qEn":"Which EC2 purchasing option lets you use spare AWS capacity at a steep discount, with the possibility of interruption?","oEn":["On-Demand","Reserved Instances","Spot Instances","Savings Plans"],"eEn":"Spot Instances let you use unused capacity at up to about 90% off, but they can be interrupted at AWS's convenience."},{"d":"D4","q":"1〜3年で一定の利用量（時間あたりの費用）を約束すると割引される、柔軟な料金モデルはどれですか？","o":["オンデマンド","スポットインスタンス（余剰枠）","リザーブドインスタンス","Savings Plans"],"a":3,"e":"Savings Plansは一定の使用量コミットメントで、EC2やLambdaなどに柔軟に割引を適用できます。","qEn":"Which flexible pricing model gives a discount if you commit to a certain amount of usage (cost per hour) for 1 to 3 years?","oEn":["On-Demand","Spot Instances (spare capacity)","Reserved Instances","Savings Plans"],"eEn":"Savings Plans apply discounts flexibly to EC2, Lambda, and more in exchange for a commitment to a certain amount of usage."},{"d":"D4","q":"予算額を設定し、コストや使用量が閾値を超えそうなときにアラートを受け取れるAWSのツールはどれですか？","o":["AWS Budgets","AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Trusted Advisor"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Budgetsは予算を設定し、超過や超過予測時に通知を送るコスト管理ツールです。","qEn":"Which AWS tool lets you set a budget amount and receive alerts when costs or usage are about to exceed a threshold?","eEn":"AWS Budgets is a cost management tool that lets you set a budget and sends notifications when it is exceeded or forecast to be exceeded."},{"d":"D4","q":"過去のコストや使用状況をグラフで可視化し、傾向を分析・予測できるAWSのツールはどれですか？","o":["AWS Budgets","AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Organizations"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Cost Explorerは過去の利用データを可視化し、コスト傾向の分析や予測に使います。","qEn":"Which AWS tool visualizes past costs and usage in graphs and lets you analyze and forecast trends?","eEn":"AWS Cost Explorer visualizes past usage data and is used to analyze and forecast cost trends."},{"d":"D4","q":"AWS構成を利用開始前に指定し、想定される月額料金を事前に見積もれるツールはどれですか？","o":["AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Budgets","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Cost and Usage Report"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Pricing Calculatorは利用前にサービス構成を入力して料金を試算できるツールです。","qEn":"Which tool lets you specify an AWS configuration before you start using it and estimate the expected monthly cost in advance?","eEn":"AWS Pricing Calculator is a tool that lets you enter a service configuration before use and estimate the cost."},{"d":"D4","q":"最も詳細な粒度でコストと使用量のデータを提供し、S3に出力できるAWSのレポート機能はどれですか？","o":["AWS Cost Anomaly Detection","AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Cost and Usage Report"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Cost and Usage Report（CUR）は最も詳細なコスト・使用量データを提供します。","qEn":"Which AWS reporting feature provides cost and usage data at the most detailed level of granularity and can deliver it to Amazon S3?","eEn":"The AWS Cost and Usage Report (CUR) provides the most detailed cost and usage data."},{"d":"D4","q":"24時間365日対応で、ビジネスクリティカルなシステムがダウンした際の応答目標が15分未満のサポートプランはどれですか？","o":["Enterprise","Business","Developer","Enterprise On-Ramp"],"a":0,"e":"Enterpriseサポートはビジネス/ミッションクリティカルなシステム停止に15分未満の応答目標を持ち（本番システム停止は1時間未満）、TAMも付きます。Enterprise On-Rampは30分未満です。（2026年11月時点：Enterprise On-Rampは2027年1月1日に提供終了。現行の最上位はUnified Operationsで、重大インシデントにはIncident Management Engineerが5分未満で応答します）","qEn":"Which support plan operates 24/7 and has a response time target of under 15 minutes when a business-critical system goes down?","eEn":"Enterprise Support targets a response of under 15 minutes for business-critical and mission-critical system down cases (under 1 hour for a production system down) and also includes a TAM. Enterprise On-Ramp targets under 30 minutes. (As of November 2026: Enterprise On-Ramp will be discontinued on January 1, 2027. The top plan is now Unified Operations, where an Incident Management Engineer responds to critical incidents in under 5 minutes.)"},{"d":"D4","q":"本番環境での利用を想定し、営業時間外も含めて技術サポートを電話・チャットで受けられる中位のプランはどれですか？","o":["Basic","Business","Developer","Enterprise On-Ramp"],"a":1,"e":"Businessサポートは24時間365日の技術サポートを提供し、本番ワークロード向けの標準的なプランです。（2026年11月時点：Businessは2025年12月2日に新規受付を終了し、2027年1月1日に提供終了。後継のBusiness Support+は重大障害で30分未満の応答目標）","qEn":"Which mid-tier plan is intended for production use and provides technical support by phone and chat, including outside business hours?","eEn":"Business Support provides 24/7 technical support and is the standard plan for production workloads. (As of November 2026: Business Support stopped accepting new subscriptions on December 2, 2025 and will be discontinued on January 1, 2027. Its successor, Business Support+, targets a response of under 30 minutes for critical cases.)"},{"d":"D4","q":"すべてのAWSアカウントに無料で含まれ、ドキュメントやフォーラムのみ利用できるサポートプランはどれですか？","o":["Business","Developer","Basic","Enterprise"],"a":2,"e":"Basicサポートは無料で全アカウントに付属し、ドキュメントやコミュニティフォーラム等を利用できます。（2026年11月時点：Basicでもカスタマーサービス、re:Post、Trusted Advisorのコアチェック、AWS Healthを利用できるが、技術サポートのケースは開けない）","qEn":"Which support plan is included for free with every AWS account and provides access only to documentation and forums?","eEn":"Basic Support is free and included with all accounts, providing access to documentation, community forums, and more. (As of November 2026: Basic Support also includes customer service, AWS re:Post, core Trusted Advisor checks, and AWS Health, but it cannot open technical support cases.)"},{"d":"D4","q":"専任のテクニカルアカウントマネージャー（TAM）が付き、コンシェルジュ支援も受けられるサポートプランはどれですか？","o":["Enterprise On-Ramp","Developer","Business","Enterprise"],"a":3,"e":"EnterpriseサポートではTAMが専任で付き、積極的なガイダンスやコンシェルジュ支援を提供します。（2026年11月時点：専任TAMは現行の最上位Unified Operationsにも付き、Enterprise Supportの請求支援は「White-glove billing concierge」と記載。Enterprise On-Rampは2027年1月1日に提供終了）","qEn":"Which support plan provides a dedicated Technical Account Manager (TAM) and also offers concierge support?","eEn":"With Enterprise Support, a TAM is assigned to you and provides proactive guidance and concierge support. (As of November 2026: a designated TAM also comes with Unified Operations, now the top plan, and Enterprise Support lists its billing assistance as a white-glove billing concierge. Enterprise On-Ramp will be discontinued on January 1, 2027.)"},{"d":"D4","q":"コスト最適化やセキュリティなど6つの観点でベストプラクティスを自動チェックするAWSのサービスはどれですか？","o":["AWS Trusted Advisor","Amazon CloudWatch Logs","AWS Config","AWS CloudTrail"],"a":0,"e":"AWS Trusted Advisorはコスト最適化・パフォーマンス・セキュリティ・回復力・運用上の優秀性・サービスの制限を点検します。","qEn":"Which AWS service automatically checks best practices across six areas, such as cost optimization and security?","eEn":"AWS Trusted Advisor checks cost optimization, performance, security, resilience, operational excellence, and service limits."},{"d":"D4","q":"複数のAWSアカウントを一元管理し、請求をまとめて一括で支払えるようにするサービスはどれですか？","o":["AWS IAM","AWS Organizations","AWS Control Tower","AWS Config"],"a":1,"e":"AWS Organizationsは複数アカウントを統合管理し、一括請求（Consolidated Billing）を実現します。","qEn":"Which service lets you centrally manage multiple AWS accounts and pay for them together through a single consolidated bill?","eEn":"AWS Organizations manages multiple accounts centrally and provides consolidated billing."},{"d":"D4","q":"複数アカウントの利用量を合算することで、ボリューム割引の適用を受けやすくする仕組みはどれですか？","o":["リザーブドインスタンス","Savings Plans（コンピューティング割引）","一括請求（Consolidated Billing）機能","無料利用枠"],"a":2,"e":"一括請求では複数アカウントの使用量が合算され、ボリューム割引の階層に到達しやすくなります。","qEn":"Which mechanism makes it easier to qualify for volume discounts by combining the usage of multiple accounts?","oEn":["Reserved Instances","Savings Plans (compute discount)","Consolidated Billing","Free Tier"],"eEn":"With consolidated billing, usage across multiple accounts is combined, making it easier to reach volume discount tiers."},{"d":"D4","q":"新規顧客が一定期間・一定量まで特定サービスを無料で試せる、AWSの制度はどれですか？","o":["リザーブドインスタンス","Savings Plans（長期利用割引）","スポットインスタンス","AWS無料利用枠（Free Tier）"],"a":3,"e":"AWS無料利用枠は12か月間無料、常時無料、トライアルの3種類で新規利用を支援します。","qEn":"Which AWS program lets new customers try certain services for free for a limited period or up to a limited amount?","oEn":["Reserved Instances","Savings Plans (long-term usage discount)","Spot Instances","AWS Free Tier"],"eEn":"The AWS Free Tier supports new users with three types of offers: 12 months free, always free, and trials."},{"d":"D4","q":"AWSでインターネットへ送信されるデータ（アウトバウンド転送）について、一般的に正しいのはどれですか？","o":["データ転送量に応じて課金される","受信も送信も常に完全無料である","受信のみ課金される","一律月額固定である"],"a":0,"e":"一般にAWSではインバウンド転送は無料ですが、アウトバウンド（外向き）転送は従量課金されます。","qEn":"Which statement about data transferred out from AWS to the internet (outbound data transfer) is generally correct?","oEn":["It is charged based on the amount of data transferred.","Both inbound and outbound transfer are always completely free.","Only inbound transfer is charged.","It is a flat monthly fee."],"eEn":"In general, inbound data transfer to AWS is free, but outbound data transfer is charged on a pay-as-you-go basis."},{"d":"D4","q":"サーバーの物理的な調達・保守が不要になることで削減できる、クラウド利用のコスト面のメリットはどれですか？","o":["ソフトウェアのライセンス料","資本的支出（CAPEX）の初期設備投資","クラウド利用に応じて毎月発生する従量課金の料金","オフィスの毎月のインターネット回線料金"],"a":1,"e":"クラウドでは初期の設備投資（CAPEX）を、使った分だけ払う変動費（OPEX）に置き換えられます。","qEn":"Which cost benefit of using the cloud can be reduced because physical procurement and maintenance of servers are no longer required?","oEn":["Software license fees","Upfront capital expenditure (CAPEX) on equipment","Pay-as-you-go charges incurred monthly based on cloud usage","Monthly internet line fees for the office"],"eEn":"With the cloud, upfront capital expenditure (CAPEX) on equipment can be replaced with variable expenses (OPEX), where you pay only for what you use."},{"d":"D4","q":"AWS利用料金の確認、支払い方法の管理、請求書の閲覧を行うためのコンソール上のツールはどれですか？","o":["AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Billing（請求）ダッシュボード画面","AWS Budgets"],"a":2,"e":"AWS Billingダッシュボードでは請求額の確認、支払い方法や請求書の管理ができます。","qEn":"Which console tool do you use to check AWS charges, manage payment methods, and view invoices?","oEn":["AWS Cost Explorer","AWS Pricing Calculator","AWS Billing dashboard","AWS Budgets"],"eEn":"The AWS Billing dashboard lets you check your charges and manage payment methods and invoices."},{"d":"D4","q":"サードパーティのソフトウェアをAWS上で購入・デプロイできる、ソフトウェアのオンラインストアはどれですか？","o":["AWS Config","AWS Service Catalog","AWS Systems Manager","AWS Marketplace"],"a":3,"e":"AWS Marketplaceはサードパーティ製ソフトウェアを検索・購入・デプロイできるデジタルカタログです。","qEn":"Which online software store lets you purchase and deploy third-party software on AWS?","eEn":"AWS Marketplace is a digital catalog where you can find, purchase, and deploy third-party software."},{"d":"D4","q":"リソースにキーと値のラベルを付け、コストを部門やプロジェクト単位で分類・追跡する仕組みはどれですか？","o":["コスト配分タグ","リザーブドインスタンス","一括請求","Savings Plans"],"a":0,"e":"コスト配分タグを使うと、タグ単位でコストを集計し、部門やプロジェクトごとに費用を可視化できます。","qEn":"Which mechanism lets you attach key-value labels to resources so you can categorize and track costs by department or project?","oEn":["Cost allocation tags","Reserved Instances","Consolidated billing","Savings Plans"],"eEn":"With cost allocation tags, you can aggregate costs by tag and see spending for each department or project."},{"d":"D4","q":"Businessサポートに加え、より短い応答時間や運用支援を求める顧客向けの中上位プランはどれですか？","o":["Basic","Enterprise On-Ramp","Developer","Enterprise（最上位プラン）"],"a":1,"e":"Enterprise On-RampはBusinessとEnterpriseの中間で、より手厚い支援とプールされたTAM支援を提供します。（2026年11月時点：Enterprise On-Rampは2026年12月31日までの提供で、2027年1月1日に終了。Enterprise Supportの最低料金はOn-Rampを下回る月額5,000ドルに下がり、現行の最上位はUnified Operations）","qEn":"Which upper-mid-tier plan is for customers who want faster response times and operational assistance in addition to Business Support?","oEn":["Basic","Enterprise On-Ramp","Developer","Enterprise (top-tier plan)"],"eEn":"Enterprise On-Ramp sits between Business and Enterprise and provides more hands-on support and pooled TAM support. (As of November 2026: Enterprise On-Ramp is supported through December 31, 2026 and ends on January 1, 2027. Enterprise Support's minimum fee has dropped to $5,000 per month, below On-Ramp's, and the top plan is now Unified Operations.)"},{"d":"D4","q":"開発・テスト段階での利用を想定し、営業時間内にメールでの技術サポートを受けられる低価格プランはどれですか？","o":["Basic","Enterprise","Developer","Business"],"a":2,"e":"Developerサポートは開発・検証向けで、営業時間内にメールで技術的な問い合わせができます。（2026年11月時点：Developerは2025年12月2日に新規受付を終了し、2027年1月1日に提供終了。後継は月額29ドルからで24時間365日対応のBusiness Support+）","qEn":"Which low-cost plan is intended for use during development and testing and provides technical support by email during business hours?","eEn":"Developer Support is for development and testing, and lets you submit technical questions by email during business hours. (As of November 2026: Developer Support stopped accepting new subscriptions on December 2, 2025 and will be discontinued on January 1, 2027. Its successor is Business Support+, which starts at $29 per month and offers 24/7 access.)"},{"d":"D4","q":"同じEC2利用でも、一般的に時間単価が最も高くなる購入方法は次のうちどれですか？","o":["3年前払いのリザーブドインスタンス","スポットインスタンス","Savings Plans適用時","オンデマンドインスタンス"],"a":3,"e":"オンデマンドは前払いや契約なしで最も柔軟な反面、時間単価は最も高くなる傾向があります。","qEn":"Which of the following purchasing options generally has the highest hourly rate for the same EC2 usage?","oEn":["Reserved Instances with a 3-year all-upfront payment","Spot Instances","With Savings Plans applied","On-Demand Instances"],"eEn":"On-Demand is the most flexible because it requires no upfront payment or commitment, but it tends to have the highest hourly rate."},{"d":"D4","q":"AWSの料金に影響する主要な3つの要素として、一般的に挙げられるものはどれですか？","o":["従業員数・オフィスの数・年間の契約期間","コンピューティング・ストレージ・データ転送","会社の設立年・所在地・業種","電気代・水道代・ガス代"],"a":1,"e":"AWSの料金は主にコンピューティング使用量、ストレージ量、アウトバウンドのデータ転送量によって決まります。","qEn":"Which of the following are generally cited as the three main factors that affect AWS pricing?","oEn":["Total number of employees, number of offices, and annual contract term","Compute, storage, and data transfer","Year the company was founded, location, and industry","Electricity, water, and gas bills"],"eEn":"AWS pricing is determined mainly by compute usage, the amount of storage, and the amount of outbound data transfer."}];
